export const QIY_SKILL_FILES: Record<string, string> = {
  "examples/warehouse-admin/app.qiy": "qiy v0;\n\napplication qiy-warehouse-admin {\n  database sqlite {}\n  workspace {\n    name warehouse-admin;\n    aliases {\n      server ops-api;\n      web ops-console;\n      deploy ops-admin;\n    }\n  }\n\n  include \"modules/application-config.qiy\";\n  include \"modules/catalog.qiy\";\n  include \"modules/inventory.qiy\";\n  include \"modules/navigation.qiy\";\n}\n",
  "examples/warehouse-admin/modules/application-config.qiy": "api { client rest; }\nstorage { provider local; }\n",
  "examples/warehouse-admin/modules/catalog.qiy": "include \"shared/enums.qiy\";\n\nentity warehouses @label(\"Warehouses\") @icon(HomeOutlined) {\n  field id UUID @id;\n  field code Text @unique;\n  field name Text;\n}\n\nentity products @label(\"Products\") @icon(ShoppingOutlined) {\n  field id UUID @id;\n  field sku Text @unique;\n  field name Text;\n}\n",
  "examples/warehouse-admin/modules/inventory.qiy": "entity movements @label(\"Stock movements\") @icon(SwapOutlined) {\n  field id UUID @id;\n  field warehouseId UUID;\n  field productId UUID;\n  field type movementType;\n  field quantity Integer;\n  field occurredAt DateTime;\n}\n\nrelation movementWarehouse movements warehouseId warehouses id one @onDelete(restrict);\nrelation movementProduct movements productId products id one @onDelete(restrict);\n",
  "examples/warehouse-admin/modules/navigation.qiy": "menu {\n  group operations @label(\"Operations\") @icon(AppstoreOutlined) {\n    resource movements;\n  }\n  group masterData @label(\"Master data\") @icon(DatabaseOutlined) {\n    resource warehouses;\n    resource products;\n  }\n}\n\ndashboard {\n  metric movementCount movements @label(\"Movements\") @icon(SwapOutlined) @span(8);\n}\n",
  "examples/warehouse-admin/modules/shared/enums.qiy": "enum movementType {\n  value inbound label \"Inbound\" color \"green\" icon LoginOutlined;\n  value outbound label \"Outbound\" color \"orange\" icon LogoutOutlined;\n  value adjustment label \"Adjustment\" color \"blue\" icon SwapOutlined;\n}\n",
  "examples/warehouse-admin/README.md": "# Warehouse Admin Example\n\nThis is a complete modular Qiy project. Copy the entire `warehouse-admin` folder into your own project (for example, as `models/warehouse`), then run Qiy from your project root. Do not separate `app.qiy` from the `modules/` directory: the root model includes those files by relative path.\n\nThe model generates warehouses, products, and stock movements; explicit warehouse/product relations; movement type labels/colors/icons; grouped navigation; and a movement count dashboard.\n\n## What this example demonstrates\n\n| Concept | Where |\n| --- | --- |\n| Root `app.qiy` plus relative include fragments and a nested fragment include | `app.qiy`, `modules/catalog.qiy` |\n| Shared enums with labels, colors and icons | `modules/shared/enums.qiy` |\n| Entities with `UUID @id`, unique `Text` codes, enum and `DateTime` fields | `modules/catalog.qiy`, `modules/inventory.qiy` |\n| Explicit foreign keys and `@onDelete` behavior | `modules/inventory.qiy` |\n| Grouped menu plus a legacy dashboard metric | `modules/navigation.qiy` |\n| `api`/`storage` config blocks and workspace aliases for `qiy init` | `modules/application-config.qiy`, `app.qiy` |\n\nIt deliberately stays small: it does not demonstrate auth, permissions, `@code`, dataflows, actions, charts, realtime or `features`. For those, read the focused references below and the full-feature model in the Qiy repository (`examples/self`). Every `.qiy` snippet can be added to this example after regenerating.\n\n## Where to read next\n\n- [Language reference](../../references/language-reference.md) - complete DSL map, all blocks and annotations\n- [Modeling and generation](../../references/modeling-and-generation.md) - fields, relations, indexes, generated codes, limits\n- [Auth and permissions](../../references/auth-permissions.md) - login modes, roles, restrict/scope/pages\n- [Dataflows and actions](../../references/dataflows-actions.md) - transactional commands and buttons\n- [CLI workflows](../../references/cli-workflows.md) - create/init/generate/--sync/skill install\n- [Skill entrypoint](../../SKILL.md) - routing table for all references\n\n## Generate and run\n\nFrom the project root after copying this folder to models/warehouse:\n\n~~~sh\nqiy create -f models/warehouse/app.qiy -n warehouse-admin -o out/warehouse-admin\ncd out/warehouse-admin\nbun install\nbun run typecheck\nbun run test\nbun run build\nbun run preview\n~~~\n\nOpen http://127.0.0.1:3000/movements (or the URL printed by preview). The preview uses in-memory data and is for local evaluation only.\n\nThe generated workspace includes `apps/server` (Bun + Elysia API, Drizzle schema and tests), `apps/web` (Refine + Ant Design + React Router), and deployment examples. Try the warehouse, product, and movement resources; inspect the Operations/Master data menu groups and the movement count dashboard. The generated app is editable source, but preview data is not durable and is not a production deployment.\n\n## Integrate into an existing Bun project\n\nThe same model contains optional workspace aliases. From a host Bun project's root, whose package.json declares packageManager bun@<version>, run:\n\n~~~sh\nqiy init -f models/warehouse/app.qiy\nbun install\nbun run qiy:warehouse-admin:typecheck\nbun run qiy:warehouse-admin:test\n~~~\n\nThis adds apps/ops-api and apps/ops-console, deploy/ops-admin, ops-admin.Dockerfile, and docker-compose.ops-admin.yml. It does not add Turborepo. Change names in the workspace block before generation if those paths conflict with the host project.\n\nFor later model changes, run `qiy init -f models/warehouse/app.qiy --sync` and review the diff. Keep custom integrations in files not owned by Qiy, for example `apps/ops-api/src/integrations/` and `apps/ops-console/app/plugins/`. Never assume sync preserves edits made directly inside generated files.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n- Missing include: copy the complete example folder and keep module paths relative to the file containing each `include`.\n- Name/path collision during `init`: change `workspace.aliases` in `app.qiy`, then retry; do not remove host files to force generation.\n- Preview port is occupied: stop the other process or set a free `PORT` for the preview process.\n- A generated build passes but a real service fails: configure and test the database, identity provider, storage, and external API separately; compilation is not a production integration test.\n- Any other error: look up the exact message in [Troubleshooting](../../references/troubleshooting.md).\n\n## Files\n\n~~~text\nwarehouse-admin/\n|-- app.qiy\n|-- README.md\n+-- modules/\n    |-- application-config.qiy\n    |-- catalog.qiy\n    |-- inventory.qiy\n    |-- navigation.qiy\n    +-- shared/\n        +-- enums.qiy\n~~~\n\napp.qiy is the only entrypoint. Included files are application fragments: they do not repeat the qiy version or application wrapper.\n",
  "references/auth-permissions.md": "# Authentication, permissions and policy\n\nUse this file when you add login, identity providers, roles, atomic permissions, data scope, row/field policy, page guards or command authorization - and when you must state what the generated security model does *not* protect.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/permissions (`/dsl/auth` for providers and sessions)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Choose an auth mode](#choose-an-auth-mode)\n- [auth block grammar](#auth-block-grammar)\n- [User model contract](#user-model-contract)\n- [Sessions, tokens and password policy](#sessions-tokens-and-password-policy)\n- [OTP login](#otp-login)\n- [Multi-provider and hybrid login](#multi-provider-and-hybrid-login)\n- [Provider settings and environment variables](#provider-settings-and-environment-variables)\n- [Permission declarations](#permission-declarations)\n- [Effective permissions and endpoints](#effective-permissions-and-endpoints)\n- [Command authorization (allow)](#command-authorization-allow)\n- [Row and field policy (restrict)](#row-and-field-policy-restrict)\n- [Data scope (scope)](#data-scope-scope)\n- [Page rules (pages)](#page-rules-pages)\n- [Declaration to artifact map](#declaration-to-artifact-map)\n- [Security boundaries and limits](#security-boundaries-and-limits)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## Choose an auth mode\n\n| Mode | Declaration | Generated result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Local password | `provider local;` | Argon2id verify + HS256 session JWT + `/auth/login` + Refine `AuthPage` |\n| Single OAuth/OIDC/SSO | `provider oidc;` (also `oauth2`, `sso`, `okta`, `auth0`, `azure-ad-b2c`, `keycloak`, `google`, `kinde`) | Browser PKCE + server JWKS verification; one `QIY_OIDC_ISSUER/AUDIENCE/JWKS_URL` block |\n| Multiple providers | `providers okta, keycloak, google;` | Login buttons from `GET /api/v1/auth/providers`; one `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_*` block per provider |\n| Hybrid (password + OAuth) | `providers local, okta, google;` plus username/password fields | One login page with password form + provider buttons; first-login onboarding, bind/unbind, profile page |\n| One-time password | `provider otp;` | `/auth/otp/request` + `/auth/otp/verify`, 5-minute signed challenge, 12-hour session |\n| Host integration | `mode integration` | No Qiy server, no Qiy auth; host adapter supplies identity ([workspace-integration.md](workspace-integration.md)) |\n\nDerived modes: a model has local login when `provider local` or `providers` contains `local`; also has hybrid when local login **and** at least one OAuth provider. A provider selector page appears for hybrid or >= 2 OAuth providers.\n\nAn application without `auth` generates no guard and **refuses to start in production** unless `QIY_DEV_MODE=1`.\n\n## auth block grammar\n\n```text\nauth {\n  ( \"provider\" <id> [ \"{\" ( \"subjectField\" <field> \";\" | \"claim\" <name> \";\" )* \"}\" | \";\" ] )\n| \"providers\" <id> ( \",\" <id> )* \";\"\n| \"user\" <entity> \";\"\n| \"subjectField\" <field> \";\"\n| \"roleField\" <field> \";\"\n| \"usernameField\" <field> \";\"\n| \"passwordField\" <field> \";\"\n| \"profileField\" <field> \";\"\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\nauth {\n  providers local, okta, google;\n  user users;\n  subjectField subject;          // canonical external identity column\n  roleField role;                // required: enum with exactly admin/operator/viewer\n  usernameField email;           // local / otp login identifier\n  passwordField passwordHash;    // local password hash\n  profileField oauthProfiles;    // optional: per-provider profile JSON\n  provider okta { subjectField oktaSubject; }\n  provider google { subjectField googleSubject; claim sub; }\n}\n```\n\n`provider <id> { ... }` is a **mapping block**, not a second login mode. It must name an already-configured provider. `provider` and `providers` are mutually exclusive.\n\n| Attribute | Required | Default | Rule |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `provider` | one of two | - | Single provider: `local`, `otp`, `oidc`, `oauth2`, `sso`, `okta`, `auth0`, `azure-ad-b2c`, `keycloak`, `google`, `kinde` |\n| `providers` | one of two | - | Comma list; unique; cannot contain `otp`; may contain `local` |\n| `user` | yes | - | Declared user entity (`Auth: unknown user entity X`) |\n| `subjectField` | required for OAuth family | empty | Required + unique + Text column |\n| `roleField` | yes | - | Enum whose values are **exactly** `admin`, `operator`, `viewer` |\n| `usernameField` | required for `local`/`otp` | empty | Required + unique + Text; must differ from `passwordField` |\n| `passwordField` | required for `local` | empty | Nullable Text; never appears in the API schema |\n| `profileField` | no | empty | Nullable Text JSON; only with at least one OAuth provider |\n| mapping `subjectField` | required in hybrid | - | Existing nullable + unique Text column |\n| mapping `claim` | no | `sub` | Plain claim name `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`; quotes are rejected |\n\n## User model contract\n\n```qiy\nenum userRole {\n  value admin;\n  value operator;\n  value viewer;\n}\n\nentity users table users @label(\"Users\") {\n  field id UUID @id;\n  field email Text @unique;                       // usernameField\n  field displayName Text @nullable;\n  field passwordHash Text @nullable;              // passwordField\n  field role userRole;                            // roleField\n  field subject Text @unique;                     // canonical subjectField\n  field oktaSubject Text @unique @nullable;       // per-provider mapping column\n  field orgId UUID @nullable;                     // enables scope claim org.id for local/API-key sessions\n  field oauthProfiles Text @nullable;             // profileField\n  field permissions Text @nullable;               // permission from database field\n}\n```\n\n| Field role | Requirement | Error (excerpt) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `usernameField` | required, unique, Text | `Auth: usernameField must be a required unique Text field` |\n| `passwordField` | nullable Text | `Auth: passwordField must be a nullable Text field storing the password hash` |\n| distinct columns | - | `Auth: usernameField and passwordField must be different fields` |\n| `subjectField` | required, unique, Text (with OAuth) | `Auth: subjectField must be a required unique Text field` |\n| `roleField` | enum exactly admin/operator/viewer | `Auth: roleField must be an enum with admin, operator and viewer values` |\n| per-provider column | exists, Text, nullable, unique | `Auth: provider okta subjectField oktaSubject must be nullable ...` |\n| `profileField` | nullable Text | `Auth: profileField must be a nullable Text field storing per-provider profile metadata` |\n| onboarding | every other required column must be nullable | `Auth: OAuth onboarding cannot populate required user fields: ...; make them nullable` |\n| scope claim column (local/hybrid) | users needs a matching column (`org.id` -> `orgId`) | `Data scope claim org.id needs a matching field on users (expected orgId) ...` |\n\nIdentity write rules (not configurable):\n\n| Mode | Column | Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Single provider, no mapping | `subjectField` | `<iss>|<sub>` |\n| Mapping with `claim` | mapped subject field | that claim's string value |\n| Mapping without `claim` | mapped subject field | `sub` |\n| Hybrid onboarding | mapped column **and** canonical `subjectField` | mapped column `sub`; canonical `<provider>:<subject>` |\n| Local password bootstrap (hybrid) | canonical `subjectField` | `local:<username>` |\n\n## Sessions, tokens and password policy\n\n| Token | Issued by | Algorithm | Lifetime | Payload/use |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Local password session | `POST /auth/login` | HS256 (`QIY_AUTH_SECRET`) | **12 hours** | `iss=aud=qiy-admin`, `sub=<user id>`, `role`, `typ=qiy-local` |\n| OTP session | `POST /auth/otp/verify` | HS256 | 12 hours | same `sub`/`role`, `typ=qiy-otp` |\n| OTP challenge | `POST /auth/otp/request` | HS256 | **5 minutes** | `typ=qiy-otp-challenge`, `identifier`, `otpHash`, `valid`, `sub` |\n| Onboarding token | `POST /auth/exchange` (hybrid) | HS256 | **10 minutes** | `typ=qiy-onboarding`, `provider`, `identitySubject`, optional username/email/name |\n| Provider access token | IdP | RS256/ES256 | IdP policy | Server routes by unverified `iss` to that provider's JWKS, then verifies |\n| API key | `POST /api/v1/auth/api-keys` | HMAC-SHA256 stored | optional expiry | See [system-features.md](system-features.md) |\n\n- The Web stores the access token in `localStorage[\"qiy.access_token\"]`; multi-provider also stores `id_token`/`expires_at`; `/auth/me` identity is cached 60 seconds and invalidated by token changes.\n- Single-provider OIDC uses `qiy.expires_at` (60 seconds early) and one silent `prompt=none` renewal. **No refresh token**: 401 clears the session and redirects to login.\n- The server signs/verifies session tokens; the browser only holds strings. `role` is inside the token but **every request re-reads the user row** (`findUserById`), so a demotion applies on the next request.\n- Provider `iss` must exactly match a configured provider issuer (trailing `/` stripped); audience or client id may match; algorithms limited to RS256/ES256.\n- Claims are flattened into `Principal.claims` (`org.id`, `realm_access.roles`), used by `scope`, `permission from claim` and `restrict mask claim`. `iss/aud/exp/iat/nbf/jti/sub` are excluded.\n- Password hashing: `Bun.password.hash(..., { algorithm: \"argon2id\" })`; **minimum 8 characters**, no complexity rules. Unknown accounts still run one dummy Argon2id verify before 401.\n- Login response `{ accessToken, tokenType: \"Bearer\", expiresIn: 43200, id, name, role }`; failures are a uniform 401 `Invalid username or password`.\n- No self-service password change is generated. Operate accounts with `bun run auth:bootstrap-admin` (initial admin, refuses if an admin exists) and `bun run auth:set-password` (unique row by username/email).\n- The login page has no register, forgot-password or remember-me links. Accounts are created by bootstrap, an administrator, or hybrid onboarding.\n\n## OTP login\n\n```qiy\nauth { provider otp; user users; usernameField email; roleField role; }\n```\n\n| Endpoint | Request | Response |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `POST /api/v1/auth/otp/request` | `{ identifier }` (1..190 chars) | `{ challengeToken, expiresIn: 300, devCode? }` |\n| `POST /api/v1/auth/otp/verify` | `{ identifier, challengeToken, code }` (code 4..12) | `{ accessToken, tokenType, expiresIn: 43200, id, name, role }` |\n\n- Codes are 6 digits; the challenge is an HMAC-SHA256(`identifier\\ncode`) signed token, so it needs no process memory and scales horizontally.\n- Delivery adapter: `POST QIY_OTP_DELIVERY_URL` with `{ recipient, code, expiresIn: 300 }`; adds `Authorization: Bearer` when `QIY_OTP_DELIVERY_TOKEN` is set; must be HTTPS and return 2xx.\n- Delivery failure -> **502** `{ errorKey: \"auth.otpDeliveryFailed\" }` and **no** challenge is issued. Dev mode adds adapter detail; production returns generic text. Codes are never logged.\n- `QIY_OTP_DELIVERY_TIMEOUT_MS` default 10000 (100..60000).\n- Unknown identifiers get the same 200 + challenge with `valid:false`; verify then 401 (no account enumeration).\n- `QIY_DEV_MODE=1` + `QIY_OTP_DEV_CODE` uses the fixed code and echoes `devCode`; never allowed in production.\n- Limits: no per-identifier/IP rate limit; a challenge can be reused within its 5-minute window (no one-time consumption record). Add rate limiting and persistence in the delivery adapter or gateway if needed.\n\n## Multi-provider and hybrid login\n\n| Endpoint | local | single provider | multi provider | hybrid | otp |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `POST /auth/login` | yes | - | - | yes | - |\n| `GET /auth/providers` | - | - | `{ providers }` | `{ providers, local: true }` | - |\n| `POST /auth/exchange` | - | - | raw `{ access_token, id_token?, expires_in? }` | session or `{ needsOnboarding }` | - |\n| `POST /auth/oauth/register` | - | - | - | yes | - |\n| `POST /auth/bind` / `POST /auth/unbind` | - | - | - | yes | - |\n| `GET /auth/identities` | yes | - | - | yes | - |\n| `POST /auth/otp/request` / `verify` | - | - | - | - | yes |\n| `GET /auth/me` | yes | yes | yes | yes | yes |\n\nHybrid first-login onboarding:\n\n1. Provider button -> PKCE authorize -> callback sends `code` + `code_verifier` to `POST /auth/exchange`.\n2. If the provider identity column already maps to a user, a 12-hour session is issued.\n3. Otherwise `{ needsOnboarding: true, onboardingToken, provider, profile }`; the Web opens `/auth/onboarding`.\n4. `POST /auth/oauth/register { onboardingToken, username, email?, password }`. Only the token's `provider`/`subject` are trusted; username/email duplicates return 409; the password uses the same Argon2id + 8-character rule; the role comes from `QIY_OIDC_DEFAULT_ROLE` (default `viewer`, invalid values fail at startup); it writes `displayName`, the provider profile metadata, the mapped identity column and canonical `subjectField = <provider>:<subject>`.\n5. The onboarding token is valid for 10 minutes; expired/tampered/wrong-issuer tokens return 401 and require a new provider login.\n\nProfile page (`/profile`, hybrid only) reads `GET /api/v1/auth/identities`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"user\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"username\": \"ops@example.com\", \"email\": \"ops@example.com\", \"name\": \"Ops\", \"role\": \"operator\" },\n  \"password\": { \"set\": true },\n  \"providers\": [\n    { \"id\": \"okta\", \"label\": \"Okta\", \"bound\": true, \"subject\": \"00u...\", \"email\": \"ops@example.com\", \"name\": \"Ops\" },\n    { \"id\": \"google\", \"label\": \"Google\", \"bound\": false }\n  ],\n  \"loginMethodCount\": 2\n}\n```\n\n| Operation | Endpoint | Rule |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Bind | `POST /auth/bind` with `{ provider, code, codeVerifier, redirectUri }` or `{ onboardingToken }` | Requires a session; identity owned by another account -> 409; writes the mapped column + profile |\n| Unbind | `POST /auth/unbind` with `{ provider }` | Requires a session; removing the **last** login method -> 409 `Cannot remove the last login method...` |\n| Bind button | `beginProviderBind` on `/profile` | Same PKCE flow; callback carries `?linked=<provider>` |\n\nNon-hybrid multi-provider mode **does not create accounts**. A valid IdP identity with no user row logs in but has no principal data (403). Create rows and fill provider columns first; `auth:bootstrap-admin` only creates a local account.\n\n## Provider settings and environment variables\n\n`QIY_OIDC_<PROVIDER>_*` uses the provider name uppercased with non-alphanumerics replaced by `_`: `okta` -> `OKTA`, `azure-ad-b2c` -> `AZURE_AD_B2C`.\n\n| Provider id | Issuer shape | Audience | JWKS | Identity claim |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `okta` | `https://<domain>/oauth2/default` | `api://default` or custom AS audience | `/oauth2/default/v1/keys` | `sub` |\n| `keycloak` | `https://<host>/realms/<realm>` | `account` or client id | `/realms/<realm>/protocol/openid-connect/certs` | `sub` (roles usually in `realm_access.roles`) |\n| `google` | `https://accounts.google.com` | OAuth client id | `https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v3/certs` | `sub` (no built-in groups) |\n| `kinde` | `https://<subdomain>.kinde.com` | client id | `/.well-known/jwks.json` | `sub` |\n| `azure-ad-b2c` | `https://<tenant>.b2clogin.com/<tenantId>/<policy>/v2.0/` | app client id | `<policy>/discovery/v2.0/keys` | `sub` (custom policies often add `roles`) |\n| `auth0` | `https://<tenant>.<region>.auth0.com/` | API identifier | `/.well-known/jwks.json` | `sub` |\n| `oidc`/`oauth2`/`sso` | your issuer | your audience | your JWKS | `sub` |\n| Dex (via `keycloak`/`oidc`) | `https://<host>/dex` | `qiy-admin` or your client | `/dex/keys` | `sub` (no `roles`/`groups` by default) |\n\nThese are configuration starting points, not acceptance claims: verify each real tenant (issuer, audience, JWKS, claims, logout, third-party cookie behavior) in its own environment. `tools/verify-*.ts` scripts prove protocol shape, not your tenant.\n\nServer variables:\n\n| Variable | Default | Required when | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET` | random in dev, empty in prod | local / hybrid / OTP / API keys | **>= 32 chars** or startup throws; signs sessions, OTP challenges, onboarding tokens and peppers API keys. Rotation invalidates all of them |\n| `QIY_OIDC_ISSUER` / `_AUDIENCE` / `_JWKS_URL` | empty | single OAuth provider | issuer/JWKS must be HTTPS |\n| `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_ISSUER` / `_AUDIENCE` / `_JWKS_URL` | empty | hybrid / multi | all three required or the provider is skipped; issuer must match token `iss` exactly |\n| `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_AUTHORIZATION_URL` / `_TOKEN_URL` / `_CLIENT_ID` | empty | hybrid / multi | public login-page fields; a missing one hides the provider from `/auth/providers` |\n| `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_SCOPE` | `openid profile email` | hybrid / multi | authorization scope |\n| `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_REDIRECT_URI` | global `QIY_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI` | hybrid / multi | must match the IdP registration |\n| `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_CLIENT_SECRET` | empty | confidential clients | server only; never a `VITE_` value |\n| `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_LOGOUT_URL` | empty | optional | browser logout redirect |\n| `QIY_OIDC_JWKS_TIMEOUT_MS` | `5000` | OAuth | single JWKS request timeout, min 1 |\n| `QIY_OIDC_JWKS_COOLDOWN_MS` | `30000` | OAuth | minimum interval before refetching on an unknown `kid` |\n| `QIY_OIDC_JWKS_CACHE_MAX_AGE_MS` | `600000` | OAuth | key cache age; also the worst-case revocation delay |\n| `QIY_OIDC_DEFAULT_ROLE` | `viewer` | hybrid | onboarding role; must be admin/operator/viewer |\n| `QIY_OTP_DELIVERY_URL` / `_TOKEN` / `_TIMEOUT_MS` | empty / empty / `10000` | otp | HTTPS adapter, optional bearer, 100..60000 ms |\n| `QIY_OTP_DEV_CODE` | `246810` in dev | otp dev | fixed code + `devCode` echo; only with `QIY_DEV_MODE=1` |\n| `QIY_DEV_MODE` | `1` without auth, else `0` | - | startup gate for no-auth apps, OTP dev code, error detail |\n\nWeb variables are generated **only for single-provider OIDC**: `VITE_QIY_AUTHORIZATION_URL`, `VITE_QIY_TOKEN_URL`, `VITE_QIY_CLIENT_ID`, `VITE_QIY_AUTH_SCOPE`, `VITE_QIY_REDIRECT_URI`, `VITE_QIY_LOGOUT_URL`, `VITE_QIY_API_TRANSPORT`. Multi/hybrid modes read public config from `/auth/providers` and never send a client secret to the browser.\n\n## Permission declarations\n\n`permission` declarations must be **contiguous immediately after `messages`**, before `workflow`/`enum`/`entity`. Any non-empty permission model requires a generated `auth` block, and at least one `permission field`.\n\n```qiy\npermission field    <Name> \"<value>\" [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] ;\npermission group    <Name> [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] { A, B, ... } [;]\npermission group    <Name> [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] = A & B & ... ;\npermission from database field <entity>.<field> ;\npermission from claim <provider> \"<claim>\" ;\npermission verification <Name> [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] {\n  input { field <name> Text|Array<String>; ... }\n  return <expression> ;\n}\n```\n\n| Form | Rules |\n| --- | --- |\n| `field` | Value non-empty, no whitespace, globally unique, case-sensitive. Convention `<domain>:<action>` (`inventory:receive`). This string is the contract shared with claims, DB columns, OpenAPI `x-qiy-permissions` and 403 `missing` |\n| `group` (list) | Members are permission fields or other groups; trailing comma allowed; trailing `;` optional |\n| `group` (`= A & B`) | **`&` is union**, not intersection. No intersection operator exists. Must end with `;` |\n| `from database field` | At most one per model; column must be a `Text` field on the auth user entity |\n| `from claim` | Provider must be a configured OAuth/OIDC provider; `local`/`otp` are rejected; duplicate provider+claim rejected; multiple entries allowed |\n| `verification` | Must have `return`; `input` optional; input types are only `Text` and `Array<String>` |\n\nGroup semantics: unknown member (`unknown member`), empty group, duplicate member, self reference and cycles are rejected. A group named `admin`/`operator`/`viewer` becomes a **role group**: a principal with that role receives all expanded values. Groups expand recursively into a sorted, de-duplicated set.\n\nDatabase column content contract:\n\n```text\n[\"inventory:receive\",\"manager\"]   # JSON string array (recommended)\ninventory:receive,manager         # comma/space separated text (compatible)\n```\n\n- Non-string array elements are dropped; text starting with `[` that fails JSON parsing makes the whole source empty (fail-closed).\n- Each entry is matched against declared permission values first, then expanded as a group name; unknown entries are ignored.\n- A failed database read never 500s `/auth/me`: that source is ignored and role groups/claims still apply.\n\nClaim sources: `^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.-]*` (dots allowed for flattened keys such as `realm.roles`). At runtime only the **claim name** is read, regardless of which configured provider supplied it; the provider in the declaration is a configuration constraint, not runtime isolation. Values are normalized like the DB column: string arrays keep strings and dedupe; a string is split on commas/whitespace; numbers/booleans/null/objects yield nothing. The IdP must actually issue the claim (Google needs a custom `groups` mapping; Dex issues no roles/groups by default).\n\nVerification expression grammar:\n\n```text\nexpression  := orExpr\norExpr      := andExpr ( \"||\" andExpr )*\nandExpr     := unary ( \"&&\" unary )*\nunary       := \"!\" unary | \"(\" orExpr \")\" | comparison\ncomparison  := operand op operand\noperand     := \"self\" \".\" ( \"permissions\" | \"groups\" | \"role\" )\n             | \"input\" \".\" <name>\n             | <quoted string>\nop          := [ \"not\" ] ( \"some\" | \"all\" ) ( \"included\" \"in\" | \"in\" )\n             | \"=\"\n             | \"!=\"\n```\n\nPrecedence: `!` > `( )` > `&&` > `||`. Operands normalize to string sets; comparisons are order-independent.\n\n| Operator | Alias | Semantics | `missing` diagnostic |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `all included in` | `all in` | left subset of right | left elements not in right |\n| `some included in` | `some in` | intersection non-empty | left elements |\n| `not all included in` | `not all in` | not a subset | none |\n| `not some included in` | `not some in` | disjoint | intersection elements |\n| `=` | - | set equality | symmetric difference |\n| `!=` | - | set inequality | none |\n\n`missing` is explanatory only; `allowed` is authoritative. `self.role` cannot be used in a membership comparison against another role set (`role membership comparison requires a non-role set`) - compare it with `=`/`!=` and a literal. `input` fields are required once declared (a missing one is 400); undeclared fields are ignored; `self` is reserved.\n\nWhere verification is evaluated: `POST /api/v1/auth/verify-permission` (any authenticated principal may self-check; it cannot check another user), `dataflow ... allow verification Name` (inputs must have same-named `@required` Text/enum flow inputs), `action ... allow verification Name` (navigate only, no inputs, visibility only), and the Web `CanAccess` for input-free verifications.\n\n## Effective permissions and endpoints\n\nEffective permissions are the union of three sources, **additive only**:\n\n| Source | Declaration | Runtime read |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Role group | none needed | `principal.role`; a group named after the role applies automatically |\n| Database column | `permission from database field users.permissions;` | the user row's Text column |\n| OAuth claim | `permission from claim okta \"roles\";` | verified id_token claims (local/OTP sessions have none) |\n\n```bash\ncurl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/permissions\n# { \"permissions\": [\"inventory:receive\",\"report:read\"], \"groups\": [\"admin\",\"operator\"] }\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"verification\":\"CanAccessUserApi\",\"input\":{\"permission\":[\"api:getUser\"]}}' \\\n  http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/verify-permission\n# { \"allowed\": false, \"missing\": [\"api:putUser\"] }\n```\n\n| Endpoint | Auth | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `GET /api/v1/auth/permissions` | session or API key | `{ permissions, groups }`, sorted and unique |\n| `POST /api/v1/auth/verify-permission` | same | `{ verification, input? }` -> `{ allowed }` or `{ allowed: false, missing }`; unknown verification/missing input/type error 400; unauthenticated 401 |\n| `GET /api/v1/auth/me` | same | `{ ...principal, permissions, groups }`; OIDC principals also carry `claims` |\n\nAPI keys are equal to a session for permissions but have **no id_token claims**: their `claims` contain only scope-derived keys read from user columns (`org.id` <- `orgId`). Therefore `permission from claim` never applies to API keys, and a `verification` that reads a claim set evaluates as empty (fail-closed).\n\n## Command authorization (allow)\n\nAuthorization is written on the **dataflow**; a dataflow-bound action inherits it. Two forms are mutually exclusive per command.\n\n```qiy\ndataflow receiveInventory @label(\"Receive\") {\n  allow permission InventoryReceivePermission;\n  ...\n}\n\ndataflow shipSalesOrder @label(\"Ship\") {\n  allow verification CanShipOrders;\n  ...\n}\n\ndataflow reserveStock @label(\"Reserve\") {\n  allow roles admin, operator;   # legacy form\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n| Rule | dataflow | action (`navigate`) | action (bound dataflow) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `allow roles` | only `admin`/`operator`, non-empty, no duplicates | non-empty subset of admin/operator/viewer | forbidden (declare it on the dataflow) |\n| `allow permission` | one or more permission fields/groups, expanded to values at generation | allowed; controls button/page visibility | forbidden |\n| `allow verification` | verification may have inputs; each needs a same-named `@required` Text/enum flow input | verification must have **no** input (`requires inputs and cannot guard a navigate action`) | forbidden |\n| Default | `admin, operator` | resource default | inherited from the dataflow |\n\nRuntime (inside the command route, before the transaction):\n\n- Unauthenticated -> 401. Role not allowed -> 403 `{ error: \"Command execution is restricted\" }`.\n- Missing permission -> 403 `{ error: \"Missing required permissions: ...\", errorKey: \"command.forbidden\", missing }`.\n- Failed verification -> 403 `{ errorKey: \"command.forbidden\" }` with optional `missing`; unknown verification -> 403; bad input shape -> 400.\n- **admin does not bypass an explicit allowlist**: `allow roles operator;` rejects admin too.\n- `/api/v1/commands` is exempt from the generic role guard (authentication only); the command route enforces authorization, so a non-admin/operator principal holding the permission can run the command.\n- Checks happen before idempotency receipt lookup and the transaction; a denial writes no business data, audit or receipt. Replay re-checks; an existing receipt does not grant access.\n- The Web records `commandPolicies` (roles, expanded permissions, input-free verification) and prefers permission/verification checks when `/auth/me` carries permission metadata; a verification with inputs falls back to the role list in the browser while the server still enforces.\n\n## Row and field policy (restrict)\n\n```text\nrestrict <resource> {\n  allow roles <role> [, <role>]* ;                      // at most once\n  when <field> claim <claim> ;                          // row predicate: field == claim\n  when <field> ==|!= \"<v>\" [, \"<v>\"] ;                  // literals (==/!= take exactly one value)\n  when <field> in|notIn \"<v>\" [, \"<v>\"] ;               // sets, max 64\n  when ( <condition> or <condition> ) ;                 // disjunction group\n  when <boolean-expression> ;                           // not / and / or / parentheses\n  mask <field> [roles <r>, ...] [claim <present|absent> <claim>] mode <omit|null|redact> [replacement \"<text>\"] ;\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\nrestrict orders {\n  allow roles admin, operator;\n  when tenantId claim tenant.id;\n  when status in \"draft\", \"pending\";\n  when ( ownerId claim user.id or scope );\n  when amount > field cost;\n  mask unitCost roles operator, viewer mode redact replacement \"***\";\n  mask internalNote claim absent compliance.level mode omit;\n}\n```\n\n| Setting | Values | Default | Semantics |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `allow roles` | admin/operator/viewer, non-empty, unique | unrestricted | Whether the resource is usable at all; admin is **not** exempt |\n| `when <field> claim <claim>` | non-null, non-PK field; claim may contain dots | - | Row predicate, `==`; missing claim -> 403 |\n| `when <field> == / != \"<v>\"` | one value | - | Literal row predicate; types Text/enum/Integer/Decimal/Money/Date/Time/DateTime |\n| `when <field> in / notIn \"<v1>\", ...` | <= 64 unique values | - | Set predicate (`hide` semantics) |\n| `when <a> <op> field <b>` | `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `==`, `!=`; comparable classes must match | - | Cross-field comparison; UUID only `==`/`!=` |\n| `when scope` | requires a matching `scope` on the same resource | - | Scope atom, can be OR-ed |\n| `when ... and/or/not/(...)` | general boolean expression | - | ANDed onto rows/groups |\n| `mask <field>` | non-PK, non-`Vector` field; optional roles and claim presence | `mode omit` | Field masking, see below |\n\nRuntime (`security/policy.ts`):\n\n| Case | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Role not in `allow roles` | 403 `policy.resourceDenied` |\n| Claim row predicate with missing claim | 403 `policy.missingClaim` |\n| Literal row predicate | Generates an always-false predicate (`__qiy_policy_never_matches__`); rows are hidden, no error |\n| All disjunction branches dropped for missing claims | 403 `policy.missingClaim` (fail-closed, never \"all rows\") |\n| Expression cannot be evaluated (e.g. `scope` without value) | 403 `policy.missingClaim` |\n| `not (branch with missing claim)` | Unsatisfiable, never \"allow everything\" |\n| Writing a masked field | 400 `policy.maskedField` (masking is read **and** write) |\n| Import containing a masked column | 400 `Masked fields cannot be imported: ...` (`import.maskedField`) |\n| Aggregating a masked field | 403 `policy.maskedField` |\n| Reading | `mask(record)` applies per role/claim: `omit` deletes the key, `null` sets null, `redact` substitutes the fixed string |\n\nRow predicates push down to SQL for list/detail/aggregate/trend/export/update/delete - never client-side filtering. Rows AND together; each group ORs internally and ANDs with rows; expressions AND on top. `mask` is the only mechanism that truly hides data; `pages` field rules only stop rendering.\n\nHard mutual exclusions (generation fails closed):\n\n- A resource with **any** `restrict` block cannot appear in a `dataflow` (context load or create target): `Restrict <resource>: dataflow <name> cannot use a restricted resource until command authorization applies the same row policy`. This applies even if the block only has `allow roles` or `mask`.\n- Realtime cannot subscribe to a resource with a `restrict` row predicate (`when`): `restrict row predicates cannot be enforced on a shared channel`. Role/mask-only restrictions may coexist; `mask` trims the payload before enqueue.\n\n## Data scope (scope)\n\n```text\nscope <resource> <field> claim <claim> [ tree <treeEntity> <parentField> ] ;\n```\n\n```qiy\nscope orders customerId claim tenant.customerId;\nscope warehouses orgId claim org.id tree organizations parentId;\n```\n\n| Slot | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| resource | Entity or table name; at most one declaration per resource |\n| field | `UUID` or `Text`; not a database-enforced restriction on primary keys, but use a tenant/FK column |\n| claim | `^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_.-]*$`, read from `principal.claims` |\n| `tree <entity> <parentField>` | Entity must exist; parent field UUID/Text; types must match the scope field, tree primary key and parent. Generates a `WITH RECURSIVE` subtree CTE (64-level cap) and an organization tree page at `/<treeResource>/tree`; missing parents/self-references/cycles are surfaced as orphans |\n| local/hybrid auth | Every scope claim needs a matching users column (`org.id` -> `orgId`), otherwise generation fails: `Data scope claim org.id needs a matching field on users ...` |\n\nRuntime:\n\n| Path | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Reads (list/detail/aggregate/trend/export/GraphQL) | Adds `field = claim value` (or subtree expansion); missing claim -> 403 `Missing required data scope claim: <claim>` |\n| Claim points to a missing node | Empty subtree -> empty result, never full data |\n| Writes (create/update) | The scope field is **forced** to the claim value; client values are overwritten |\n| Dataflow | `update` may not touch a scope field (`cannot update scope field`); `create` derives it (`create scope field ... is derived from the authenticated principal`) |\n| `restrict { when (scope or ...) }` | The repository-level implicit scope filter is skipped so OR semantics hold; the expression is evaluated instead |\n| API key | Claims are derived from user columns (`org.id` <- `orgId`), so scope applies |\n\n## Page rules (pages)\n\n```qiy\npages orders {\n  list   roles admin, operator, viewer;\n  show   roles admin, operator, viewer;\n  create roles admin, operator;\n  edit   roles admin, operator;\n  delete roles admin;\n  field totalCost roles admin;    // UI only: non-admins do not see the field\n}\n```\n\n| Rule | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Actions | `list`, `show`, `create`, `edit`, `delete`; each at most once |\n| Roles | Non-empty, unique, only admin/operator/viewer |\n| Undeclared actions | Not restricted by page rules (still subject to `restrict.roles` and the role model) |\n| `field <name> roles ...` | UI rendering only (`canSeeField`); it does **not** filter API responses - use `mask` to hide data |\n| Empty block | At least one action or field rule, else `requires at least one page action or field rule` |\n\nThree enforcement layers:\n\n1. Server guard (`auth/guard.ts`): REST maps by method/path (`GET` list -> `list`, `GET /:id` -> `show`, `POST` -> `create`, `PATCH|PUT` -> `edit`, `DELETE` -> `delete`, `export` read -> `list`, `import` read -> `list` / write -> `create`); GraphQL maps by root field; failure is 403 `Page access denied`.\n2. Web: `qiyAccessControlProvider` checks resource role policy then page rules; `resource-page-guard.tsx` wraps the four CRUD routes with `CanAccess`, so a direct URL also renders a 403 result.\n3. API docs: `/api/v1/openapi.json` and `/api/v1/docs/model` trim operations by `pages` (a viewer only keeps `list`/`show`).\n\n## Declaration to artifact map\n\n| DSL | Artifact | Enforcement point |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `auth { ... }` | `auth/guard.ts`, `auth/local.ts`, `auth/oidc.ts`, `auth/hybrid.ts`, `auth/password.ts` | Every request -> `Principal | null` |\n| `permission field/group/from` | `auth/permissions.ts` (`PERMISSION_FIELD_VALUES`, `PERMISSION_GROUPS`, `PERMISSION_CLAIM_SOURCES`), `auth/permission-routes.ts` | `/auth/permissions`, `/auth/verify-permission`, `/auth/me`, command routes |\n| `permission verification` | `PERMISSION_VERIFICATIONS` (serialized expression data) | Verification endpoint, `allow verification`, Web `CanAccess` (input-free) |\n| `restrict` | `security/policy.ts` (`policies`, `resolvePolicy`), resource repositories/routes | Row pushdown, mask read/write, resource-level 403 |\n| `scope` | `security/policy.ts` (`scopeResources`, `scopeHelpers`), `resolveScope()`, tree helper | Read/write implicit filtering |\n| `pages` | `PageRules` in `auth/guard.ts`, `pageRules` in `web/app/auth.ts`, `resources[].fields[].roles` | REST/GraphQL guards, page guard, field rendering, docs filtering |\n| `dataflow allow` | 403 decisions in the command route; Web `commandPolicies` | `/api/v1/commands/<name>`, button visibility |\n| `action allow` | Web `commandPolicies` + business-page route guard | Buttons and `/:id/<action>` pages |\n| `features apiKeys` | `qiy_api_keys`, `auth/api-keys.ts`, `withApiKeyAuthentication` | Bearer / `X-API-Key` fallback authentication |\n\nStable error keys (frontend-translatable): `command.forbidden` (403), `policy.denied` (403), `policy.resourceDenied` (403), `policy.missingClaim` (403), `policy.maskedField` (400/403), `policy.misconfigured` (500, generator defect). Business `require ... @error(t(\"key\"))` returns default-locale text plus `errorKey`.\n\n## Security boundaries and limits\n\n1. **Hidden buttons are not authorization.** `when`, `pages` and `CanAccess` are UX. Writes are enforced by server `restrict`/`scope`/`allow`/`require`.\n2. **Permissions only add.** Every source can only add values. To demote, change the role, the DB column or the IdP claim - there is no subtraction in the DSL, and `mask` cannot revoke a permission.\n3. **admin does not bypass explicit allowlists.** `restrict { allow roles operator; }` and `allow roles operator;` both reject admin. Add admin explicitly if operations need it.\n4. **admin short-circuits only in docs**: `/api/v1/openapi.json` is unfiltered for admin, but row predicates and `allow roles` still check admin (`mayUseResource` has no admin special case).\n5. **Field masks are read/write and cover every generated read path** (list/detail/aggregate/export/realtime payload), but the database column remains plaintext: backups, direct DB access, application logs and external systems are **not** protected. Masked fields also cannot be imported.\n6. **`restrict` blocks and dataflows are mutually exclusive**; row predicates and realtime are mutually exclusive. Do not treat \"the command cannot see it\" as row isolation.\n7. **Shared realtime channels cannot do row isolation.** Only field `mask` trimming and `when <field> claim <claim>` segmented channels exist.\n8. **API keys are session-equivalent.** Leakage grants the user's full permissions (role group + DB column + scope claims). Only an HMAC-SHA256 hash is stored server-side; revocation/expiry takes effect immediately.\n9. **The OpenAPI document is a filtered HTTP endpoint**, not an admin-only artifact or a complete attack-surface list. `allow verification` commands appear only to admin, and row-level scope is not represented in the document structure. Separately, the Elysia plugin's `/api/v1/openapi` is public and has **no** Qiy permission filtering - never treat it as the production document source.\n10. **No rate limiting is generated**: no login failure limit, no account lockout, no CAPTCHA, and OTP challenges are reusable within their 5-minute window. Put rate limiting at the gateway/WAF or the delivery adapter.\n11. **No self-service password change**; account operations are CLI scripts. No refresh tokens; a 12-hour token plus IdP session is the whole story.\n12. **Defaults must be made explicit**: no `restrict.allow roles` means no role restriction; undeclared `pages` actions are unrestricted; no dataflow `allow` means `admin, operator`.\n13. **The `role` column is authoritative**: a stale JWT `role` is ignored because the user row is re-read; do not assume token payload equals current permissions.\n14. **Permission values are a contract**: claims, DB columns, `x-qiy-permissions` and 403 `missing` all use the value string; renaming breaks external IdP/script integrations.\n15. **Integration mode has no Qiy enforcement**: host adapters own authentication and authorization ([workspace-integration.md](workspace-integration.md)).\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Permission declarations require a generated auth block` | `permission` without `auth` | Add `auth` or delete the permission model |\n| `provider is not a configured OAuth/OIDC provider` | claim source uses an unconfigured provider, or `local`/`otp` | Add the provider to `providers`, or use a database column |\n| Command 403 with empty `missing` | verification used a negated set operator or an operator without diagnostics | Trust `allowed`; `missing` is explanatory |\n| Non-admin cannot see a command button | `allow permission` not satisfied or permission metadata missing | Check `/auth/me` `permissions`; DB/claim entries must be permission values or group names |\n| Non-admin cannot see a command in API docs | Principal lacks all expanded permission values | Check group expansion; docs and execution share the same check |\n| `dataflow ... cannot use a restricted resource` | Command context/create uses a resource with any `restrict` block | Remove the resource from the command or drop its `restrict` |\n| `restrict row predicates cannot be enforced on a shared channel` | Realtime plus a row `when` on the same resource | Use `when <field> claim <claim>` or disable realtime for it |\n| `Page access denied` | `pages` disallows the action for the role | Adjust `pages`; export uses `list`, import writes use `create` |\n| `Missing required data scope claim: org.id` | Principal lacks the claim (local session without the column) | Use OIDC, add the users column, or use an API key |\n| Writing a masked field returns 400 | `mask` is bidirectional | Remove the mask or allow the role |\n| Group cycle / self reference | Groups reference each other | Flatten to a list or rewrite as a union |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET must be at least 32 characters` | Missing/short production secret | `openssl rand -hex 32` into the secret manager |\n| Login page shows no provider buttons | Provider's ISSUER/AUDIENCE/JWKS/AUTHORIZATION_URL/CLIENT_ID incomplete | Fill `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_*`; `/auth/providers` lists only complete configs |\n| Immediate 401 after login | Token `iss` differs from the configured issuer | Use the discovery issuer verbatim (trailing `/` aside) |\n| `State mismatch in the provider callback` | Concurrent logins in one browser / cleared sessionStorage | Log in again |\n| `The provider token exchange failed` | Redirect mismatch, missing client secret, unreachable token endpoint | Align redirect, add the secret, set `HTTPS_PROXY` |\n| Onboarding returns 409 | Username/email exists or the identity is bound to another account | Pick another username or bind from the original account |\n| Unbind returns 409 | It is the last login method | Set a password or bind another provider first |\n| OTP 502 `auth.otpDeliveryFailed` | Adapter unreachable, non-2xx, timeout or non-HTTPS | Check the delivery URL, token, timeout and network |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - exact auth/permission block placement and settings\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - `allow`, resources, commands\n- [System features](system-features.md) - API keys, OpenAPI, system pages\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - realtime roles and claim channels\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - auth acceptance and production checks\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - 401/403 symptom table\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [permissions (permission / restrict / scope / pages)](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/permissions)\n- [auth](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/auth)\n- [application: auth/scope/restrict/pages](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/application)\n- [auth guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/auth)\n- [real services acceptance](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/real-services)\n",
  "references/cli-workflows.md": "# CLI workflows\n\nUse this file when you need the exact Qiy CLI commands, flags, output layout, environment requirements, upgrade/sync behavior, or the skill-install command. Every command here is implemented; anything else is not.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/cli\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Install and verify the CLI](#install-and-verify-the-cli)\n- [Command reference](#command-reference)\n- [create: new standalone project](#create-new-standalone-project)\n- [generate: compatibility command](#generate-compatibility-command)\n- [init: mount into an existing Bun project](#init-mount-into-an-existing-bun-project)\n- [Install this skill from the CLI](#install-this-skill-from-the-cli)\n- [doctor](#doctor)\n- [First run](#first-run)\n- [Output layout](#output-layout)\n- [Environment requirements](#environment-requirements)\n- [Upgrade and --sync](#upgrade-and-sync)\n- [Common problems](#common-problems)\n\n## Install and verify the CLI\n\nThe skill and the executable are separate: installing this skill does not install `qiy`.\n\nDownload the asset matching the OS/CPU from [Qiy GitHub Releases](https://github.com/AI-NoDev/qiy/releases/latest):\n\n| Platform | Asset pattern |\n| --- | --- |\n| Windows x64 | `qiy-<version>-windows-x64.exe` |\n| Linux x64 | `qiy-<version>-linux-x64` |\n| Linux ARM64 | `qiy-<version>-linux-arm64` |\n| macOS x64 | `qiy-<version>-darwin-x64` |\n| macOS ARM64 | `qiy-<version>-darwin-arm64` |\n\nPut the executable on `PATH` (or call it by path), `chmod +x` on Linux/macOS, then:\n\n```bash\nqiy --version\nqiy --help\n```\n\nFrom a Qiy source checkout use `bun run qiy -- --help` instead. Do not assume `bunx qiy` exists; it only works if a published npm package is installed and resolves to the expected version.\n\nThe executable embeds the Admin template, so it can generate a complete application outside the repository. The public input format is `.qiy` only; MPS models and Database IR are maintainer tools, not CLI inputs.\n\n## Command reference\n\n```text\nqiy create -f <source.qiy> -n <name> -o <output-dir> [--sync]\nqiy generate <source.qiy> <output-dir> [--sync]\nqiy init -f <source.qiy> [-n <name>] [-o <project-root>] [--sync]\nqiy doctor [--json]\nqiy skill install [--force] [--global] [--dir <path>]\nqiy help            # same as --help\nqiy --help | -h\nqiy --version | -v\n```\n\n| Command | Required flags | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `create` | `-f`, `-n`, `-o` | Generates a standalone Turborepo + Bun workspace. `-o` must be empty or absent; `-n` names the workspace/packages |\n| `generate` | `<source>`, `<output-dir>` | Same generation as `create` with positional arguments, kept for compatibility |\n| `init` | `-f` | Mounts server/web packages into the current Bun workspace. `-o` selects another project root; `-n` overrides the integration name once |\n| `doctor` | - | Checks Bun runtime, the embedded Admin template and the current workspace's Bun declaration; `--json` prints machine-readable output |\n| `skill install` | - | Installs the bundled official skill (see below) |\n| `help` / `--help` / `-h` | - | Prints usage |\n| `--version` / `-v` | - | Prints the CLI version |\n\nUnknown commands exit 1 with `Unknown command: <name>` plus usage. There is no `qiy dev`, `qiy build`, `qiy deploy`, `qiy test` or `qiy release` subcommand - run generated package scripts with Bun instead.\n\n## create: new standalone project\n\n```bash\nqiy create -f ./models/warehouse/app.qiy -n warehouse-admin -o ./warehouse-admin\ncd ./warehouse-admin\nbun install\nbun run typecheck\nbun run test\nbun run build\nbun run preview\n```\n\n- The source must be a `.qiy` file and may use relative `include` fragments; absolute includes, `..`, cycles and symlink escapes are rejected.\n- The output directory must be empty or not exist (`Output directory must be empty`). Use `--sync` only on a directory previously generated by Qiy.\n- `create` ignores most `workspace.aliases` and always produces `apps/server` and `apps/web`.\n- `preview` binds loopback only and serves an in-memory repository; it is a local demo, not a production server. Stop it with Ctrl+C.\n- On success the project contains `openwiki/{quickstart,architecture,development}.md`, `AGENTS.md` and the compatibility `AGENT.MD`, documenting the files and scripts that were actually generated.\n\n## generate: compatibility command\n\n```bash\nqiy generate ./models/app.qiy ./out/admin\nqiy generate ./models/app.qiy ./out/admin --sync\n```\n\nIdentical to `create` except arguments are positional and no `-n` override exists (the application name is used). Prefer `create` for a first generation; use `generate ... --sync` to maintain a workspace that Qiy generated.\n\n## init: mount into an existing Bun project\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/existing-bun-project\nqiy init -f ./models/admin.qiy\nbun install\nbun run qiy:admin:typecheck\nbun run qiy:admin:test\n```\n\nRequirements and behavior:\n\n- The target root's `package.json` must declare `\"packageManager\": \"bun@<version>\"`; `qiy init` refuses to write otherwise.\n- Packages are mounted as `apps/<server-alias>` and `apps/<web-alias>`; deployment files are named from the deploy alias. Declare aliases in the model's `workspace` block ([workspace-integration.md](workspace-integration.md)).\n- Qiy preserves existing workspace patterns, adds `apps/*` when missing, and adds direct `qiy:<name>:*` scripts (`typecheck`, `test`, `preview`, ...). It does not add Turborepo, a `turbo` dependency, or replace host root scripts.\n- Conflicting host files or scripts make the command fail instead of overwriting. Resolve by choosing non-conflicting aliases.\n- Each mounted admin gets its own env files under the aliased app directories. Qiy never writes the host root `.env*`.\n- `--sync` updates only manifest-registered files and removes registered files the model no longer generates; unowned host files are never touched.\n- `mode integration` models mount only the web package (no server, Drizzle, migrations, Docker/Compose) and generate host adapters under `apps/<web>/app/host/`.\n\n## Install this skill from the CLI\n\nThe CLI bundles this skill offline; no network is required.\n\n```bash\n# Current project: <project>/.agents/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install\n\n# User level: ~/.agents/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --global\n\n# Any agent-specific skills directory\nqiy skill install --dir .claude/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --dir .cursor/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --dir ~/.codex/skills/qiy\n\n# After a CLI upgrade: replace locally modified official files\nqiy skill install --force\n```\n\n| Flag | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| none | Writes `.agents/skills/qiy` under the current project |\n| `--global` | Writes `~/.agents/skills/qiy` |\n| `--dir <path>` | Writes the given directory; relative to the project, absolute, or `~/...` |\n| `--force` | Replaces official files that were modified locally; unrelated files are always preserved |\n\nBehavior: repeating an install is idempotent; if an official file differs from the bundled version the command refuses with `Qiy skill has local changes...` and suggests `--force`; a legacy `.agent/skills/qiy` directory is updated in place when it is the only one present; only the skill's `SKILL.md`, `references/` and `examples/` are written. The installed bundle always matches the current CLI version - it never downloads a newer one.\n\nNo network? Extract the published archive instead:\n\n```bash\ntar -xzf qiy-skill.tar.gz -C .agents/skills\n# produces .agents/skills/qiy/{SKILL.md,references/,examples/}\n```\n\nStatic copies: `https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/skills/qiy/SKILL.md` and `.../skills/qiy-skill.tar.gz`. Prefer the CLI so versions stay aligned with the binary.\n\n## doctor\n\n```bash\nqiy doctor\nqiy doctor --json\n```\n\nChecks the Bun runtime, the embedded Admin template and the current directory's Bun package-manager declaration. Outside a Bun workspace it prints a warning; `qiy init` still refuses to write. `--json` emits the report for CI. The command exits 1 when the report is not OK, so it can gate a pipeline.\n\n## First run\n\n```bash\nqiy --version\nqiy doctor\nqiy create -f models/app.qiy -n my-admin -o out/my-admin\ncd out/my-admin\nbun install\nbun run typecheck\nbun run test\nbun run build\nbun run preview\n```\n\nFor a real database: edit `apps/server/.env.development`, set `DATABASE_URL`, run `bun run db:generate` and `bun run db:migrate`, then `bun run dev:server` and `bun run dev:web`. Production configuration lives in `apps/server/.env.production`. A server without auth refuses to start unless `QIY_DEV_MODE=1`.\n\n## Output layout\n\n```text\nmy-admin/\n├── apps/\n│   ├── server/                 # Bun + Elysia API\n│   │   ├── src/                # db, contracts, repositories, services, routes, auth, storage, http.ts\n│   │   ├── drizzle/            # generated migrations + down/\n│   │   ├── tests/\n│   │   └── .env.{development,production,example}\n│   └── web/                    # Refine + React Router SPA\n│       ├── app/                # routes, components, hooks, providers, ui, extensions, i18n.ts\n│       ├── tests/\n│       └── .env.{development,production,example}\n├── deploy/                     # nginx.conf, vercel.json, kubernetes/, observability/\n├── Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, turbo.json, package.json\n├── openwiki/, AGENTS.md, AGENT.MD\n└── .qiy-generated.json         # manifest of Qiy-owned files\n```\n\n`init` uses aliases instead (`apps/<server-alias>`, `apps/<web-alias>`, `deploy/<deploy-alias>`, `<deploy-alias>.Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.<deploy-alias>.yml`, `.qiy-<name>.generated.json`) and puts agent entrypoints in the web package plus `openwiki/qiy-<name>/`.\n\n## Environment requirements\n\n| Requirement | Applies to | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Bun 1.3+ | CLI and generated projects | `bun --version` |\n| `.qiy` source | All generation commands | `.qiy` is the only public input format |\n| Empty output directory | `create`/`generate` without `--sync` | Otherwise `Output directory must be empty` |\n| `packageManager: bun@...` | `init` | Hard requirement in the target root |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | Real server runtime and migrations | Preview does not need it |\n| `QIY_DEV_MODE=1` | Local server without auth | Never in production |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET` (>= 32 chars) | Local/hybrid/OTP/API-key auth | Production startup check |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` | Production storage | Startup check |\n| `HTTPS_PROXY` / `HTTP_PROXY` | Restricted networks | Bun `fetch` for IdP token endpoints |\n| Docker (optional) | Multi-platform executables, acceptance scripts | `bun run build:exe -- --all` |\n\n`.env` files are generated per mode; `--sync` merges new variables while preserving existing values and user-added entries. Never commit real secrets; the `example` files are placeholders.\n\n## Upgrade and sync\n\n- The CLI version and the skill bundle are released together. After upgrading the binary, run `qiy skill install --force` to refresh official skill files.\n- `.qiy-generated.json` records `schemaVersion: 1` and the generating `qiyVersion`. A manifest schema change makes an old `--sync` fail explicitly instead of guessing.\n- The DSL has no forward compatibility: unknown constructs/annotations fail. After an upgrade, regenerate with `qiy generate ... --sync` or `qiy init --sync` and review every generated migration before applying it.\n- `--sync` rewrites only manifest-registered files and deletes registered files the model no longer generates. Files outside the manifest (including `apps/web/app/extensions/` and `apps/server/src/extensions/`) are preserved.\n- Do not hand-edit manifest-owned files and expect merges. Put long-lived custom behavior in unowned extensions, hooks, plugins or host adapters.\n- Sync can fail on local edits to official skill files only for `qiy skill install`; project sync is unaffected by that check.\n\n## Common problems\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `qiy is not recognized` / command not found | Executable not on `PATH` | Add its directory, reopen the terminal, run `qiy --version` |\n| `Output directory must be empty` | Target has files and no `--sync` | Use a new directory, or `--sync` on a Qiy-generated workspace |\n| `qiy init requires packageManager to declare Bun` | Host root has no Bun declaration | Add `\"packageManager\": \"bun@<version>\"`, run `bun install` |\n| `Refusing to overwrite existing host file` | Alias collides with a host path/script | Change `workspace.aliases`; do not delete host files to force generation |\n| `Unknown command: dev` | Generated projects use Bun scripts | `bun run dev` / `bun run preview` inside the workspace |\n| Include error or cycle | Wrong relative path or a cycle | Fix the path relative to the including file; remove the cycle |\n| Port already in use | Another local server | Stop it or set `PORT` |\n| Build passes but API/auth is not connected | Build only compiles | Configure the real database/IdP and implement adapters |\n| `Qiy skill has local changes` | Official skill files were edited | Re-run with `--force` (unrelated files are preserved) |\n| Doctor exits 1 | Runtime/template/package-manager problem | Read the report (or `--json`), fix Bun or the workspace |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Workspace integration](workspace-integration.md) - aliases, integration mode, host adapters\n- [Modeling and generation](modeling-and-generation.md) - model syntax and includes\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - scripts, migrations, acceptance\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - every block and setting\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - cross-area errors\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [CLI and release](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/cli)\n- [Getting started](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/getting-started)\n- [Existing Bun project](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/existing-bun-project)\n- [Project structure](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/project-structure)\n",
  "references/dataflows-actions.md": "# Dataflows, actions and workflows\n\nUse this file when you add a transactional business command, bind it to a list/show button, add a manual extension page, run a batch operation, use the legacy `orderInventory` workflow, or write/run `app.test.qiy` scenario tests.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/dataflow (`/dsl/actions`, `/guide/workflow`)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Choose the right mechanism](#choose-the-right-mechanism)\n- [Dataflow grammar](#dataflow-grammar)\n- [Annotations, authorization and audit](#annotations-authorization-and-audit)\n- [Idempotency](#idempotency)\n- [input: request contract](#input-request-contract)\n- [context: load inside the transaction](#context-load-inside-the-transaction)\n- [steps and statements](#steps-and-statements)\n- [result and HTTP contract](#result-and-http-contract)\n- [Batch execution](#batch-execution)\n- [Actions: exposing commands and pages](#actions-exposing-commands-and-pages)\n- [Manual extension pages](#manual-extension-pages)\n- [workflow orderInventory](#workflow-orderinventory)\n- [app.test.qiy scenarios](#apptestqiy-scenarios)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n- [Non-goals](#non-goals)\n\n## Choose the right mechanism\n\n| Need | Use | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Atomic multi-record business operation (approve, receive, ship, archive) | `dataflow` + `action` | Recommended general mechanism |\n| Transactional event after commit | `dataflow` `emit` | Writes outbox rows; does not publish directly |\n| Read-only custom screen | `action ... navigate` + `page manual @comment(...)` | Implement under `app/extensions/`, preserved by `--sync` |\n| Fixed legacy ERP order/inventory slice | `workflow orderInventory;` | PostgreSQL only, fixed entities/actions, no row policy |\n| Host API business logic | Host code | `mode integration` rejects `dataflow` |\n\nA `dataflow` alone never adds UI. Declaring an `action` is what exposes it.\n\n## Dataflow grammar\n\n```qiy\ndataflow revokeConnector @label(\"Revoke\") @confirm(\"Revoke this connector?\") @comment(\"Revoke an active connector\") {\n  allow roles admin, operator;          // or allow permission / allow verification\n  idempotency required;                 // optional\n  audit \"connector.revoked\";            // optional\n\n  input {\n    field connectorId UUID @required;\n    field reason Text @required @comment(\"Reason supplied by the operator\");\n  }\n\n  context {\n    connector = entity connectors by id input.connectorId @required;\n  }\n\n  step validate @order(10) @comment(\"Check state\") {\n    require connector.status != \"revoked\" @error(\"errors.connector.alreadyRevoked\");\n  }\n\n  step revoke @order(20) {\n    update connector { status = \"revoked\"; }\n    emit \"connector.revoked\" { connectorId = connector.id; reason = input.reason; }\n  }\n\n  result { return connector; }\n}\n```\n\n```text\ndataflow <Name> ( \"@label\" \"(\" doc \")\" | \"@confirm\" \"(\" doc \")\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* {\n  ( \"allow\" ( \"roles\" role (\",\" role)* | \"permission\" ref (\",\" ref)* | \"verification\" Name ) \";\"\n  | \"idempotency\" \"required\" \";\"\n  | \"audit\" <string> \";\"\n  | \"input\" \"{\" ( \"field\" <name> <type> ( \"@required\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* \";\" )* \"}\"\n  | \"context\" \"{\" ( <binding> \"=\" \"entity\" <Entity> \"by\" <pk> \"input.\" <field> ( \"@required\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* \";\" )* \"}\"\n  | \"step\" <Name> ( \"@order\" \"(\" <int> \")\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* \"{\" <statement>* \"}\"\n  | \"result\" \"{\" \"return\" <binding> \";\" \"}\"\n  )+\n}\n```\n\n`input`, `context` and `result` blocks are mandatory (empty `{}` is allowed for the first two; `result` must return a declared binding) and at least one `step` is required. Serialization order is fixed: annotations -> `allow` -> `idempotency` -> `audit` -> `input` -> `context` -> `step...` -> `result`.\n\n`doc` is a string literal or `t(\"key\")`; the key must exist in the default `messages` locale.\n\n## Annotations, authorization and audit\n\n| Annotation | Effect | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `@label(...)` | Command display name; an action that omits `label` inherits it | none (an action needs a label or an inheritable flow label) |\n| `@confirm(...)` | Default confirmation text; an action may omit or override | none (no confirmation dialog) |\n| `@comment(...)` | JSDoc, OpenAPI description, GraphQL mutation description | none |\n\n`allow` accepts exactly one form per flow (a second declaration is `duplicate allow declaration`; no declaration defaults to `admin, operator`):\n\n```qiy\nallow roles admin, operator;                 // only admin/operator; viewer is rejected\nallow permission InventoryReceivePermission; // needs every expanded permission value\nallow verification CanShipOrders;            // evaluated with flow inputs\n```\n\n- `allow roles`: unauthenticated 401; role not listed 403 `Command execution is restricted`. admin does **not** bypass an explicit allowlist.\n- `allow permission`: permission fields or groups, expanded to values at generation; any missing value -> 403 `{ errorKey: \"command.forbidden\", missing }`.\n- `allow verification`: evaluated with flow inputs; each verification `input` needs a same-named `@required` Text or enum flow input; denial -> 403 `command.forbidden`; bad input shape 400.\n- Checks run before idempotency lookup and the transaction: a denial writes no data, audit or receipt. Replay re-checks; a receipt does not grant access.\n\n`audit \"action.name\";` writes `audit_events` in the same transaction with `actorId`, `action`, `resource` (the result binding's table), `resourceId` (its primary key) and `metadata { flow }`. An audit write failure rolls back the whole command.\n\nFull permission semantics: [auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md).\n\n## Idempotency\n\n```qiy\nidempotency required;\n```\n\n- The request must send an `Idempotency-Key` header of **1-128 printable ASCII** (`\\x21-\\x7E`); missing/invalid -> 400 `A valid Idempotency-Key header is required`.\n- Receipts are unique per `(actorId, flow, sha256(key))`. A different request body hash -> 409 `Idempotency key was already used with a different request`; an identical one replays the first response without repeating writes, audit or events.\n- Receipt table `dataflow_idempotency` (`requestKeyHash`, `requestHash`, `response` JSON text) is migrated automatically but **never auto-cleaned**.\n- Batch commands use `<flow>:batch` as an independent flow name and write one receipt.\n- Generated actions manage the key: retries with the same input keep it, changed input or success rotates it.\n- Only `required` exists; there is no `optional` mode.\n\n## input: request contract\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Types | `UUID`, `Text`, `Integer`, `Decimal`, `Boolean`, or a declared enum name |\n| `@required` | Required marker; default is optional. Any input referenced by a context key, `require`, `update`, `create`, `emit` or `call` **must** be `@required` |\n| `@comment(...)` | TypeBox/OpenAPI description and Refine form field label; supports `t(\"key\")` |\n| Defaults | No default syntax; an omitted optional input is `undefined` |\n| Request boundary | Only declared fields (`additionalProperties: false`); `Integer` range -2147483648..2147483647; type violations -> 422 |\n\n```qiy\ninput {\n  field decision reviewState @required;   // enum input: must be the same declared enum\n  field quantity Integer @required;\n  field note Text;\n}\n```\n\n## context: load inside the transaction\n\n```qiy\ncontext {\n  order = entity sales_orders by id input.orderId @required;\n  item  = entity sales_order_lines by id input.lineId @required;\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Loading | Primary key only: `by <pk> input.<field>`; no arbitrary `where` |\n| `@required` | Mandatory today (`context bindings must declare @required until optional-flow semantics are implemented`) |\n| Input | Must be `@required` and `UUID` (the primary key type) |\n| Missing record | 404 `{ error: \"Not found\", resource: \"<table>\" }` |\n| Names | Cannot be `input`; cannot collide with a `create` binding |\n| Locking | PostgreSQL/MySQL use `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`; SQLite runs synchronously in one transaction |\n\n## steps and statements\n\nEach step has a unique positive `@order`; omitted orders default to declaration order (1, 2, 3...). Duplicates/non-positive/non-integer -> `step order must be a unique positive integer`. Statements are order-sensitive: a `require` sees the state after earlier `update`/`create`/`delete` statements.\n\n### require\n\n```qiy\nrequire connector.status != \"revoked\" @error(\"errors.connector.alreadyRevoked\");\nrequire input.quantity >= 100 @error(t(\"inventory.quantityTooLow\"));\n```\n\n| Left operand type | Operators | Right operand |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Text` / enum | `==`, `!=` | String literal (enum value must be declared) |\n| non-null `Integer` | `==`, `!=`, `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=` | Signed 32-bit integer literal (negatives allowed) |\n| Anything else (Decimal/Money/Date/Time/DateTime/Boolean/UUID/Vector) | **unsupported** | - |\n\nThe left operand must be `input.<field>` (that input `@required`) or an undeleted context field. `@error(...)` is mandatory (literal or `t(\"key\")`). Failure -> **409** with default-locale `error` and a stable `errorKey`. Field-to-field comparison, arithmetic, function calls and Decimal/Boolean conditions are not supported; nullable Integer comparison is rejected.\n\n### update\n\n```qiy\nupdate connector { status = \"revoked\"; revokedReason = input.reason; }\n```\n\n| Value source | Allowed target types |\n| --- | --- |\n| Literal (`\"text\"` / enum name) | `Text`, enum |\n| `input.<field>` | `Text`, `Integer`, `UUID`, or the same declared enum |\n\nAt least one field; a field may not be written twice (`duplicate update field`). Forbidden: primary key (`cannot update primary key`), `scope` field (`cannot update scope field`), local `passwordField` (`cannot update password field`), deleted context (`cannot update deleted context`). Decimal/Boolean input assignment is not supported for updates. Later `require` statements see the new value; a failed assertion rolls back.\n\n### create\n\n```qiy\ncreate review = entity reviews {\n  userId = input.userId;\n  note = input.note;\n  status = \"pending\";\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Binding | Enters the context namespace; usable by later `require`/`update`/`delete`/`result`; cannot collide with another binding or `input` |\n| Primary key | Generated; explicit assignment is rejected (`create primary key ... is generated automatically`) |\n| Scope fields | Derived from the authenticated principal; client input cannot override |\n| Required columns | Every non-null, non-PK, non-scope field must be assigned; nullable may be omitted (`create requires value for <entity>.<field>`) |\n| Value source | Literals only `Text`/enum; `input.<field>` supports `UUID`/`Text`/`Integer`/`Decimal` and a same-named enum |\n| Password field | Rejected |\n\n### delete\n\n```qiy\ndelete review;\n```\n\nDeletes a loaded or newly created binding; FK policy decides cascade/reject. The binding cannot be used afterwards (`cannot use deleted context` / `context ... is already deleted`), but it **may** be returned in `result` as its pre-delete snapshot. Same transaction as everything else.\n\n### emit\n\n```qiy\nemit \"order.approved\";\nemit \"order.approved\" {\n  orderId = order.id;\n  requestedBy = input.reason;\n  source = \"dashboard\";\n  priority = 2;\n};\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Event name | Non-empty fixed string; no variables/concatenation |\n| Payload | At most **32** fields, unique keys |\n| Sources | `@required` inputs, current undeleted context fields, string or safe-integer constants |\n| Forbidden | Local password fields; deleted/unknown context; unknown input/field |\n| Persistence | `dataflow_outbox` (event name, actor, payload JSON, created time) in the same transaction |\n| Realtime | With `realtime` declared, also writes `qiy_realtime_outbox` with channel `qiy:event:<event>`, committed/rolled back together |\n\n`emit` only persists; it does not publish to a broker. Consumers, idempotency and dead letters are your responsibility. An idempotent replay does not duplicate events.\n\n### call\n\n```qiy\ncall reviewPolicy {\n  reviewId = review.id;\n  status = review.status;\n  reason = input.reason;\n  source = \"qiy-dashboard\";\n  priority = 1;\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Adapter | Identifier; a flow may call several adapters |\n| Payload | At most 32 unique fields with the same sources as `emit` |\n| Forbidden | Password fields, deleted context, unknown fields |\n| Contract | Generated in `apps/server/src/dataflows/calls.ts` |\n| Implementation | `apps/server/src/extensions/dataflow-calls.ts` (not managed by `--sync`) |\n| Default | Fail-closed: handlers must return `{ ok: true }` or `{ ok: false, error, errorKey? }` |\n| Failure | `{ ok: false }` -> 409 with `error`/`errorKey`; a thrown error rolls back the transaction |\n| Sync only | Handlers must not return a Promise and must not do network/irreversible work; use `emit` + a post-commit worker for that |\n\n```ts\nimport type { DataflowCallHandlers } from \"../dataflows/calls\";\n\nexport const dataflowCallHandlers: DataflowCallHandlers = {\n  reviewPolicy: (request) => {\n    const reason = String(request.payload.reason ?? \"\").trim();\n    if (!reason) return { ok: false, error: \"A reason is required\", errorKey: \"review.reasonRequired\" };\n    return { ok: true };\n  },\n};\n```\n\n## result and HTTP contract\n\n```qiy\nresult { return connector; }\n```\n\n`result` must return a declared context binding (including a `create` binding), else `result must return a declared context binding`. The REST success body is that record's JSON (200); GraphQL returns the entity type. A deleted record may be returned as its last snapshot.\n\n| HTTP | Case | Body |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 200 | Success / idempotent replay | Result record |\n| 400 | Missing/invalid `Idempotency-Key`; bad request shape | `error` |\n| 401 | Unauthenticated | `error: \"Authentication required\"` |\n| 403 | Role/permission/verification denial; missing scope claim | `error`, `errorKey` (`command.forbidden`, ...), optional `missing` |\n| 404 | Context record not found | `error: \"Not found\"`, `resource` |\n| 409 | `require` failure; `create` conflict; idempotency body mismatch | `error`, optional `errorKey`, `resource` |\n| 422 | Type/range validation (Elysia) | Validation details |\n| 500 | Unexpected error | `error` |\n\nGraphQL commands keep the same machine contract in `extensions.status` and `extensions.errorKey`. `require ... @error(t(\"key\"))` returns the default-locale text plus `errorKey`; the Refine data provider translates it for the current UI language and falls back to the API text.\n\nGenerated endpoints: `POST /api/v1/commands/<name>` (plus `/batch`), GraphQL `run<Name>(input: <Name>CommandInput!, idempotencyKey: String!)` and `run<Name>Batch(items: [...], idempotencyKey: String!)`, OpenAPI operations under `tags: [\"Dataflow\"]`. `/api/v1/commands` is exempt from the generic role guard; the command route runs authorization itself.\n\n## Batch execution\n\n```qiy\ndataflow archiveReview @label(\"Archive selected\") {\n  allow roles admin, operator;\n  idempotency required;\n  input { field reviewId UUID @required; field reason Text @required; }\n  context { review = entity reviews by id input.reviewId @required; }\n  step archive { update review { status = \"archived\"; note = input.reason; } }\n  result { return review; }\n}\n\naction archiveSelected {\n  resource reviews;\n  dataflow archiveReview;\n  placement list;\n  batch true;\n}\n```\n\n- Endpoint `POST /api/v1/commands/<name>/batch`, body `{ \"items\": [ { ... }, ... ] }` with 1-100 unique IDs (duplicates -> 400 `Batch item identifiers must be unique`).\n- All items run sequentially in **one transaction**; any failure rolls back everything and the response carries `item: { index, id }` plus `resource`/`errorKey`.\n- One receipt is written under flow name `<name>:batch`; identical items and key replay, different order/content -> 409.\n- Action constraints: `placement list` only, no record-level `when`, the flow must declare `idempotency required`, and the target resource must be loaded by exactly one required UUID input.\n\n## Actions: exposing commands and pages\n\n```text\naction <Name> {\n  \"resource\" <entity> \";\"\n  ( \"dataflow\" <Name> | \"navigate\" <string> ) \";\"\n  \"placement\" ( \"list\" | \"show\" ) ( \",\" ( \"list\" | \"show\" ) )* \";\"\n  [ \"label\" doc \";\" ]\n  [ \"confirm\" doc \";\" ]            // dataflow action only\n  [ \"when\" <field> ( \"==\" | \"!=\" ) <string> \";\" ]\n  [ \"allow\" ( \"roles\" role (\",\" role)* | \"permission\" ref (\",\" ref)* | \"verification\" <Name> ) \";\" ]   // navigate only\n  [ \"batch\" \"true\" \";\" ]           // dataflow action only\n  [ \"page\" \"manual\" \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" \";\" ]   // navigate only\n}\n```\n\n`resource`, `placement` and exactly one of `dataflow`/`navigate` are required.\n\n| Property | Required | Default | Rules |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `resource` | yes | - | Entity or table name; unknown -> `unknown resource` |\n| `dataflow <Name>` | one of two | - | Must be declared, and its `context` must load this resource, else `dataflow <f> does not load resource <t>` |\n| `navigate \"<path>\"` | one of two | - | Absolute route matching `^/[a-z0-9_-]+(/[a-z0-9_-]+|:[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)*$`, must contain `:id`, no `..`, `\\`, `?`, `#` |\n| `placement list` / `show` | yes (>=1) | - | Table actions column / detail action area; duplicates rejected |\n| `label` | navigate yes; dataflow optional | inherits flow `@label` | Display name; `t(\"key\")` supported; neither -> generation fails |\n| `confirm` | no | inherits flow `@confirm` | Confirmation dialog; dataflow actions only |\n| `when <field> == \\| != \"<value>\"` | no | always visible | Record visibility. Field must be `Text` or enum on this resource; enum values must be declared; only `==`/`!=` |\n| `allow roles/permission/verification` | no | inherits flow (dataflow action) | navigate actions accept admin/operator/viewer, permission fields/groups, and input-free verification; **forbidden** on dataflow actions |\n| `batch true` | no | `false` | See batch constraints above |\n| `page manual @comment(...)` | navigate yes | - | Placeholder page + unmanaged extension file; `@comment` required |\n\n`when` is presentation logic only. A missing field or non-matching value hides the button, but direct command calls are still enforced by server `allow`/`require`. `when` is not allowed on batch actions.\n\nGenerated behavior:\n\n- `placement list` adds a table row action; `placement show` adds a detail-page action. A `confirm` value shows an Ant Design `Modal.confirm`; cancel sends nothing.\n- Visibility goes through Refine `CanAccess`: resource role policy and page rules first, then command policy (`roles` -> expanded `permissions` -> input-free `verification`).\n- Success shows a notification and refreshes list/detail caches; failure keeps the dialog and inputs and translates `errorKey`; batch success clears the selection.\n- The primary-key input (e.g. `input.reviewId`) is injected from the current record (`idInput`) and does not appear in the form. Other `@required` inputs render as: Text -> Input, Integer -> InputNumber, enum -> Select with enum labels, UUID -> Input. `@comment`/`t(\"key\")` becomes the field label/help.\n- Requests go only to `/api/v1/commands/<flow>`; the generated data provider rejects any undeclared command URL (fail-closed).\n- i18n keys when no explicit text is declared: `qiy.actions.<action>.label`, `qiy.actions.<action>.confirm`, `qiy.actions.<action>.inputs.<input>.label`.\n\nIntegration mode: `qiyHostAuth.can` is the single visibility source; `action allow` cannot replace host policy ([workspace-integration.md](workspace-integration.md)).\n\n## Manual extension pages\n\n```qiy\naction reviewConnector {\n  allow roles operator, viewer;\n  resource connectors;\n  placement list, show;\n  label \"Review\";\n  navigate \"/connectors/:id/review\";\n  page manual @comment(t(\"review.pageHelp\"));\n}\n```\n\n- Generates route `/connectors/:id/review` wrapped in `CanAccess` (`action: \"reviewConnector\"`); direct URLs are checked too.\n- Generates a placeholder page under `apps/web/app/extensions/` (explanation + empty state). That directory is **not** in the generated manifest, so `qiy create --sync` / `qiy init --sync` will not overwrite your implementation.\n- The page receives only `:id`. Read data with Refine hooks or your own API; implement server authorization separately (`restrict`/`scope`/host API). Do not put extension code outside `app/extensions/`.\n\n## workflow orderInventory\n\n```qiy\napplication qiy-erp-admin {\n  database postgresql {}\n  workflow orderInventory;\n}\n```\n\n- Only `orderInventory` is accepted (`Unsupported workflow X`); duplicates fail. It sits after `messages`/`permission`, before `enum`/`entity`.\n- Requires **PostgreSQL** and the entities `orders`, `orderItems`, `inventoryItems` with the fixed field contract (missing fields produce specific errors such as `orderInventory workflow requires orders.approvedBy`).\n- Generates submit/approve/ship/cancel actions (REST endpoints + detail buttons), multi-warehouse reservation/release, transactional state checks, `order_reservations` and `order_idempotency` tables, and order/inventory relation queries.\n\nState machine:\n\n```text\ndraft --submit--> submitted --approve--> approved --ship--> shipped\n  |                    |\n  +----> cancelled <---+\n```\n\nOnly `draft` and `submitted` can be cancelled; `approved` must ship (no approval rollback). Reservation on submit, release on cancel and deduction on ship happen in the server transaction. Replays return the first result; different content 409.\n\nAuthorization: the workflow reuses generated role guards and account roles; `scope` filtering applies (missing claim -> 403 `Missing required data scope claim`); `restrict` row policy is **not supported** (`Restrict <resource>: orderInventory does not apply row policy yet`); the workflow does not participate in `allow permission`/`allow verification`. Use a `dataflow` when you need permission-gated approvals.\n\nAcceptance: `bun tools/verify-postgres-erp.ts qiy-erp-pg` creates and drops a temporary database and exercises idempotent submits, approval roles, tenant claim denials, insufficient-stock rollback, cancel/release and duplicate cancel. Identity is injected; it is not a real-login or browser acceptance test.\n\n## app.test.qiy scenarios\n\nWhen the entry model is `app.qiy`, the CLI looks for `app.test.qiy` in the same directory and compiles `given -> when dataflow -> expect` into Bun tests for the generated server.\n\n```qiy\nqiy test v0;\napplication dataflow-call;\n\nscenario approve-review {\n  given review = entity reviews {\n    id = \"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001\";\n    status = \"pending\";\n    note = \"Requires policy approval\";\n  }\n  when dataflow approveReview {\n    reviewId = review.id;\n    reason = \"Approved by operator\";\n  }\n  expect status == 200;\n  expect review.status == \"approved\";\n}\n```\n\n| Element | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| `application` | Must equal the main model's application name |\n| `given` | At least one fixture; every non-null field must be provided; values must match types (`Date` `\"YYYY-MM-DD\"`, `Time` `\"HH:mm:ss\"`, `DateTime` millisecond timestamp, enum name) |\n| `identity` | Optional. `identity anonymous;` or `identity { id = \"...\"; role = \"operator\"; claims { \"tenant.id\" = review.tenantId; } }`; id non-empty, role one of the three, claims may reference fixtures |\n| `when dataflow` | Only declared flows; every required input present; inputs may reference fixture fields |\n| `expect status` | **Required** (100-599) |\n| `expect errorKey == \"...\"` | Optional stable error key assertion |\n| `expect <alias>.<field> == value` | Optional, repeatable; duplicate assertions fail |\n| `expect exists <alias> == false` | Asserts deletion; cannot coexist with field assertions for that alias |\n| `expect outbox \"<event>\" count == <n>` | Asserts `dataflow_outbox` count; the event must be declared by a model `emit` |\n\n- Scenarios reuse the generated auth roles, idempotency headers, transactional route and `call` contract; `call` adapters are stubbed to succeed rather than exercising your policy.\n- SQLite uses an in-memory database. PostgreSQL/MySQL require migrated dedicated databases named `qiy_test_*`, with `DATABASE_URL` and `QIY_TEST_DATABASE_URL` both set to the same value; otherwise execution is refused before importing the database.\n- Fixtures insert parents before children following explicit relations and clean up children first; cyclic foreign keys fail at generation. Tests clear model tables and Dataflow auxiliary tables before and after each scenario - never point them at a business database or share the database between parallel runners.\n- These tests cover authorization and isolation **after** the authenticator returns a principal; they do not issue or verify real JWTs, cookies or IdP logins. Browser action scenarios are not implemented.\n\nRun generated scenario tests:\n\n```bash\n# SQLite\ncd apps/server && bun test tests/qiy-scenarios.test.ts\n\n# PostgreSQL / MySQL\nexport DATABASE_URL='postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/qiy_test_admin'\nexport QIY_TEST_DATABASE_URL=\"$DATABASE_URL\"\nbun run --bun drizzle-kit generate\nbun run --bun drizzle-kit migrate\nbun test tests/qiy-scenarios.test.ts\n```\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 400 `A valid Idempotency-Key header is required` | Flow declares `idempotency required` but the caller sent no key | Send the header; generated actions do it for you |\n| 409 with a business `errorKey` | A `require` assertion failed | Fix the caller's input/state; add frontend copy for the key |\n| 404 `Not found` + `resource` | `context` cannot load the record (bad id or out of scope) | Check the id and data scope |\n| 403 `command.forbidden` | `allow permission`/`allow verification` denied | Inspect `/auth/me` `permissions`/`groups` |\n| `cannot update scope field` | Command writes a scope column | Scope columns derive from the principal |\n| `create requires value for <e>.<f>` | Non-null field not assigned | Assign it or make it `@nullable` |\n| `Dataflow <n> requires input, context, and result blocks` | Missing block, even when empty | Write `input {}`, `context {}` |\n| `result must return a declared context binding` | Returned an undeclared name | Return a context/create binding |\n| `literal updates currently support Text and enum fields only` | Literal used for Integer/Decimal/Date | Use a matching `input.<f>` or a `call` adapter |\n| `call` always returns 409 | Extension still returns the fail-closed default | Implement the handler and return `{ ok: true }` |\n| Button does not render | `when` mismatch, `CanAccess` denial, or missing permission metadata | Check record value, role and `/auth/me` |\n| Button click returns 403 | Server `allow`/`require` denied | Hiding buttons is not authorization |\n| Primary-key field missing from the form | Injected from the current record by design | Expected (`idInput`) |\n| Batch button disabled/failing | Missing `batch true`, no `idempotency required`, or a `when` | Follow the batch constraints |\n| Manual page overwritten by `--sync` | Implementation placed outside `app/extensions/` | Only edit `app/extensions/` |\n| GraphQL mutation complains about a missing argument | Idempotency enabled | Pass `idempotencyKey` |\n\n## Non-goals\n\nDo not promise these:\n\n- Arbitrary expressions, arithmetic, function calls, loops, dynamic SQL, reflection, embedded JS/TS.\n- Arbitrary `where` loading, joins or aggregate reads inside a flow (use resource REST/GraphQL for queries).\n- Async/external side effects: `call` must be synchronous and network-free; use `emit` plus a post-commit worker.\n- Direct broker publishing, consumer idempotency or dead-letter handling.\n- Optional context, field-to-field comparisons, Decimal/Boolean conditions, dynamic Decimal writes.\n- Nested transactions, cross-command compensation or distributed transactions.\n- Generated commands in `mode integration` (rejected).\n- Custom roles in `allow roles` (only admin/operator); use `allow permission` for finer control.\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - `allow`, verification, restrict/scope\n- [Modeling and generation](modeling-and-generation.md) - entities, relations, generated values\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - emitted events and realtime delivery\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - generated test suites and release checks\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - block order and declaration grammar\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - command error table\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [dataflow](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/dataflow)\n- [actions](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/actions)\n- [workflow guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/workflow)\n- [permissions: command allow](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/permissions)\n",
  "references/language-reference.md": "# Qiy DSL language reference\n\nUse this file as the complete map of the `.qiy` language: lexical rules, strict declaration order, every application block and setting, entity/field grammar, relations/indexes, enums, generated values, display templates, and the placement matrix for every annotation. Open the focused reference for deep behavior; this page is enough to write a syntactically valid model.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/overview\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Lexical rules](#lexical-rules)\n- [Declaration order](#declaration-order)\n- [Validation pipeline](#validation-pipeline)\n- [Minimal valid model](#minimal-valid-model)\n- [application settings](#application-settings)\n- [database](#database)\n- [mode and integration](#mode-and-integration)\n- [workspace](#workspace)\n- [ui](#ui)\n- [api](#api)\n- [features](#features)\n- [realtime](#realtime)\n- [elysia](#elysia)\n- [storage](#storage)\n- [auth](#auth)\n- [env](#env)\n- [messages](#messages)\n- [permission](#permission)\n- [workflow](#workflow)\n- [enum](#enum)\n- [entity and field](#entity-and-field)\n- [relation and index](#relation-and-index)\n- [scope, restrict, pages](#scope-restrict-pages)\n- [menu](#menu)\n- [dashboard](#dashboard)\n- [chart and chart panels](#chart-and-chart-panels)\n- [dataflow](#dataflow)\n- [action](#action)\n- [Annotation inventory](#annotation-inventory)\n- [Generated values](#generated-values)\n- [Display templates](#display-templates)\n- [i18n keys](#i18n-keys)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## Lexical rules\n\n| Category | Rule | Example |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Identifier | `[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9-]*` (internal hyphens allowed) | `orders`, `azure-ad-b2c`, `order_items` |\n| Integer | `-?\\d+` (negatives only in dataflow integer comparisons) | `1536`, `8`, `-1` |\n| Double-quoted string | JSON string: `\\\" \\\\ \\/ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\uXXXX` | `\"用户总数\"`, `\"a\\nb\"` |\n| Single-quoted string | Only `\\\\` and `\\'` escape; other backslashes are literal | `'C:\\path'` |\n| Comment | `#` or `//` to end of line (not inside strings) | `# domain note` |\n| Multi-char symbols | `&&`, `\\|\\|`, `==`, `!=`, `>=`, `<=` | permission/policy expressions |\n| Single-char symbols | `{ } ( ) ; , @ . = < > ! & \\|` | structure |\n| Whitespace | any amount, separators only | - |\n\nAnything else (`:`, `[`, `]`, `*`, `+`, `%`, `?`, `$`, backticks, non-ASCII) fails the lexer with `Unexpected Qiy syntax at offset N`. Put such content in quotes (`\"CN-0001\"`, `\"https://...\"`, `\"{seq:4}\"`). Bare values are allowed only for ASCII identifiers (`@icon(AppstoreOutlined)`, `theme blue`); double and single quotes are not equivalent (`\"a\\nb\"` is a newline, `'a\\nb'` is a backslash plus `n`).\n\nSemicolons:\n\n| Position | `;` | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `field`, `index`, `relation`, `scope`, `metric`, `permission field/from`, `workflow`, `variable` declarations | required | Missing -> `Expected ; near token N` |\n| Block closing `}` (`database`, `ui`, `entity`, `enum`, `menu`, `chart`, ...) | **not allowed** | Extra `;` -> `Expected ... near token N` |\n| `permission group { ... }`, `permission verification { ... }` | optional | List form may end with `;` |\n| `chart` view properties | required between properties; optional before `}` | `expected ; after the property value` |\n| `emit`/`call` payload blocks | block `;` optional; each assignment needs `;` | - |\n| `require ... @error(\"...\");` | required | - |\n\nNumbers are integers only (type parameters, annotations, `chart panels` grid/coords, dataflow integer comparisons). There are no float literals; use `Decimal`/`Money` types.\n\n## Declaration order\n\n```text\nqiy v0;                                   # first declaration (only v0 exists)\napplication <name> [@comment] { ... }     # exactly one per project\n  database <dialect> [@comment] { extension ...; }    # first inside application\n  mode standalone|integration;\n  integration { ... }\n  workspace { ... }\n  ui { ... }\n  api { ... }\n  features { ... }\n  realtime { ... }\n  elysia { ... }\n  storage { ... }\n  auth { ... }\n  env { ... }\n  messages { ... }\n  permission ...                          # contiguous, 0..N\n  workflow orderInventory;\n  enum ...                                # before entities\n  entity ... { field ...; index ...; }\n  relation ...;                           # after all entities\n  scope ...;\n  restrict ... { ... }\n  pages ... { ... }\n  menu { ... }                            # at most one\n  dashboard { metric ...; } / chart ... / chart panels ...\n  dataflow ... { ... }\n  action ... { ... }\n}\n```\n\nThe parser is a single-pass recursive descent: it `expect`s each construct in this order and reports `Expected <keyword> near token N` on the first mismatch. Consequences:\n\n- `database` must be the first declaration after `application {`.\n- `permission` declarations must come immediately after `messages` (and before `workflow`/`enum`/`entity`); writing another top-level block between them fails.\n- Enums before entities, entities before relations, `pages` before `menu`, `menu` before `dashboard`/`chart`, `dataflow` before `action`.\n- Optional singleton blocks (`mode`, `integration`, `workspace`, `ui`, `api`, `features`, `realtime`, `elysia`, `storage`, `auth`, `env`, `messages`) may be omitted, but their slot cannot move.\n- `dashboard` and `chart` share one slot and may interleave.\n- After `include` expansion the whole model must satisfy the same order ([modeling-and-generation.md](modeling-and-generation.md)).\n\n## Validation pipeline\n\n```text\ninclude expansion -> lexer/parser -> IR validation -> generation validation -> write files\n```\n\n| Stage | Checks | Typical error |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Include expansion | relative `.qiy` paths, `..`/absolute/symlink escapes, cycles, selectors | `Qiy include cycle detected: ...` |\n| Parser | tokens, block order, annotation values, duplicates, templates, chart semantics, permission model, cross-block references | `Expected entity near token 42`, `Unsupported field attribute @required` |\n| IR validation | names/types/indexes/relations/display templates with FK info | `V3 foreign keys require UUID fields` |\n| Generation | primary-key shape, icons, route names, auth columns, scope/restrict, menu/metrics, CORS, cron/static, features deps, permission sources | `V0 CRUD requires exactly one UUID primary key named id` |\n| Write | path safety, env merge, manifest, `--sync` cleanup | `Output directory must be empty` |\n\nParse errors abort on the first problem; IR/generation errors are collected and joined. The CLI exits 1 and writes nothing on failure. Parse success does not imply generation success.\n\n## Minimal valid model\n\n```qiy\nqiy v0;\n\napplication inventory @comment(\"Inventory operations console\") {\n  database sqlite @comment(\"Local inventory records\") {}\n\n  entity products @label(\"Products\") @icon(ShoppingOutlined) {\n    field id UUID @id;\n    field sku Text @unique;\n    field name Text;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## application settings\n\n| Block | Syntax / keys | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `database` | `postgresql` / `mysql` / `sqlite` | dialect identifier | required |\n| `mode` | `standalone` / `integration` | identifier | `standalone` |\n| `integration` | `apiBase`, `auth`, `response`, `pagination`, `tenant` | see below | only with `mode integration` |\n| `workspace` | `name`, `aliases { server web deploy }`, `packages { server web }` | identifiers / quoted names | application name |\n| `ui` | `library`, `theme`, `themes`, `colorMode`, `allowThemeSwitch`, `allowColorModeSwitch` | see below | antd/blue/all five/system/true/true |\n| `api` | `client`, `cors { origin ...; }` | `rest`/`graphql`; exact origins | `rest` |\n| `features` | `overview`, `apiDocs`, `apiKeys` | booleans | `true`, `false`, `false` |\n| `realtime` | `mode`, `resource { events; roles; when }` | see below | `auto` |\n| `elysia` | `bearer`, `serverTiming`, `html`, `drizzle`, `jwt`, `static`, `graphqlAdapter`, `cron` | switches/blocks | off, `native` |\n| `storage` | `provider` | `local`/`s3` | `local` |\n| `auth` | `provider`/`providers`, `user`, `subjectField`, `roleField`, `usernameField`, `passwordField`, `profileField`, provider mappings | see below | required fields |\n| `env` | `variable NAME { secret; development; production; example; }` | literals/`required`/`generate` | empty |\n| `messages` | `default`, `locale` | BCP 47 + dictionaries | `zh-CN`, empty |\n| `permission` | `field`, `group`, `from`, `verification` | see below | none |\n| `workflow` | `orderInventory;` | single fixed value | none |\n| `scope` | `scope <resource> <field> claim <claim> [tree <entity> <parentField>];` | fields/claims | none |\n| `restrict` | `allow roles`, `when`, `mask` | see below | none |\n| `pages` | actions + field rules | roles | none |\n\n## database\n\n```text\ndatabase <postgresql|mysql|sqlite> [@comment(...)] {\n  extension <name> ;\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Dialect | `postgresql`, `mysql`, `sqlite` | required (`Unsupported database dialect X`) |\n| `@comment` | literal or `t(\"key\")` | none; becomes `schema.ts` file JSDoc |\n| `extension` | identifier; `pgvector` and `postgis` are recognized | none |\n\n`pgvector`/`postgis` require PostgreSQL (`pgvector and postgis require PostgreSQL`). A `Vector` field needs PostgreSQL + declared `extension pgvector` + `@extension(pgvector)`. One dialect per model; multiple databases mean multiple projects.\n\n## mode and integration\n\n```text\nmode standalone | integration ;\n\nintegration {\n  apiBase \"<absolute-http-url-or-/path>\" ;\n  auth none | bearer | cookie | portal ;\n  auth cookie { csrfCookie \"<name>\" ; csrfHeader \"<header>\" ; } ;\n  response { data \"<path>\" ; total \"<path>\" ; error \"<path>\" ; } ;\n  pagination page | offset | none ;\n  tenant { header \"<header>\" ; identity \"<identity-key>\" ; } ;\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `apiBase` | absolute http(s) URL or a path starting with `/` | required |\n| `auth` | `none`, `bearer`, `cookie`, `portal` | `none` |\n| CSRF | only inside `auth cookie` | none |\n| `response.*` | dotted JSON key paths (`items`, `meta.count`) | `data`, no total, `error` |\n| `pagination` | `page`, `offset`, `none` | `page` |\n| `tenant` | header + identity key, both required | none |\n\nRules: `mode integration` needs an `integration` block and vice versa; duplicate keys fail (`Duplicate integration setting X`); `$.items` is rejected (`dotted JSON path`). Integration mode **rejects** `api { cors }`, `auth`, `scope`, `restrict`, `workflow`, `dataflow`, `permission`, `storage`, `elysia`, `env` and `realtime`, and cannot be generated by `create`/`generate` - mount it with `qiy init`. Full contract: [workspace-integration.md](workspace-integration.md).\n\n## workspace\n\n```text\nworkspace {\n  name <identifier> ;\n  aliases { server <identifier>; web <identifier>; deploy <identifier>; }\n  packages { server \"<package-name>\"; web \"<package-name>\"; }\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Default |\n| --- | --- |\n| `name` | application name |\n| `aliases.server` / `.web` / `.deploy` | `<name>-server`, `<name>-web`, `<name>` |\n| `packages.server` / `.web` | derived from the workspace name |\n\nOnly `name`/`aliases`/`packages` and their sub-keys are allowed; duplicates and invalid identifiers fail. Aliases affect `qiy init` only; `create`/`generate` still use `apps/server`/`apps/web`. `-n` overrides the name once.\n\n## ui\n\n```text\nui {\n  library antd;\n  theme <blue|purple|green|orange|red>;\n  themes <key> [, <key>]*;\n  colorMode <light|dark|system>;\n  allowThemeSwitch <true|false>;\n  allowColorModeSwitch <true|false>;\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `library` | `antd` only | `antd` |\n| `theme` | five keys | first of `themes`, else `blue` |\n| `themes` | comma list, >= 1 | all five |\n| `colorMode` | `light`, `dark`, `system` | `system` |\n| switches | boolean | `true` |\n\n`mui`/`mantine`/`chakra` fail (`only antd is implemented`). `theme` must be in `themes`; duplicate/empty keys fail. Behavior: [ui-charts-i18n.md](ui-charts-i18n.md).\n\n## api\n\n```text\napi {\n  client <rest|graphql> ;\n  cors { origin \"<exact-origin>\" ; ... }\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Values | Default | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `client` | `rest`, `graphql` | `rest` | Web DataProvider transport; server always exposes both REST and `/graphql` |\n| `cors.origin` | exact `http(s)://host[:port]`, repeated | none | `QIY_CORS_ORIGINS` + server CORS middleware |\n\n`client` must be written before `cors`. REST prefix is fixed at `/api/v1`, GraphQL at `/graphql`; there is no `basePath`. Origins must be quoted (`CORS origins must be quoted strings`), without wildcards/paths/userinfo (`CORS origin must be an exact http(s) origin without a path or wildcard`), at least one (`CORS configuration requires at least one origin`).\n\n## features\n\n```text\nfeatures {\n  overview <true|false> ;\n  apiDocs <true|false> ;\n  apiKeys <true|false> ;\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Default | Generates |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `overview` | `true` | `/system/overview` + menu entry, only when `apiDocs`/`apiKeys` is on |\n| `apiDocs` | `false` | `/system/api-docs` + `/api/v1/openapi.json` + `/api/v1/docs/model` |\n| `apiKeys` | `false` | `/system/api-keys` + `qiy_api_keys` + `/api/v1/auth/api-keys` + key auth |\n\n`apiKeys` requires `auth` (parse) and the auth user entity (generation). Details, filtering and key lifecycle: [system-features.md](system-features.md).\n\n## realtime\n\n```text\nrealtime {\n  mode <auto|manual> ;\n  resource <tableName> {\n    events <created|updated|deleted> [, ...] ;\n    roles <admin|operator|viewer> [, ...] ;\n    when <field> claim <claim> ;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `mode` | `auto`, `manual` | `auto` |\n| `resource` | entity/table name, unique | required (>=1) |\n| `events` | >=1 of the three, unique | required |\n| `roles` | >=1 of the three, unique | required |\n| `when` | field (Text/Integer, non-null) + claim | none |\n\nRealtime requires generated `auth`, is rejected in integration mode, and cannot combine a `restrict` row predicate with `when ... claim` on the same resource. Full semantics: [storage-realtime.md](storage-realtime.md).\n\n## elysia\n\n```text\nelysia {\n  bearer;\n  serverTiming;\n  html;\n  drizzle;\n  jwt { name <identifier>; secretEnv <identifier>; }\n  static { assets <string>; prefix <string>; }\n  graphqlAdapter adapter <native|yoga|apollo>;\n  cron { job <name> pattern \"<5-or-6-field cron>\" task cleanupMissingAttachments; }\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `bearer`/`serverTiming`/`html`/`drizzle` | switch | off |\n| `jwt` | bare or `{ name, secretEnv }` | `jwt`, `QIY_JWT_SECRET` |\n| `static` | bare or `{ assets, prefix }` | `public`, `/public` |\n| `graphqlAdapter` | `native`, `yoga`, `apollo` | `native` |\n| `cron` | jobs, only `cleanupMissingAttachments` | none; `QIY_CRON_ENABLED=0` by default |\n\nStatic `prefix` must start with `/`, `assets` must be `public` or a subdirectory, and the prefix must be outside `/api`, `/graphql`, `/assets`. Cron patterns need 5 or 6 fields and unique job names. CORS belongs in `api { cors }`, not here.\n\n## storage\n\n```text\nstorage { provider local | s3 ; }\n```\n\n| Key | Values | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `provider` | `local`, `s3` | `local` |\n\nAliases and endpoints: [storage-realtime.md](storage-realtime.md).\n\n## auth\n\n```text\nauth {\n  provider <provider-id> ;\n  providers <provider-id> [, <provider-id>]* ;\n  provider <provider-id> { subjectField <user-field>; claim <plain-claim-name>; }\n  user <entity> ;\n  subjectField <user-field> ;\n  roleField <user-field> ;\n  usernameField <user-field> ;\n  passwordField <user-field> ;\n  profileField <user-field> ;\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Values | Required |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `provider` | `local`, `otp`, `oidc`, `oauth2`, `sso`, `okta`, `auth0`, `azure-ad-b2c`, `keycloak`, `google`, `kinde` | one of `provider`/`providers` |\n| `providers` | comma list (may include `local`, never `otp`) | one of the two |\n| `user` | declared entity | yes |\n| `subjectField` | required unique Text | OAuth family |\n| `roleField` | enum with exactly admin/operator/viewer | yes |\n| `usernameField` | required unique Text | `local`/`otp` |\n| `passwordField` | nullable Text | `local` |\n| `profileField` | nullable Text | optional, OAuth only |\n| mapping `subjectField` | nullable unique Text | hybrid/multi |\n| mapping `claim` | plain identifier | optional, default `sub` |\n\n`provider` and `providers` are mutually exclusive; provider mappings must name configured providers. Sessions, onboarding, bind/unbind, env vars and security notes: [auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md).\n\n## env\n\n```text\nenv {\n  variable <UPPER_NAME> {\n    secret;\n    development <\"literal\" | required | generate> ;\n    production  <\"literal\" | required> ;\n    example     <\"literal\" | required> ;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Name | `^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$` |\n| `secret;` | No literal values allowed |\n| `generate` | Only for a secret `development` value |\n| Output | Server gets non-`VITE_` variables; web gets `VITE_` only |\n| `VITE_` | Bundled into client code; cannot be secret |\n| Credential-like names | `SECRET`/`TOKEN`/`PASSWORD`/`API_KEY`/`ACCESS_KEY` must be marked `secret` |\n\n`--sync`/`init` merge new variables into existing files and preserve current values.\n\n## messages\n\n```text\nmessages {\n  default \"<locale>\";\n  locale \"<locale>\" {\n    \"<key>\" \"<value>\";\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| `default` | First in the block, canonical BCP 47, matching `locale` block must exist |\n| `locale` | Unique canonical tags |\n| key | `^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9.-]*$`, no prototype-polluting segments |\n| value | Any string with `{{name}}` interpolation / plural suffixes |\n\n`@comment(t(\"key\"))`, `@label(t(\"key\"))`, `@confirm(t(\"key\"))`, `@error(t(\"key\"))` require the key in the default locale. Full rules: [ui-charts-i18n.md](ui-charts-i18n.md).\n\n## permission\n\n```text\npermission field <Name> \"<value>\" [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] ;\npermission group <Name> [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] { A, B } [;]\npermission group <Name> [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] = A & B ;\npermission from database field <entity>.<field> ;\npermission from claim <provider> \"<claim>\" ;\npermission verification <Name> [@label(...)] [@comment(...)] {\n  input { field <name> Text|Array<String>; }\n  return <expression> ;\n}\n```\n\nRequires generated `auth` and at least one `permission field`. `&` means **union**. Verification grammar, sources, endpoints and command `allow`: [auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md).\n\n## workflow\n\n```text\nworkflow orderInventory ;\n```\n\nOnly `orderInventory`, PostgreSQL only, requires fixed `orders`/`orderItems`/`inventoryItems` contracts, and fails with `restrict` row policy. See [dataflows-actions.md](dataflows-actions.md).\n\n## enum\n\n```text\nenum <Name> [@comment(\"...\" | t(\"key\"))] {\n  value <valueName> [label \"...\"] [color <color>] [icon <IconName>] [@comment(...)] ;\n}\n```\n\nValue `label`/`color`/`icon` take **no `@`**; only `@comment` does. Values must be non-empty; names unique; enums before entities. `color` is passed to Ant Design `Tag`; `icon` must match `^[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*Outlined$`. Only `@comment` is allowed on enums/values (`Enum X: unsupported annotation @Y`).\n\n## entity and field\n\n```text\nentity <Name> [table <tableName>] [@annotation(...)]... {\n  field <name> <Type>[(<params>)] [@attribute[(<value>)]...] ;\n  index <name> <method>(<field> [<opclass>], ...) [@unique] [@concurrently] [@comment(...)] ;\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Entity name | identifier, not a JS reserved word | required |\n| `table` | `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$`, becomes route `/<table>` | entity name |\n| Block content | only `field`/`index`; at least one field | required |\n| Primary key | exactly one `field id UUID @id` | required |\n| Entity annotations | `@label`, `@icon`, `@comment`, `@singular`, `@plural`, `@display`, `@tableDisplay`, `@relationDetail` | all optional |\n\nField types (closed set):\n\n| Type | PostgreSQL | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `UUID` | `uuid` | PK/FK |\n| `Text` | `text` | strings, enum storage |\n| `Integer` | `integer` | 32-bit |\n| `Decimal(p[,s])` / `Money(p[,s])` | `numeric(p,s)` | precision required |\n| `Date` / `Time` / `DateTime` | `date` / `time` / `timestamptz` | `YYYY-MM-DD` / `HH:mm:ss` / ISO |\n| `File` / `Files` | `text` / `jsonb` | storage key(s) |\n| `Vector(n)` | `vector(n)` | PostgreSQL + pgvector |\n| `<enumName>` | `text` | declared enum |\n\nUnknown types (`String`, `Boolean`, `Json`, ...) fail. Parameters only on `Vector`/`Decimal`/`Money` (`Field type Text has no parameters`). Field attributes: `@id`, `@nullable`, `@unique`, `@label`, `@comment`, `@icon`, `@visible`, `@listVisible`, `@formVisible`, `@showVisible`, `@sortable`, `@filterable`, `@filter(...)`, `@upload(...)`, `@maxBytes`, `@maxFiles`, `@mime`, `@extension`, `@code`, `@generated(uuid)`, `@column`, `@dimension`, `@precision`, `@scale`. There is no `@required`, `@default`, `@length`, `@computed`. Full matrices: [modeling-and-generation.md](modeling-and-generation.md).\n\n## relation and index\n\n```text\nrelation <name> <fromEntity> <fromField> <toEntity> <toField> <one|many>\n         [@onDelete(<restrict|cascade|setNull>)]\n         [@comment(\"...\")] ;\n\nindex <name> <btree|hnsw|ivfflat> ( <field> [<opclass>] [, ...] )\n      [@unique] [@concurrently] [@comment(\"...\")] ;\n```\n\nRelation rules: only `one` (writing `many` parses but fails IR validation); both endpoints must be `UUID`; target must be primary or `@unique`; source cannot be `@code`/`@generated`; `setNull` requires `@nullable`; single-column only; self relations allowed; relations come after all entities. Index rules: name globally unique; `hnsw`/`ivfflat` require PostgreSQL + pgvector, one `Vector` column, an opclass from `vector_l2_ops`/`vector_ip_ops`/`vector_cosine_ops`, dimension <= 2000; `@concurrently` is PostgreSQL only. Details: [modeling-and-generation.md](modeling-and-generation.md).\n\n## scope, restrict, pages\n\n```text\nscope <resource> <field> claim <claim> [ tree <treeEntity> <parentField> ] ;\n```\n\n`field` must be `UUID`/`Text`; claim matches `^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_.-]*$`; one per resource; `tree` types must match; local/hybrid sessions need a matching users column.\n\n```text\nrestrict <resource> {\n  allow roles <role> [, <role>]* ;\n  when <field> claim <claim> ;\n  when <field> ==|!= \"<value>\" [, \"<value>\"] ;\n  when <field> in|notIn \"<value>\" [, \"<value>\"] ;\n  when ( <condition> or <condition> ) ;\n  when <boolean-expression> ;\n  mask <field> [roles <r>, ...] [claim <present|absent> <claim>] mode <omit|null|redact> [replacement \"<text>\"] ;\n}\n```\n\nOnly `one` per resource; `when` leaves are claim comparisons, literals (`==`/`!=` single value), sets (`in`/`notIn`, max 64), cross-field comparisons (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `==`, `!=`; UUID only equality), the `scope` atom, and `not`/`and`/`or`/parentheses. Mask targets cannot be primary keys or `Vector`. A resource with any `restrict` block cannot be used by a dataflow.\n\n```text\npages <resource> {\n  list|show|create|edit|delete roles <role> [, <role>]* ;\n  field <fieldName> roles <role> [, <role>]* ;\n}\n```\n\nAt least one action or field rule; actions at most once; roles non-empty. `field ... roles` is UI-only; use `restrict mask` to hide data. Full policy semantics: [auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md).\n\n## menu\n\n```text\nmenu {\n  group <name>\n    [@label(\"...\")] [@icon(IconName)] [@parent(<group>)] [@comment(\"...\")] {\n    resource <tableName>;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAt most one `menu` block; groups unique; `resource` is the entity table name and may appear once across all groups; `@parent` must exist and be acyclic. Ungrouped resources append at root. Details: [ui-charts-i18n.md](ui-charts-i18n.md).\n\n## dashboard\n\n```text\ndashboard {\n  metric <name> <resource>\n    [@label(\"...\")] [@icon(IconName)] [@span(8|12|24)]\n    [@type(<count|distribution|trend|aggregate>)]\n    [@groupBy(<field>)] [@days(<1..365>)]\n    [@field(<field>)] [@agg(<sum|avg|min|max>)]\n    [@comment(\"...\" | t(\"key\"))]\n    ;\n}\n```\n\n| Type | Requirement |\n| --- | --- |\n| `count` | none |\n| `distribution` | enum `@groupBy` |\n| `trend` | `DateTime` `@groupBy`, optional `@days` 1..365 |\n| `aggregate` | numeric `@field` + `@agg` |\n\n`@span` is 8/12/24; `@field`/`@agg` only on aggregate; `@days` only on trend. `chart` takes precedence on the home page.\n\n## chart and chart panels\n\n```text\nchart [const|pie|bar|line|table] <ChartName> {\n  icon  = \"<IconName>\" ;\n  title = \"<text>\" ;\n  data  = <data expression> ;\n  labels = <enumField> ;\n  labels [=] { <value> \"<text>\" ; ... } ;\n}\n\nchart panels <PanelName> {\n  title = \"<text>\" ;\n  grid <cols> <rows> ;\n  <ChartName> { <variant> <x> <y> <w> <h> ; ... }\n}\n```\n\nData expressions: `count <entity>` (const), `sum|avg|min|max <entity>.<field>` (const), `count <entity> group by <enumField>` (pie/bar), `trend <entity>.<DateTimeField> days <1..365>` (line), `list <entity> columns <a>, <b>` (table). Same-name declarations with different kinds are multiple views of one card (first is default). `grid cols` 1..24, `rows` 1..200; variants `larger`/`medium`/`small` (aliases `large`/`lg`/`xl`, `md`, `sm`/`xs`) with `x+w<=cols`, `y+h<=rows`. Full grammar, labels and limits: [ui-charts-i18n.md](ui-charts-i18n.md).\n\n## dataflow\n\n```text\ndataflow <Name> ( \"@label\" \"(\" doc \")\" | \"@confirm\" \"(\" doc \")\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* {\n  allow roles ... | allow permission ... | allow verification ... ;\n  idempotency required ;\n  audit \"<action>\" ;\n  input { field <name> <type> ( \"@required\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* ; }\n  context { <binding> = entity <Entity> by <pk> input.<field> @required ; }\n  step <Name> ( \"@order\" \"(\" <int> \")\" | \"@comment\" \"(\" doc \")\" )* { <statement>* }\n  result { return <binding> ; }\n}\n```\n\n`input`, `context`, `result` blocks are required (empty `{}` allowed for the first two) and at least one `step` is required. Statements: `require ... @error(...)`, `update <binding> { field = value; }`, `create <binding> = entity <E> { ... }`, `delete <binding>`, `emit \"event\" { ... }`, `call <adapter> { ... }`. Full contracts, batch and tests: [dataflows-actions.md](dataflows-actions.md).\n\n## action\n\n```text\naction <Name> {\n  resource <entity> ;\n  ( dataflow <Name> | navigate \"<path>\" ) ;\n  placement ( list | show ) [, ...] ;\n  [ label doc ; ]\n  [ confirm doc ; ]\n  [ when <field> ( == | != ) \"<value>\" ; ]\n  [ allow roles ... | permission ... | verification ... ; ]\n  [ batch true ; ]\n  [ page manual @comment(doc) ; ]\n}\n```\n\n`resource`, `placement` and exactly one of `dataflow`/`navigate` are required. `navigate` needs an absolute route containing `:id` plus `page manual @comment(...)`. `when` accepts one Text/enum field and a quoted value. Batch requires list-only placement, no `when`, an idempotent flow and a single required UUID input. Full details: [dataflows-actions.md](dataflows-actions.md).\n\n## Annotation inventory\n\n42 annotation names exist; the same name means different things by placement. Unknown annotations fail (`Unsupported ... attribute @X`); unimplemented annotations are never silently ignored.\n\n| Placement | Annotations |\n| --- | --- |\n| Documentation | `@comment(...)` (application, database, enum, enum value, entity, field, index, relation, menu group, metric, permission field/group/verification, dataflow and its input/context/step, action page manual), `@label(...)` (entity, field, menu group, metric, permission field/group/verification, dataflow), `@icon(...)` (entity, field, menu group, metric), `@confirm(...)` (dataflow), `@error(...)` (require) |\n| Entity | `@label`, `@icon`, `@comment`, `@singular`, `@plural`, `@display`, `@tableDisplay`, `@relationDetail` |\n| Field | `@id`, `@nullable`, `@unique`, `@label`, `@comment`, `@icon`, `@visible`, `@listVisible`, `@formVisible`, `@showVisible`, `@sortable`, `@filterable`, `@filter(...)`, `@upload(...)`, `@maxBytes`, `@maxFiles`, `@mime`, `@extension`, `@code`, `@generated`, `@column`, `@dimension`, `@precision`, `@scale` |\n| Index | `@unique`, `@concurrently`, `@comment` |\n| Relation | `@onDelete(...)`, `@comment` |\n| Menu group | `@label`, `@icon`, `@parent`, `@comment` |\n| Dashboard metric | `@label`, `@icon`, `@span`, `@type`, `@groupBy`, `@days`, `@field`, `@agg`, `@comment` |\n| Permission / dataflow / action | `@label`, `@comment`, `@confirm`, `@required`, `@order`, `@error` |\n\nParameter forms: `documentation` accepts a literal or `t(\"key\")`; `string` accepts a quoted string or bare identifier; `integer` is a non-negative decimal; boolean is `@x` (= true) or `@x(true|false)` - not all booleans allow omitting parentheses; identifiers are enumeration values. Duplicates usually overwrite silently; explicitly rejected duplicates: `@singular`, `@plural`, `@display`, `@tableDisplay`, `@relationDetail`, `@code`, `@generated`, `@filter` (same operator), `@mime` (same type), `@comment` on definition-site blocks, `@order` (via step uniqueness).\n\nCommon miswrites: field `@required` (use `@nullable` for optional), `@optional`, `@default(...)`, `@searchable`/`@hidden`/`@readonly`, field/entity `@order(...)`, `@length`/`@min`/`@max`/`@format`, `@enum`/`@relation`/`@index`, enum `@label`, field `@plural`, `@transient`/`@computed`, `@primaryKey`.\n\n## Generated values\n\n| Annotation / shape | Applies to | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `@code(\"template\")` | Text, non-enum, non-PK | Server-rendered business code |\n| `@generated(uuid)` / `@generated` | UUID, non-PK | Server UUIDv4 |\n| Non-PK `UUID` with no relation | UUID | Treated as a system reference: random UUID, hidden in forms |\n| `field id UUID @id` | UUID | Always server-generated |\n| FK source with a relation | UUID | User-selected, never generated |\n\nTemplate tokens: `{uuid}`, date/time parts (`{YYYY}` `{YY}` `{MM}` `{DD}` `{HH}` `{mm}` `{ss}` `{SSS}` and concatenations), `{seq}`/`{seq:N}`, `{count+1}`, `{random:N}`, `{random:N:charset}`, `{{`/`}}`. A template must be non-empty, <= 512 chars, contain at least one token and a uniqueness token. Sequences persist per `(entity, field, date-time bucket)` in `qiy_code_sequences`; conflict retries use `QIY_GENERATED_ATTEMPTS` (5) then 409 `generated.conflict`. Details: [modeling-and-generation.md](modeling-and-generation.md).\n\n## Display templates\n\n```text\nplain text              escaped, output as-is\n{$.fieldName}           interpolation (UUID, Text, enum, Integer, Decimal, Money, Date, Time, DateTime)\n<b>{$.name}</b></br>    whitelisted tags: br b strong i em span small p div\n```\n\nNo fallback is generated when `@display` is absent unless one of `name` -> `title` -> `displayName` -> `code` -> `number` -> `sku` -> `email` -> `label` -> `inventoryKey` exists (first match becomes `{$.field}`). `@tableDisplay` defaults to `@display`; `@relationDetail` defaults to `@display`. Rejected: empty template, malformed placeholder, unknown field, `File`/`Files`/`Vector`, FK source fields, non-whitelisted/uppercase tags, self-closing tags other than `br`, unpaired tags, attributes.\n\n## i18n keys\n\nKeys derive from identifiers (never label text). `<resource>` is the **table** name.\n\n| Key | Covers |\n| --- | --- |\n| `qiy.resources.<table>.label` / `.singular` / `.plural` | Resource name/titles |\n| `qiy.resources.<table>.fields.<field>.label` | Column/detail/form/filter labels |\n| `qiy.enums.<enum>.label` / `.values.<value>` | Enum descriptions and Tags |\n| `qiy.menu.<group>.label` | Sidebar group |\n| `qiy.dashboard.<metric>.label` | Legacy metric card |\n| `qiy.charts.<chart>.label`, `.views.<kind>.label`, `.labels.<value>`, `qiy.charts.<panel>.label` | Charts |\n| `qiy.actions.<action>.label` / `.confirm` / `.inputs.<input>.label` | Command buttons/forms |\n| `qiy.dataflows.<dataflow>.label` | Overview dataflow name |\n\n`<resource>` uses the entity's **table** name, so `entity Product table products` produces `qiy.resources.products.*`. See [ui-charts-i18n.md](ui-charts-i18n.md) for chrome keys, fallback order and locale rules.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Error (stage) | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Unexpected Qiy syntax at offset N` (lexer) | Unquoted non-ASCII, `:`, `[`, `/`, `*`, `$` | Quote the value; use only supported symbols |\n| `Expected database near token N` | `database` not first in `application` | Move it first |\n| `Expected <block> near token N` | Block order wrong | Reorder per [Declaration order](#declaration-order) |\n| `Expected <end> near token N` | Content after `}` or missing `application` `}` | Check braces |\n| `Expected ; near token N` | Missing semicolon, or a `;` after a block `}` | Add/remove the semicolon |\n| `Unsupported field type X` | Not a closed-set type | Use `Text`/`Integer`/enum/... |\n| `Unsupported field attribute @X` | Wrong placement or typo | Check the annotation inventory |\n| `duplicate ... annotation` | Same annotation twice | Keep one |\n| `Missing default locale message for <purpose>: key` | `messages` after the referencing declaration, or missing key | Move `messages` earlier; add the key |\n| `Unsupported database dialect X` | Typo | `postgresql`/`mysql`/`sqlite` |\n| `Invalid Ant Design icon X` | Not `*Outlined` | Use an Ant Design icon name |\n| `V0 CRUD requires exactly one UUID primary key named id` | Missing/renamed PK | `field id UUID @id` |\n| `route path must be lowercase and URL-safe` | Bad `table` name | `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$` |\n| `required field cannot be hidden from the create form` | Required field hidden | Add `@nullable` or show it |\n| `Auth: ...` (generation) | User table columns violate the contract | See [auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md) |\n| `Scope ...` / `Restrict ...` (generation) | Missing resource/field | See [auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md) |\n| `Output directory must be empty` | Target non-empty without `--sync` | Clear it or use `--sync` |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Modeling and generation](modeling-and-generation.md) - includes, fields, relations, indexes, generated codes, limits\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - auth modes, permission/verification/restrict/scope/pages\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - commands, actions, workflows, scenario tests\n- [UI, charts and i18n](ui-charts-i18n.md) - ui, menu, dashboard, charts, messages\n- [System features](system-features.md) - features, OpenAPI, API keys\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - storage and realtime\n- [CLI workflows](cli-workflows.md) - commands, flags, layout, upgrade\n- [Workspace integration](workspace-integration.md) - init, aliases, integration mode\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - scripts, migrations, acceptance\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - cross-area error table\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [DSL overview](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/overview)\n- [application](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/application)\n- [entity and field](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/entity)\n- [relations and indexes](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/relation-index)\n- [annotations](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/annotations)\n- [generated values](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/generated-values)\n- [modules/include](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/modules)\n",
  "references/modeling-and-generation.md": "# Modeling and generation\n\nUse this file when you create or change the data model: entities, fields, types, relations, indexes, generated business codes, display templates, includes/modules, and every \"parses but does not generate\" rule. For the complete block/annotation inventory read [language-reference.md](language-reference.md); for auth, policy, commands, charts and features read the dedicated references listed at the end.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/entity\n\n## Contents\n\n- [What the model generates](#what-the-model-generates)\n- [Smallest correct model](#smallest-correct-model)\n- [Includes and modules](#includes-and-modules)\n- [Entities, tables and primary keys](#entities-tables-and-primary-keys)\n- [Field types](#field-types)\n- [Field attributes](#field-attributes)\n- [Generated values and business codes](#generated-values-and-business-codes)\n- [Display templates](#display-templates)\n- [Filters, visibility and defaults](#filters-visibility-and-defaults)\n- [Relations](#relations)\n- [Indexes](#indexes)\n- [Validation pipeline and modeling limits](#validation-pipeline-and-modeling-limits)\n- [Worked modeling walkthrough](#worked-modeling-walkthrough)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## What the model generates\n\n| Model construct | Generated artifact | Edit policy |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `entity` + `field` | Drizzle table in `apps/server/src/schema.ts`, TypeBox/GraphQL contracts, repository/service, REST + GraphQL resource, Refine list/create/edit/show routes | Owned by `.qiy-generated.json`; regenerate through the model, do not hand-edit |\n| `relation` | FK constraint, `RelationSelect`, batch foreign-key loading, record drawer | Owned |\n| `index` | Drizzle index / migration SQL | Owned |\n| `@code` / `@generated` | `apps/server/src/generated-values.ts` and create paths | Owned |\n| `enum` / `menu` / `dashboard` / `chart` | `resources.ts` metadata, navigation, home page | Owned |\n| Custom behavior | `apps/web/app/extensions/`, `apps/server/src/extensions/` | Not registered in the manifest; `--sync` preserves it |\n\nTreat generated TypeScript as editable for a one-off, but for anything long-lived prefer an unowned extension file: `--sync` rewrites or removes every file listed in `.qiy-generated.json`.\n\n## Smallest correct model\n\n```qiy\nqiy v0;\n\napplication inventory @comment(\"Inventory operations console\") {\n  database sqlite @comment(\"Local inventory records\") {}\n  ui { library antd; theme blue; themes blue, purple, green; colorMode system; }\n  api { client rest; }\n\n  entity products @label(\"Products\") @icon(ShoppingOutlined) {\n    field id UUID @id;\n    field sku Text @unique;\n    field name Text;\n    field active Integer @nullable;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRules that make this valid: `qiy v0;` first; exactly one `application`; `database` is the first declaration inside it; every entity has exactly one UUID primary key named `id`; declarations end in `;` but block braces do not; `api { client ... }` before any `cors` inside the block.\n\n## Includes and modules\n\nSplit a large application into relative fragments. `include` is expanded textually before parsing, so the expanded model must satisfy one global declaration order.\n\n```qiy\nqiy v0;\n\napplication warehouse {\n  database sqlite {}\n\n  include \"modules/messages.qiy\";     # after config blocks, before enums/entities\n  include \"modules/catalog.qiy\";\n  include \"modules/inventory.qiy\";\n  include \"modules/relations.qiy\";    # after all entities\n}\n```\n\n```text\ninclude \"<relative-path>.qiy\" [@messages | @message] ;\n```\n\n| Slot | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Path | Quoted string ending in `.qiy`, relative to the current file's directory. Absolute paths, `..`, empty paths and non-`.qiy` suffixes are rejected. |\n| Selector | `@messages` / `@message` imports only the single top-level `messages` block of the target file. Other selectors are rejected. |\n| Semicolon | Required (`Expected ; after include path`). |\n| Placement | Direct child of `application` (or top level of a fragment). Not inside `entity`, `menu`, `dataflow`, `chart`. |\n\nFragment rules:\n\n- A fragment contains application children only. It must not repeat `qiy v0;` and must not wrap content in `application`.\n- Nested includes resolve relative to the including fragment; expansion is recursive.\n- All files share one namespace: entity, table, enum, relation name, index name (global), menu group, metric, dataflow and action names are checked after expansion.\n- Including the same file twice is not deduplicated; it produces duplicate declarations.\n- Cycles are detected by realpath; symlinks escaping the project root and `..` are rejected.\n- Recommended layout: `app.qiy` holds header + `database` + config + includes + `scope`/`restrict`; `modules/messages.qiy`, `modules/permissions.qiy`, `modules/platform.qiy` (shared enums + users), domain `entities.qiy`, `relations.qiy`, `pages.qiy`, `menu.qiy`, `charts.qiy`, `dataflows.qiy`, `actions.qiy`.\n\nUse `include \"modules/catalog.qiy\" @messages;` when a mixed module also contains entities/enums but the current app only needs its dictionary. The target must contain exactly one top-level `messages` block; dropped content does not enter the model.\n\nFailure examples: `include statements must be direct children of the application or fragment`, `include path cannot contain ..`, `Qiy include cycle detected: a.qiy -> b.qiy -> a.qiy`, `include selector @messages did not find a top-level messages block`, `unsupported include selector @menu.operations`.\n\n## Entities, tables and primary keys\n\n```text\nentity <Name> [table <tableName>] [@annotation(...)]... {\n  field <name> <Type>[(<params>)] [@attribute[(<value>)]...] ;\n  index <name> <method>(<field> [<opclass>], ...) [@unique] [@concurrently] [@comment(...)] ;\n}\n```\n\n| Slot | Rule | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `<Name>` | Identifier `[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9-]*`, not a JavaScript reserved word; used as API/GraphQL resource and permission resource name | Required |\n| `table <tableName>` | Physical table and Web route (`/<tableName>`); must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$` | Same as `<Name>` |\n| Block content | Only `field` and `index` (`Expected field or index`); at least one field | Required |\n| Primary key | Exactly one `field id UUID @id`; other names or types fail generation | Required |\n\nEntity and table names are globally unique (`Entity X: duplicate entity or table name`). A bad route name fails with `X: route path must be lowercase and URL-safe`; a missing/renamed id fails with `X: V0 CRUD requires exactly one UUID primary key named id`.\n\nEntity annotations (order does not matter): `@label`, `@icon` (must match `^[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*Outlined$`), `@comment`, `@singular`, `@plural`, `@display`, `@tableDisplay`, `@relationDetail`. Duplicates of `@singular`/`@plural`/`@display`/`@tableDisplay`/`@relationDetail` are rejected. `@icon` heuristics: `user` -> `UserOutlined`, `order` -> `ShoppingOutlined`, `warehouse` -> `DatabaseOutlined`, otherwise `TableOutlined`.\n\n## Field types\n\nThe type set is closed. Unknown names (including `String`, `Boolean`, `Email`, `Json`) fail with `Unsupported field type X`.\n\n| Syntax | PostgreSQL column | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `UUID` | `uuid` | Primary key (must be `id`) and foreign keys |\n| `Text` | `text` | Strings; enum storage type |\n| `Integer` | `integer` | 32-bit |\n| `Decimal(p[, s])` | `numeric(p, s)` | Precision required; scale defaults `0` |\n| `Money(p[, s])` | `numeric(p, s)` | Same as Decimal, money semantics |\n| `Date` | `date` (string mode) | Transports `YYYY-MM-DD` |\n| `Time` | `time` | Transports `HH:mm[:ss]`, normalized to `HH:mm:ss` |\n| `DateTime` | `timestamp with time zone` | Transports ISO date-time |\n| `File` | `text` (storage key) | One protected file |\n| `Files` | `jsonb` (string array) | Multiple storage keys |\n| `Vector(n)` | `vector(n)` | Requires PostgreSQL + `extension pgvector` + `@extension(pgvector)` |\n| `<enumName>` | `text` | Declared enum; rendered as Tag |\n\nType parameters and validation:\n\n- `Vector(1536)` or `@dimension(1536)`: dimension must be a positive integer, column max 16000, vector index max 2000.\n- `Decimal`/`Money` accept `(precision)` or `(precision, scale)`, or `@precision`/`@scale`. Precision > 0 (MySQL <= 65, PostgreSQL <= 1000); `0 <= scale <= precision` (MySQL scale <= 30).\n- Parentheses on any other type fail: `Field type Text has no parameters`.\n- Enum fields take no parameters and cannot carry `@code`.\n- `Files` cannot be a primary key or `@unique`.\n- Field names are globally unique; physical column names (`@column`) must be unique (`duplicate column name`).\n\nDate/time behavior: invalid values such as `2026-02-31` or `25:61:00` return **400** naming the field. Forms use `DatePicker`, `TimePicker`, `DatePicker showTime`; lists and display templates localize with `Intl.DateTimeFormat`. Only `DateTime` can drive a dashboard `trend` group-by. Sorting is string comparison (ISO shapes sort correctly).\n\n## Field attributes\n\nAttributes follow the type, any order, and booleans accept `@x` or `@x(false)`.\n\n| Attribute | Types | Default | Effect / error |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `@id` | UUID | none | `.primaryKey()`; server-generated; hidden in forms. Exactly one per entity |\n| `@nullable` | all | not null | Nullable column, request field optional. Required for `setNull` relations |\n| `@unique` | all except `Files` | false | Unique constraint; usable as relation target. `Files cannot be unique` |\n| `@label(\"...\")` | all | field name | Column/form/filter label; derives `qiy.resources.<table>.fields.<field>.label` |\n| `@comment(\"...\" / t(\"key\"))` | all | none | Schema JSDoc + metadata; missing default-locale key fails |\n| `@icon(Icon)` | all | none | Field metadata; must be `*Outlined` |\n| `@visible(bool)` | all | `!primaryKey && type !== Vector` | Default for the three visibility flags |\n| `@listVisible(bool)` | all | `@visible` | Default list column |\n| `@formVisible(bool)` | all | `@visible` | Form rendering; hiding a required field fails generation |\n| `@showVisible(bool)` | all | `@visible` | Detail/drawer rendering |\n| `@sortable(bool)` | all | `true` (`Files` false) | Server rejects other sort fields with 400 `Unsupported sort field` |\n| `@filterable(bool)` | all | `true` (`Files` false) | Server rejects other filter fields with 400 `Unsupported filter field` |\n| `@filter(mode, ...)` | all | by type | Restricts operators: `eq, contains, startsWith, endsWith, gt, gte, lt, lte, between, in` |\n| `@upload(binary\\|base64\\|both)` | File/Files | `binary` | Upload channel |\n| `@maxBytes(n)` | File/Files | `26214400` | 1..104857600 |\n| `@maxFiles(n)` | File/Files | `1` for `File`, `6` for `Files` | `File` only 1; `Files` 1..20 |\n| `@mime(\"a/b\", ...)` | File/Files | `[\"*/*\"]` | Mergeable whitelist |\n| `@extension(name)` | Vector | none | DB extension already declared in `database` |\n| `@code(\"template\")` | Text, non-enum, non-PK | none | Server-rendered business code (see below) |\n| `@generated(uuid)` | UUID, non-PK | none | Server UUIDv4 |\n| `@column(\"name\")` | all | field name | Physical column name |\n| `@dimension/@precision/@scale` | Vector / Decimal / Money | type parameter | Alternative spelling |\n\nThere is no `@required`, no `@default`, no `@length`/`@min`/`@max`/`@format`, no `@searchable`/`@hidden`/`@readonly`, no `@computed`/`@transient`. Required is the default; use `@nullable` for optional. Defaults and business validation belong in migrations, seeds or server extensions.\n\n## Generated values and business codes\n\n```qiy\nentity orgs @label(\"Organizations\") {\n  field id UUID @id;\n  field code Text @unique @code(\"ORG-{YYYY}{MM}-{seq:4}\");\n  field name Text;\n  field parentId UUID @nullable;\n  field externalId UUID @nullable @generated(uuid);\n}\n\nrelation orgParent orgs parentId orgs id one @onDelete(setNull);\n```\n\n| Annotation / shape | Type | When | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `@code(\"template\")` | `Text`, non-enum, non-PK | Server create | Renders a business code |\n| `@generated(uuid)` / `@generated` | `UUID`, non-PK | Server create | UUIDv4 |\n| Non-PK `UUID` with **no** relation | `UUID` | Server create | Treated as a system reference: random UUID, hidden in forms |\n| `field id UUID @id` | `UUID` | Server create | Always generated |\n| FK source field with a relation | `UUID` | User choice | Never auto-generated |\n\n**Declare a relation for every real foreign key.** Without one, a UUID field is filled with a random UUID and the form cannot select a target. Conversely, a FK source cannot be `@code` or `@generated`.\n\nTemplate tokens (all validated at parse/generation time):\n\n| Token | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `{uuid}` | Random UUIDv4 |\n| `{YYYY}`, `{YY}`, `{MM}`, `{DD}`, `{HH}`, `{mm}`, `{ss}`, `{SSS}` | Date/time parts, rendered in `QIY_CODE_TIMEZONE` (default `UTC`) |\n| `{YYYYMMDD}`, `{YYYY}{MM}` etc. | Any ordered concatenation; the parser splits by fixed widths |\n| `{seq}` / `{seq:4}` | Sequence, width 1..12, zero-padded |\n| `{count+1}` / `{count+1:4}` | Legacy alias of `{seq}` |\n| `{$.seq}` / `{$.count+1}` | Legacy alias |\n| `{random:10}` | Random string from `a-zA-Z0-9`, length 1..256 |\n| `{random:8:A-F0-9}` | Random with an explicit ASCII alphanumeric charset |\n| `{random a-z/A-Z/0-9 length 10}` | Natural spelling of the same |\n| `{{` / `}}` | Literal braces |\n\n- The pattern must be non-empty, <= 512 chars, contain at least one token, and contain a uniqueness token (`seq`, `count+1`, `random`, `uuid`).\n- The bucket is the concatenation of rendered date/time tokens. Sequences are persisted per `(entity, field, bucket)` in `qiy_code_sequences`; `PO-{YYYYMMDD}-{seq:4}` resets daily.\n- Two `{seq}` tokens in one template share the same allocated number, padded per width; multiple `@code` fields keep separate counters.\n- Generated values are rendered only on the server. Client input is stripped (`qiyStripGeneratedValues`); PATCH/GraphQL update strips generated fields and returns the record unchanged when the patch becomes empty.\n- Unique-conflict retries: 5 (`QIY_GENERATED_ATTEMPTS`), then HTTP **409** `{ errorKey: \"generated.conflict\" }` - not 500.\n- PostgreSQL/SQLite allocate atomically (`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE ... RETURNING`); MySQL uses `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` inside the transaction.\n- Seeds, migrations, raw SQL and Dataflow `create` bypass `@code`; a Dataflow `create` must supply non-null generated fields explicitly.\n- Frontend: generated fields are not rendered in create forms (read-only `qiy.autoGenerated` hint), shown disabled when editing, visible in list/detail. `autoGenerated: true` in `resources.ts`; `@formVisible(true)` cannot override it.\n\n## Display templates\n\n`@display`, `@tableDisplay` and `@relationDetail` share one tiny template language:\n\n```text\nplain text                 escaped, output as-is\n{$.fieldName}              interpolation: UUID, Text, enum, Integer, Decimal, Money, Date, Time, DateTime\n<b>{$.name}</b></br>...    whitelisted tags: br b strong i em span small p div\n```\n\nFallback chain: without `@display`, the first readable field named `name` -> `title` -> `displayName` -> `code` -> `number` -> `sku` -> `email` -> `label` -> `inventoryKey` becomes `{$.<field>}`. `File`, `Files` and `Vector` never participate. `@tableDisplay` defaults to `@display`; `@relationDetail` defaults to `@display`; the three are independent.\n\nRejected: empty template, malformed placeholder (must be exactly `{$.field}`), unknown field, interpolating `File`/`Files`/`Vector`, interpolating a foreign-key source field (`cannot interpolate foreign key field X`), non-whitelisted or uppercase tags, self-closing tags other than `br`, unpaired/stray tags, attributes/events. Text and values are HTML-escaped; enum values use the current language; dates use `Intl.DateTimeFormat`; `<br>`, `<br/>`, `</br>` all normalize to one newline.\n\n## Filters, visibility and defaults\n\n```qiy\nentity products {\n  field id UUID @id;\n  field name Text @filter(contains, startsWith, endsWith, eq);\n  field amount Integer @filter(eq, gte, lte, between, in);\n  field createdAt DateTime @filter(gte, lte, between);\n  field status productStatus;        // enum: only eq by default\n  field attachment Files @nullable;  // not sortable/filterable by default\n}\n```\n\n| Operator | Semantics | Input |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `eq`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte` | equality/comparison | single value |\n| `contains`, `startsWith`, `endsWith` | text matching | single value |\n| `between` | inclusive range | two comma-separated values |\n| `in` | set | comma-separated values |\n\nDefault operator sets: `@filter(...)` -> enum `[\"eq\"]` -> Text `[\"contains\",\"startsWith\",\"endsWith\",\"eq\"]` -> other `[\"eq\",\"gt\",\"gte\",\"lt\",\"lte\",\"between\",\"in\"]`.\n\n- Server-side whitelists reject undeclared fields/operators with **400** `Unsupported filter field` / `Unsupported filter operator`.\n- REST preserves nested `and`/`or` groups: max **8 levels**, **50 leaves**. GraphQL uses a flat `QiyFilterInput` (top-level AND).\n- Visibility: primary keys and `Vector` are hidden in list/form/show by default; `File`/`Files` are visible. List columns are all `listVisible` fields in declaration order; the column picker persists to `localStorage`. Field order is declaration order everywhere (schema, forms, detail, list, CSV); there is no `@order`.\n\n## Relations\n\n```text\nrelation <name> <fromEntity> <fromField> <toEntity> <toField> <one|many>\n         [@onDelete(<restrict|cascade|setNull>)]\n         [@comment(\"...\")] ;\n```\n\n```qiy\nrelation orderCustomer orders customerId customers id one @onDelete(restrict);\nrelation lineOrder orderItems orderId orders id one @onDelete(cascade);\nrelation orgParent orgs parentId orgs id one @onDelete(setNull);\n```\n\n| Slot | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Name | Globally unique (`Relation X: invalid or duplicate name`) |\n| Source | Declared entity + its `UUID` field; one relation per source field (`duplicate source field X.Y`) |\n| Target | Declared entity + primary key or `@unique` field (`target field must be primary or unique`) |\n| Cardinality | Only `one`. `many` parses but fails validation: `only one-to-one/many-to-one foreign keys are supported; model many-to-many with an explicit join entity` |\n| `@onDelete` | `restrict`, `cascade`, `setNull` (default: database default). `setNull` requires `@nullable`; `@onDelete(\"\")` emits no action |\n| `@comment` | JSDoc on the FK column |\n\nHard rules: both endpoints must be `UUID` (`V3 foreign keys require UUID fields`); the source cannot be `@generated` or `@code`; only single-column FKs exist (no composite syntax); self relations are legal and generate a typed `.references((): AnyPgColumn => ...)` callback; `relation` declarations come after all `entity` blocks. Relations carry no authorization - use `restrict` for row/field policy ([auth-permissions.md](auth-permissions.md)).\n\nGenerated UI: FK cells render the target's display text (`@tableDisplay` -> `@display` -> natural field), not a bare UUID. The list batches FK lookups per resource (deduplicated, <= 200 ids, one `getMany` per target); detail pages and the drawer use `useOne`. The drawer mirrors the target's detail page, keeps a `@relationDetail` summary, supports nested FKs, and is `min(92vw, 760px)` wide. `pages ... field X roles ...` also gates drawer fields.\n\n## Indexes\n\n```text\nindex <name> <btree|hnsw|ivfflat> ( <field> [<opclass>] [, ...] )\n      [@unique] [@concurrently] [@comment(\"...\")] ;\n```\n\n```qiy\nindex products_sku_uq btree(sku) @unique;\nindex products_name_idx btree(name);\nindex products_embedding_hnsw hnsw(embedding vector_cosine_ops) @comment(\"Similarity search\");\n```\n\n| Slot | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Name | Globally unique (`duplicate index name`) |\n| Method | `btree`, `hnsw`, `ivfflat` (`Unsupported index method X`) |\n| Columns | Entity field names (not physical `@column` names); at least one |\n| Opclass | Vector only: `vector_l2_ops`, `vector_ip_ops`, `vector_cosine_ops`; btree opclass is rejected |\n| `@unique` | Not allowed on vector indexes |\n| `@concurrently` | PostgreSQL only (`concurrently requires PostgreSQL`); migration cannot run in a transaction |\n\nVector indexes require PostgreSQL + `pgvector`, exactly one `Vector` column, a compatible opclass, and dimension <= 2000 (`hnsw vector dimension cannot exceed 2000`). PostgreSQL does not index foreign keys automatically - add `btree(<fk>)` when lists filter by them. For composite indexes put equality columns first and range/sort columns after (`btree(status, placedAt)`). MySQL narrows indexed `Text`/`File` columns to `varchar(255)`.\n\n## Validation pipeline and modeling limits\n\n```text\ninclude expansion -> lexer/parser -> IR validation -> generation validation -> write files\n```\n\n- Parse errors abort immediately with the first error; IR/generation errors are collected and joined in one message; the CLI exits 1 and writes nothing on failure.\n- Parse success is not generation success: missing `id`, bad icons, bad route names, hidden required fields, auth columns, scope/restrict references, features dependencies and permission sources are all checked later.\n\nModeling limits (do not promise these):\n\n- No expressions, functions, template strings, default values, computed/transient fields or Text length constraints.\n- One database dialect per model; no cross-database joins.\n- No implicit many-to-many: model an explicit join entity with two `one` relations.\n- No business workflow inference from fields/relations. Use `workflow orderInventory` (fixed, PostgreSQL, exact field contract) or an explicit `dataflow` ([dataflows-actions.md](dataflows-actions.md)).\n- Format: `mode integration` models generate a Refine web package only; they reject `auth`, `scope`, `restrict`, `workflow`, `dataflow`, `storage`, `elysia`, `env` and `realtime` ([workspace-integration.md](workspace-integration.md)).\n- `restrict` cannot be combined with `dataflow`/`orderInventory` on the same resource; the generator fails closed.\n- No forward compatibility: unknown constructs/annotations are rejected, so regenerate after CLI upgrades.\n\n## Worked modeling walkthrough\n\n```qiy\nqiy v0;\n\napplication catalog @comment(\"Catalog back office\") {\n  database postgresql {}\n  api { client rest; }\n\n  include \"modules/shared.qiy\";\n\n  enum productStatus {\n    value draft label \"Draft\" color default;\n    value active label \"Active\" color green;\n    value archived label \"Archived\" color red;\n  }\n\n  entity products table catalog_products\n    @label(\"Products\") @icon(AppstoreOutlined)\n    @display(\"{$.sku} · {$.name}\") @tableDisplay(\"{$.sku}\") {\n    field id UUID @id;\n    field sku Text @unique @code(\"PRD-{YYYYMM}-{seq:4}\");\n    field name Text @filter(contains, startsWith, eq);\n    field price Money(12, 2) @nullable @filter(eq, gte, lte);\n    field status productStatus;\n    field supplierId UUID;\n    index catalog_products_sku_uq btree(sku) @unique;\n    index catalog_products_supplier_idx btree(supplierId);\n  }\n\n  entity suppliers @display(\"{$.name}\") {\n    field id UUID @id;\n    field name Text @unique;\n  }\n\n  relation productSupplier products supplierId suppliers id one @onDelete(restrict);\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\n# modules/shared.qiy - a fragment: no qiy header, no application wrapper\nenum auditAction { value created; value updated; value deleted; }\n```\n\nSteps after editing: run `qiy generate <model> <dir> --sync` (or `qiy init --sync` for a mounted admin), review the generated Drizzle migration and the options table, run `bun run check`, `bun test`, and `bun run build` inside the generated workspace, then exercise list/create/edit/show for the changed resource. Never apply a migration you have not read, especially when it drops or renames a column.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Error | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Unsupported field type String` | Type is a closed set | Use `Text`, `Integer`, an enum, or `Text` + `@mime` |\n| `Field type Text has no parameters` | Parentheses on a non-parameterized type | Remove them; enforce length in migrations/business code |\n| `Unsupported field attribute @required` | Fields have no `@required` | Required is the default; use `@nullable` |\n| `... V0 CRUD requires exactly one UUID primary key named id` | Missing/renamed/retyped PK | Keep `field id UUID @id` |\n| `required field cannot be hidden from the create form` | Non-null field hidden via `@visible(false)`/`@formVisible(false)` | Add `@nullable` or keep it visible |\n| `... cannot interpolate foreign key field customerId` | Display template references an FK source | Reference a scalar field of the target (`{$.customerName}`) |\n| `invalid @code template \"...\": the pattern needs {seq}, ...` | Template has no uniqueness token | Add `{seq:N}` or `{random:N}` |\n| `Entity X: duplicate entity or table name` | Include repeated or name collision | Include once; unique names |\n| `Expected field or index` | Unsupported token inside an entity | Only `field` and `index` are allowed |\n| `Expected relation near token N` | `relation` before entities | Move all relations after all entities |\n| `Expected enum near token N` | Enum declared after an entity | Move enums before entities |\n| FK filled with a random UUID at create | Relation missing | Declare the `relation` |\n| `hnsw requires PostgreSQL and pgvector` | Wrong dialect or extension missing | PostgreSQL + `extension pgvector;` + `@extension(pgvector)` |\n| `X: route path must be lowercase and URL-safe` | Uppercase/invalid `table` name | Use `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$` |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - complete DSL map, all blocks/settings/annotations\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - roles, scope, restrict, pages\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - transactional commands and UI actions\n- [UI, charts and i18n](ui-charts-i18n.md) - menu, dashboard, charts, messages\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - file fields and subscriptions\n- [CLI workflows](cli-workflows.md) - generate, `--sync`, install, run\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - cross-area error table\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [entity and field](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/entity)\n- [relation and index](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/relation-index)\n- [generated values](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/generated-values)\n- [modules/include](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/modules)\n- [annotations](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/annotations)\n- [validation overview](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/overview)\n",
  "references/refine-providers.md": "# Generated Refine providers\n\nUse this file when you need to understand or extend the generated Web layer after generation: DataProvider request mapping, AuthProvider login/identity, AccessControlProvider `can()`, LiveProvider, AuditLogProvider, notifications, i18n, routing and kbar. Everything here is generated from the model, so change the model first and keep hand-written code in unowned files.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/refine-providers\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Provider matrix](#provider-matrix)\n- [DataProvider](#dataprovider)\n- [AuthProvider](#authprovider)\n- [AccessControlProvider](#accesscontrolprovider)\n- [LiveProvider](#liveprovider)\n- [AuditLogProvider](#auditlogprovider)\n- [Notifications, i18n, router, kbar](#notifications-i18n-router-kbar)\n- [Extending safely](#extending-safely)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## Provider matrix\n\n`apps/web/app/root.tsx` injects every provider; `apps/web/app/resources.ts` is the shared metadata source (`resources`, `resourceNames`, `getResource`, `menuGroups`, field `type`/`enumValues`/`relation`/`liveMode`/visibility/roles).\n\n| Provider | File | Exports | DSL switch |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `DataProvider` | `app/data-provider.ts` | `dataProvider`, `createDataProvider`, `createGraphQLDataProvider` | `api { client rest\\|graphql; }` (overridable by `VITE_QIY_API_TRANSPORT`) |\n| `AuthProvider` + `AccessControlProvider` | `app/auth.ts` | `qiyAuthProvider`, `qiyAuthToken`, `fetchCurrentIdentity`, `clearIdentityCache`, `qiyAccessControlProvider` | any `auth` block |\n| `LiveProvider` | `app/providers/live-provider.ts` | `qiyLiveProvider`, `createQiyLiveProvider` | `realtime` (requires `auth`) |\n| `AuditLogProvider` | `app/providers/audit-log-provider.ts` | `auditLogProvider`, `createAuditLogProvider` | any `auth` |\n| `NotificationProvider` | `app/ui/index.tsx` | `useQiyNotificationProvider` | always |\n| `i18nProvider` | `app/i18n.ts` | `createI18nProvider`, `resolveLocale`, `getAntdLocale` | `messages` (always present) |\n| `routerProvider` | `app/root.tsx` + `app/routes.ts` | `@refinedev/react-router` default | resources/`features`/`actions` |\n| kbar | `app/root.tsx` | `RefineKbarProvider`, `RefineKbar` | always |\n\nHelpers: `app/api-error.ts` (`qiyApiError`), `app/messages.ts` (`projectMessages`, `projectMessage`, `defaultMessageLocale`), `app/auth/oidc-client.ts` (single-provider PKCE), `app/auth/oidc-multi.ts` (multi/hybrid callbacks, bind, onboarding), `app/auth/account.ts` (profile identities/unbind).\n\nGenerated provider files are listed in `.qiy-generated.json` and are rewritten by `--sync`. `app/extensions/**` and integration-mode `app/host/**` are not.\n\n## DataProvider\n\nREST base is `/api/v1`, GraphQL base is `/graphql`. Every request adds `Authorization: Bearer <qiy.access_token>` when present; there is no refresh, CSRF or automatic retry. An unknown `resource` fails before the request with `Unknown resource: <resource>`.\n\n| Refine method | REST request | Returns |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `getList` | `GET /api/v1/<resource>?page&pageSize&sort&order&search&filters` | `{ data, total }` |\n| `getOne` | `GET /api/v1/<resource>/:id` | `{ data }` |\n| `getMany` | chunks of 100: `GET /api/v1/<resource>?page=1&pageSize=<n>&filters=[{\"field\":\"id\",\"operator\":\"in\",\"value\":\"a,b\"}]` | `{ data }` |\n| `create` | `POST /api/v1/<resource>` | `{ data }` (201) |\n| `update` | `PATCH /api/v1/<resource>/:id` | `{ data }` |\n| `deleteOne` | `DELETE /api/v1/<resource>/:id` | `{ data }` |\n| `deleteMany` | `DELETE /api/v1/<resource>?ids=a,b` | `{ data }` array |\n| `custom` (command) | `POST /api/v1/commands/<flow>` or `/api/v1/orders/:uuid/(submit\\|approve\\|ship\\|cancel)` | `{ data }` |\n| `custom` (analytics) | `GET /api/v1/<resource>/(distribution\\|trend\\|aggregate)` | `{ data: { items } }` or `{ data: { value, operator } }` |\n\nPagination/sort/search/filter mapping:\n\n| Refine input | Query parameter | Server constraint |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `pagination.currentPage` (default 1) | `page` | min 1 |\n| `pagination.pageSize` (default 20) | `pageSize` | max **100** (larger -> 422); generated list pages use 10 |\n| `sorters[0]` (first only) | `sort`, `order` (`asc`/`desc`) | sortable field, else 400 `Unsupported sort field` |\n| filter field `q` or `__search` | `search` | max 200 chars; list search box uses `__search` |\n| other filters | `filters` JSON string | max 50 clauses / 2000 chars; field+operator whitelist |\n\nThe generated provider sends the **array** filter shape:\n\n```json\n[{\"field\":\"status\",\"operator\":\"eq\",\"value\":\"approved\"},\n {\"operator\":\"and\",\"filters\":[{\"field\":\"price\",\"operator\":\"gte\",\"value\":\"10\"},\n                              {\"field\":\"price\",\"operator\":\"lte\",\"value\":\"20\"}]}]\n```\n\nArray values are joined with commas (`in`/`between`). Operators are `eq`, `contains`, `startsWith`, `endsWith`, `gt`, `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `between`, `in`; `id` supports all except text operators. Unknown field -> 400 `Unsupported filter field`; bad operator -> 400 `Unsupported filter operator`; invalid JSON -> 400 `Invalid filters`.\n\n`getMany` protections: ids normalized/deduplicated/nulled and truncated to **200**; chunked at **100** per request; a 30-second merged cache keyed by resource + sorted ids with in-flight promise sharing; `create`/`update`/`deleteOne`/`deleteMany`/command POSTs clear it. Ids beyond 200 are silently dropped. GraphQL `getMany` chunks but has no cache.\n\nErrors are always `Error` instances with `statusCode`, plus `errorKey` when the server sends one; `message` is resolved through `projectMessages` with the server `error` text as fallback. Typical statuses: 401 unauthenticated, 403 policy/page denial, 400 bad filter or empty PATCH, 404 not found, 422 body validation.\n\nREST vs GraphQL:\n\n| Aspect | REST | GraphQL |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| List | query parameters | `QiyList(page, pageSize, search, sort, order, filters)` |\n| Detail | `/:id` | `<apiName>ById(id:)` |\n| Writes | POST/PATCH/DELETE | `create*`/`update*`/`delete*`/`delete*Many` |\n| Commands | REST command route | **same REST command route** |\n| `getMany` | chunk + 30s cache | chunk, no cache |\n| Errors | `statusCode` + `errorKey` localization | `statusCode` only, no `errorKey` localization |\n| Analytics | REST endpoints | `*Distribution`/`*Trend`/`*Aggregate` fields |\n\n`custom` is allowlisted, not a general escape hatch: POST commands must be declared dataflows (or the fixed order workflow URLs) and GET analytics must be `<resource>/(distribution|trend|aggregate)` for a known resource. Others throw `Unknown workflow command` / `Unknown analytics resource` (GraphQL: `Unknown analytics field` / `Unknown aggregate field`). Analytics validation: `aggregate` op in `sum/avg/min/max` on numeric fields; `distribution` on enum fields; `trend` on `DateTime` with `days` 1..365.\n\n`resources[].liveMode` comes from `realtime` `mode` (`auto`/`manual`, otherwise `off`). Only the generated show route passes it to `useOne`; list pages must pass `liveMode` to `useTable` themselves.\n\n## AuthProvider\n\n| Mode | Login page | Browser implementation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Local password | `AuthPage` (no register/forgot/remember) | `POST /api/v1/auth/login` |\n| OTP | two phases | `/auth/otp/request`, `/auth/otp/verify` |\n| Single OIDC | one button + one silent renewal | browser PKCE direct to `VITE_QIY_TOKEN_URL` |\n| Multi-provider | buttons from `GET /auth/providers` | `oidc-multi`, callback via `/auth/exchange` |\n| Hybrid | password form + provider buttons | local login + `oidc-multi`, new identities go to onboarding |\n| Integration | host login extension | delegates to `window.qiyHostAuth` |\n\nMethods: `login` (username/email+password, OTP triplet, `providerName`, or OIDC redirect), `logout` (clears identity/token/flow state; single OIDC also hits IdP logout), `check` (local only, no request), `getIdentity` (`/auth/me`, 60s cache with in-flight merge), `getPermissions` (returns the **role string**, not an array), `onError` (clears identity; 401 logs out, 403 keeps the session). `register`/`forgotPassword`/`updatePassword` are not generated.\n\nIdentity cache: TTL 60s keyed by the access token; failed `/auth/me` caches `null` for 60s too; cleared by `logout`, any `onError`, or `clearIdentityCache()`.\n\nStorage keys: `qiy.access_token` (all generated modes), `qiy.id_token` + `qiy.expires_at` (single OIDC/multi), PKCE state in sessionStorage (`qiy.oidc.verifier`, `.state`, `.return_to`, `.provider`, `.mode`, `.silent_attempt`), `qiy.oauth.onboarding` (hybrid). Multi-provider `logout` removes only the access token, not `id_token`/`expires_at`.\n\nRedirects: unauthenticated protected route -> `/auth/login`; local/OTP success -> `/`; provider success -> stored `return_to` or `/`; onboarding -> `/auth/onboarding?token=...`; bind -> `/profile?linked=<provider>`; 401 -> logout -> login; 403 stays on the page.\n\n`check()` verifies only that `qiy.access_token` exists (single OIDC also checks `qiy.expires_at` with a 60s margin). It does **not** verify signature, issuer, revocation, the user row, role changes or account status - the server decides on every request. An expired token counts as logged in until the first 401.\n\nSSR: the Web is `ssr: false`; `check()` returns unauthenticated without `window`, `authHeaders()` is empty, and `createQiyLiveProvider()` returns `undefined`. Use `fetchCurrentIdentity()` where hooks are unavailable.\n\n## AccessControlProvider\n\n`can()` evaluates in order and returns on the first match:\n\n| Order | Condition | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | No identity / `/auth/me` failed | `{ can: false, reason: \"Authentication required\" }` |\n| 2 | `restrict.allow roles` excludes the role | deny |\n| 3 | `pages` rule for that action | allow/deny by role |\n| 4 | Command policy (`action`/`dataflow` allow) | see below |\n| 5 | `action === \"audit\"` | admin only |\n| 6 | role is `admin` | allow |\n| 7 | resource is the auth user table | deny (`User administration is restricted`) |\n| 8 | role is `operator`, or action is `list`/`show` | allow |\n| 9 | otherwise | deny with role/action reason |\n\nCommand policy precedence: a verification policy is evaluated in the browser with the same expression semantics; a permission policy requires **all** expanded values when `/auth/me` returned `permissions` (roles are then ignored) and falls back to the role list when permission metadata is absent; a roles-only policy uses the role list. The server re-runs the same rules inside the command route.\n\nConsumers: sidebar `list`, `ResourcePageGuard` (`list`/`create`/`show`/`edit`), create/show/edit/delete buttons, batch delete selection, detail audit panel (`audit`), business and batch actions (by action name, `params.id`/`ids`), manual action pages, kbar actions. `options.buttons.enableAccessControl` + `hideIfUnauthorized` hide rather than disable.\n\nFront-end role changes take up to ~1 minute (60s identity cache + query `staleTime` 30s); the server applies changes on the next request. Field visibility (`@listVisible`/`@formVisible`/`@showVisible`, `pages field roles`) is UI only. Only `restrict mask`, row predicates and `scope` are security boundaries.\n\n## LiveProvider\n\nGenerated only with `realtime` (which requires `auth`). Transport is the Ably JS SDK 2.x; the server issues a subscribe-only TokenRequest from `POST /api/v1/realtime/token`. Channels are `qiy:<table>` or `qiy:<table>:<claimValue>` for claim-segmented resources; the client resolves granted channels from the token capability instead of assuming names. Events map to the declared `created`/`updated`/`deleted`; `params.id`/`params.ids` trim callbacks by `payload.id`/`payload.data.id`; unsubscribing calls `channel.unsubscribe`.\n\n`auto` lets Refine invalidate matching queries, `manual` sends events to `onLiveEvent` (not wired by default, so implement it in the page). Token failures: 401 unauthenticated, 403 no channel permission, 503 when `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED=1`. Dataflow emits go to `qiy:event:<event>` and need a separate subscription. Delivery is at-least-once ([storage-realtime.md](storage-realtime.md)).\n\n## AuditLogProvider\n\nGenerated with `auth`; every resource gets `meta: { audit: [] }`. `get` calls `GET /api/v1/audit-logs/?resource&resourceId&action&actorId&page&pageSize` with `cache: \"no-store\"`; `create`/`update` throw because audit rows are written by the server inside the business transaction and are immutable. Unknown resource -> `Unknown audit resource` before the request; Refine `create`/`update`/`delete` map to `<resource>.created/.updated/.deleted`.\n\nServer contract: 401 unauthenticated; 403 for non-admin (`Audit history is restricted to administrators`); 400 unknown resource; 403 with `Tenant audit history requires persisted scope metadata` when the resource has `scope` (fail-closed); otherwise `{ data, total }`, `pageSize` <= 100. Rows are `{ id, resource, action, createdAt, author: { id, name, deleted } | null, meta: { id } }`; deleted actors keep their id and set `deleted: true`.\n\nThe detail-page `AuditHistory` panel uses `useLogList` and is wrapped in `CanAccess action=\"audit\"` (admin only). The server rejects again.\n\n## Notifications, i18n, router, kbar\n\n- `NotificationProvider`: `useQiyNotificationProvider` is `@refinedev/antd`'s `useNotificationProvider`, mounted inside the antd `App`/`ConfigProvider`. Use `useNotification()` or Refine mutation notifications; do not use static antd `message` in generated pages.\n- `i18nProvider`: `createI18nProvider(locale, setLocale)` uses one i18next instance with `keySeparator: false`, `nsSeparator: false`, escaping off; merges Refine messages + built-in chrome + project messages; `changeLocale` persists `qiy.locale`; `getAntdLocale` feeds `ConfigProvider`. Error keys live in the same `messages` block.\n- `routerProvider`: `@refinedev/react-router`; routes are `auth/login`, `auth/callback`, `oauth/*`, `auth/onboarding`, `profile`, `/` (overview), `/system/{overview,api-docs,api-keys}` (per `features`), and `/:resource`, `/:resource/new`, `/:resource/:id`, `/:resource/:id/edit`, each wrapped in `ResourcePageGuard`.\n- kbar: `RefineKbarProvider` wraps `<Refine>` and `<RefineKbar />` renders inside it (Ctrl/Cmd+K). Actions are generated from resources, filtered by `can()`, and labeled via i18n. Register custom actions in an unowned component with `useRegisterActions`.\n\n## Extending safely\n\nPrefer the model: `api.client`, `auth`, `pages`/`restrict`, `allow`, `scope`/`mask`, `realtime`, `messages`, `features`. Generated provider files are manifest-owned; `--sync` rewrites them.\n\nFor genuinely custom behavior, use unowned files: `app/extensions/**` (manual action pages), `app/plugins/**`, `app/hooks/**`, integration `app/host/**`. Factories such as `createDataProvider`, `createQiyLiveProvider`, `createAuditLogProvider` and `createI18nProvider` can be composed/wrapped without editing judgment logic. Host wrappers can add an outer `ConfigProvider`.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Login works but every page 403 | Role excluded by `restrict.allow roles` or `pages` | Check `can()` branch; adjust model rules |\n| Menu only shows overview | `viewer` blocked or no `list` permission | Same |\n| Direct `/{resource}/new` shows 403 | Page guard denies `create` | Expected; change `pages` or role |\n| List 422 | `pageSize > 100` or non-integer `page` | Use server pagination defaults |\n| 400 `Unsupported filter field` | Filtering a non-filterable field | Generate filters from `filterable`/`filterModes` |\n| 400 `Invalid filters` | Hand-built filters in the wrong shape | Send `[{ field, operator, value }]` |\n| FK cell shows `-` or an id | `getMany` failed: >200 ids, field without `in`, or stale 30s cache | Inspect the `filters=` request; remount if needed |\n| Many `/auth/me` calls | Identity cache cleared repeatedly or token rewritten | Check `onError`/`logout` frequency and token writes |\n| Logged out on 403 | Custom fetch wrapper treats 403 as 401 | Only 401 logs out |\n| Multi-provider login succeeds but all pages 403 | No users row (multi mode never creates accounts) | Pre-create rows and identity columns, or use hybrid |\n| `bind`/`unbind` 409 | Identity owned by another account / last login method | Bind from the original account; set a password or bind another provider first |\n| Audit panel 403 | Not admin, or the resource has `scope` | Use admin; tenant audit needs persisted scope metadata |\n| Audit panel 400 `Unknown audit resource` | Entity name instead of table name | Pass `resource.name` (table name) |\n| List does not refresh live | `useTable` has no `liveMode` | Pass `liveMode: resource.liveMode` |\n| Detail receives no events | Role not in `realtime.roles`, or segmented claim missing | Check token capability and claims |\n| Command button throws `Unknown workflow command` | Undeclared command URL or non-POST | Declare a `dataflow`/`action` |\n| GraphQL errors are not localized | GraphQL errors carry no `errorKey` | Use the REST client or map messages yourself |\n| `qiy.id_token` remains after logout | Multi-provider logout only clears the access token | Clear it yourself or use hybrid |\n| Custom provider overwritten by `--sync` | File is in `.qiy-generated.json` | Move it to an unowned path |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - login modes, roles, policies backing `can()`\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - commands, `allow`, idempotency keys\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - LiveProvider transport and outbox\n- [UI, charts and i18n](ui-charts-i18n.md) - theme, i18n, charts used by pages\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - provider tests and acceptance\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [Refine providers](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/refine-providers)\n- [API and data sources](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/api)\n- [auth guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/auth)\n- [realtime](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/realtime)\n",
  "references/storage-realtime.md": "# Storage and realtime\n\nUse this file when you add file uploads/downloads, choose a storage provider, plan attachment cleanup, or declare realtime subscriptions and operate the outbox (transport, roles, claim channels, metrics, replay).\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/realtime (`/guide/storage`)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [storage block](#storage-block)\n- [File and Files fields](#file-and-files-fields)\n- [Storage columns and API contract](#storage-columns-and-api-contract)\n- [Upload endpoints and validation](#upload-endpoints-and-validation)\n- [Attachment metadata and permissions](#attachment-metadata-and-permissions)\n- [Resumable uploads](#resumable-uploads)\n- [Storage environment variables](#storage-environment-variables)\n- [Cleanup](#cleanup)\n- [Realtime grammar](#realtime-grammar)\n- [Modes, events and channels](#modes-events-and-channels)\n- [Transports](#transports)\n- [Outbox operations and monitoring](#outbox-operations-and-monitoring)\n- [Realtime limits](#realtime-limits)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## storage block\n\n```qiy\nstorage { provider local; }   // or storage { provider s3; }\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Position | Inside `application`, after `elysia` and before `auth` |\n| Keys | Only `provider` |\n| Values | `local` or `s3` (`Unsupported storage provider X`) |\n| Default | Omitted means `provider local` (`QIY_STORAGE_PROVIDER` defaults to `local`) |\n| Effect | Sets the runtime `QIY_STORAGE_PROVIDER` default, whether S3 variables are generated, and the target of `attachments:*` tools |\n\nStorage is a **protected endpoint**, not a public static directory: every download is authenticated and ownership-checked. Metadata (size, MIME, owner, resource) is managed next to the object.\n\n## File and Files fields\n\n```qiy\nfield datasheet File\n  @nullable\n  @label(\"Datasheet\")\n  @upload(both)\n  @maxBytes(10485760)\n  @mime(\"application/pdf\")\n  @maxFiles(1);\n\nfield attachments Files\n  @nullable\n  @upload(base64)\n  @maxBytes(5242880)\n  @mime(\"application/pdf\", \"image/*\")\n  @maxFiles(5);\n```\n\n```text\nfield <name> ( \"File\" | \"Files\" ) ( \"@upload(\" ( \"binary\" | \"base64\" | \"both\" ) \")\"\n  | \"@maxBytes(\" <int> \")\" | \"@mime(\" <mime> ( \",\" <mime> )* \")\" | \"@maxFiles(\" <int> \")\" )* \";\"\n```\n\n| Attribute | Applies to | Default | Validation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `@upload(binary\\|base64\\|both)` | File/Files | `binary` | `File upload mode must be binary, base64 or both`; non-file field -> `@upload is only valid for File and Files fields` |\n| `@maxBytes(n)` | File/Files | `26214400` (25 MiB, per file) | 1..104857600 (100 MiB): `File maxBytes must be between 1 and 104857600` |\n| `@mime(\"a/b\", \"image/*\")` | File/Files | `*/*` | Lowercased, must match `type/subtype` or `type/*`; empty/duplicate rejected; at least one |\n| `@maxFiles(n)` | `File` only `1`; `Files` 1..20 | `Files` defaults to `6` | `File fields support maxFiles(1); declare the field as Files for multiple files`; `Files maxFiles must be between 1 and 20` |\n| Other field annotations | - | - | `@nullable`, `@label`, `@comment`, `@formVisible`, ... work as usual |\n\nHard constraints: `File`/`Files` cannot be a primary key; `Files` cannot be `@unique` and is not sortable/filterable by default; contradictory modifiers such as `File @maxFiles(2)` are rejected; display templates cannot interpolate `File`/`Files`.\n\n## Storage columns and API contract\n\n| Field | PostgreSQL | SQLite | MySQL |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `File` | `text` | `text` | `text` (`varchar(255)` when unique/indexed) |\n| `Files` | `jsonb` (`string[]`) | `text` with `mode:\"json\"` | `json` |\n\n`File` stores one storage key; `Files` stores an array of keys, each with its own metadata and object. Downloads, signing, ownership and orphan scanning reuse the single-file logic.\n\n| Location | `File` | `Files` |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| REST body | `string` (1..240) | `string[]` (`minItems: 1`, `maxItems: @maxFiles ?? 6`) |\n| GraphQL | `String` | `[String!]` |\n| CSV import | Supported | **Not imported** (`Files` columns are excluded) |\n| List/form | Single upload control + preview/download | Multi-file control (`maxCount = @maxFiles`) |\n\n## Upload endpoints and validation\n\n| Method | Path | Purpose | Role |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/files?key&resource&field[&fileName&contentType&resourceId]` | Binary upload (`request.blob()`) | `admin`/`operator` |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/files/base64` | JSON upload `{ key, data, contentType, resource, field, ... }` | `admin`/`operator` |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/files?key=` | Read object (authenticated stream) | Owner or `admin` |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/files/metadata?key=` | Attachment metadata | Owner or `admin` |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/files/signed?key=` | Signed URL (S3: 300s presigned; local: `null`) | Owner or `admin` |\n| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/files?key=` | Delete object + metadata | `admin` only |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/files/upload-sessions` | Start a resumable session | `admin`/`operator` |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/files/upload-sessions/:id` | Received byte count | Session creator |\n| `PUT` | `/api/v1/files/upload-sessions/:id?offset=n` | Append a chunk; offset must equal bytes received | Session creator |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/files/upload-sessions/:id/complete` | Merge + validate + persist | Session creator |\n| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/files/upload-sessions/:id` | Abandon session | Session creator |\n\nServer-side validation order (authoritative; frontend checks are only UX):\n\n1. Storage key shape (each segment `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+(\\.[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+)*`, <= 240 chars) -> 400 `Invalid storage key`.\n2. `resource + field` must match a declared file field -> 400 `Unknown file field` (fail-closed).\n3. Encoding mode (`binary`/`base64`/`both`) -> 415 `File field does not accept <enc> uploads`.\n4. Key already exists (metadata or object) -> 409 `Storage key already exists`.\n5. Size <= `@maxBytes` -> 413 `File is too large`.\n6. MIME matches `@mime` (`image/*` supported) -> 415 `File MIME type is not allowed`.\n7. Write object, then metadata; if metadata fails the written object is deleted (minimize orphans).\n\n## Attachment metadata and permissions\n\n| Mode | Storage | Trigger |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| In-process (default) | `Map` | `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA` is not `database` |\n| Database | `attachments` table | `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` + `DATABASE_URL` |\n\n**Production servers require database metadata**: `server.ts` throws when `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA !== \"database\"` at startup, because in-memory metadata is unreliable across replicas/restarts. Generated `.env` files already set `database`.\n\n| Operation | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| Read/download/metadata/signed | `principal.id === metadata.ownerId` or `principal.role === \"admin\"`; otherwise 404 (existence is not disclosed) |\n| Upload | `admin`/`operator` (`viewer` gets 403 `Permission denied`) |\n| Delete | `admin` only |\n| Missing metadata | Always 404; access is never \"restored\" from a cache |\n\n`resource`/`resourceId`/`fileName`/`contentType`/`size`/`ownerId` are recorded from the upload request for audit and cleanup. Deleting an entity row does **not** delete objects.\n\n## Resumable uploads\n\n- Session state is in **process memory**, TTL 1 hour; multi-replica deployments need sticky sessions or a shared session table.\n- `PUT` offset must exactly equal bytes already received, else 409; exceeding `@maxBytes` returns 413.\n- `complete` re-validates MIME and upload mode; an empty session is 400. S3 presigned PUT / native multipart **is not implemented** - uploads always pass through the server.\n- `Files` is one request per file: the frontend uploads each selection and collects keys. There is no atomic multi-file upload, so a failure at file N leaves N-1 objects behind (clean them with the orphan scan).\n\n## Storage environment variables\n\n| Variable | Default | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_PROVIDER` | `local` (or the model value) | `local`/`s3`; other values throw at runtime |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_ROOT` | `<server>/../../storage` (generated `.env` uses `./storage`) | Local provider root |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA` | `database` (generated `.env`) | `database` uses the attachments table; required in production |\n| `QIY_S3_BUCKET` | empty | **Required** (`S3 bucket is required`) |\n| `QIY_S3_REGION` | empty | S3 region |\n| `QIY_S3_ENDPOINT` | empty | S3-compatible endpoint (R2/MinIO) |\n| `QIY_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `QIY_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` | empty | Credentials; server only |\n| `QIY_S3_SESSION_TOKEN` | empty | Session token for temporary credentials |\n| `QIY_ATTACHMENT_ORPHAN_LIMIT` | `1000` (code cap 10000) | Orphan scan batch size (`attachments:orphans` reads only this variable, no `--limit`) |\n| `QIY_ATTACHMENT_CLEANUP_LIMIT` | `1000` (code cap 10000) | Missing-metadata cleanup batch size |\n\nS3 uses Bun's native `Bun.S3Client` (no AWS SDK) with `save/open/exists/delete/presign/list`; `list()` pages at 20x1000 keys to avoid unbounded scans from a misconfigured bucket.\n\n## Cleanup\n\n```qiy\nelysia {\n  cron { job attachmentCleanup pattern \"0 0 * * *\" task cleanupMissingAttachments; }\n}\n```\n\n| Direction | Command | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Metadata exists, object missing | `bun run attachments:cleanup` (dry-run by default; `--apply` executes) | Delete attachment rows whose file is gone; the `cleanupMissingAttachments` cron deletes them explicitly |\n| Object exists, metadata missing | `bun run attachments:orphans` (dry-run by default; `--apply` executes) | List/delete objects without records; prints `{ objects, metadata, orphans, missingObjects, removed, dryRun, truncated }` |\n\nBoth require `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` and `DATABASE_URL`; `removed` is non-zero only with `--apply`. Batch size comes from `QIY_ATTACHMENT_ORPHAN_LIMIT` / `QIY_ATTACHMENT_CLEANUP_LIMIT` (default 1000, cap 10000); an over-limit orphan scan sets `truncated: true`. Deletes are irreversible and may incur S3 delete costs - dry-run, review, then apply. Already-issued S3 URLs remain valid until they expire.\n\n## Realtime grammar\n\n`realtime` requires generated `auth` and sits with the other config blocks. It is rejected in `mode integration`.\n\n```text\nrealtime \"{\" [ \"mode\" ( \"auto\" | \"manual\" ) \";\" ]\n  ( \"resource\" <entity> \"{\"\n      \"events\" ( \"created\" | \"updated\" | \"deleted\" ) ( \",\" … )* \";\"\n      \"roles\" role ( \",\" role )* \";\"\n      [ \"when\" <field> \"claim\" <claim> \";\" ]\n    \"}\" )+\n\"}\"\n```\n\n```qiy\nrealtime {\n  mode auto;\n  resource orders {\n    events created, updated, deleted;\n    roles admin, operator, viewer;\n  }\n  resource stock_movements {\n    events created;\n    roles admin, operator;\n    when warehouseCode claim warehouse.code;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Element | Required | Default | Validation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `mode` | no | `auto` | Only `auto`/`manual` (`Unsupported realtime mode`) |\n| `resource <r>` | yes (>=1) | - | Entity or table name, normalized to table name; unknown/duplicate rejected |\n| `events` | yes | - | At least one, no duplicates; only `created`/`updated`/`deleted` |\n| `roles` | yes | - | At least one, no duplicates; only admin/operator/viewer; defines who can obtain a subscribe capability |\n| `when <field> claim <claim>` | no | none | Field must exist, be **non-nullable**, and be `Text` or `Integer`; claim may contain dots |\n| Whole block | - | - | At least one resource; without `auth` -> `Realtime requires generated authentication`; `mode integration` rejected |\n\n## Modes, events and channels\n\n| Mode | Client behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `auto` | The generated LiveProvider makes Refine refresh matching `useTable`/`useOne`/`useMany` queries (detail pages match by `id`, batch pages by `ids`) |\n| `manual` | Events go to Refine `onLiveEvent`; the page decides what to do |\n\n**Important limitation**: the generator only passes `liveMode` to detail (show) pages. Generated list pages use `useTable` without `liveMode`, so they do **not** auto-refresh. Add `liveMode` (`auto`/`manual`) manually in a custom list page if you need it.\n\nRecord-level trimming: `subscribe({ params: { id } })` or `params: { ids: [...] }` only invokes the callback when `payload.id` (or `data.id`) matches. Without those params the subscriber receives all events for the resource.\n\nChannels: `qiy:<table>` for resource events and `qiy:<table>:<claimValue>` for claim-segmented resources; dataflow emits use `qiy:event:<event>`. The browser never gets publish permission - only a subscribe-only capability computed by the server (`realtimeCapabilities(principal)`), and the client subscribes using channels parsed from the token capability rather than assuming the base name.\n\nPermission model (a channel is shared by all subscribers, so per-subscriber row filtering is impossible server-side):\n\n| Constraint | Mechanism |\n| --- | --- |\n| Who may subscribe | `roles` -> subscribe-only Ably capability |\n| Which channels | Server-computed capability; client reads granted channels from the token |\n| Field masking | Payload is trimmed **before enqueue** for every `mask` that applies to a subscribable role (global masks and `claim present/absent` masks); masks that only apply to non-subscribable roles are not applied |\n| Row isolation | Impossible on a shared channel, so a resource with a `restrict` row predicate (`when`) is **forbidden** from realtime: `restrict row predicates cannot be enforced on a shared channel` |\n| Tenant segmentation | `when <field> claim <claim>` splits the resource into `qiy:<table>:<value>`; a missing claim means **no channel is issued** (`/token` 403) |\n\n`restrict { when ... }` and `when <field> claim <claim>` cannot coexist on one resource (`a claim-scoped channel already isolates rows; remove the restrict row predicates`). Role/mask-only `restrict` blocks may coexist with realtime.\n\n## Transports\n\n| `api.client` | Transport | Generated artifacts |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `rest` | **Ably** (resource channels plus `qiy:event:<event>`) | LiveProvider logic (`createQiyLiveProvider`), `POST /api/v1/realtime/token`, outbox worker |\n| `graphql` | Ably **and** GraphQL Subscription over **SSE** (`GET /api/v1/graphql/subscribe`) | Subscription root plus `web/app/subscriptions.ts` |\n\nGraphQL subscription shape:\n\n```graphql\ntype OrdersEvent { event: String! record: Orders! }\ntype Subscription { ordersChanged: OrdersEvent! }\n```\n\n- SSE endpoint `GET /api/v1/graphql/subscribe?query=...`, one `data: {...}` frame per event. Anonymous 401; role not in `roles` 403; unknown field/non-subscription document/syntax error 400; client abort closes the iterator and cleans up.\n- Payloads come from the already-trimmed outbox: masked fields have no key; GraphQL can only return `null` for fields the client explicitly requested - it never leaks values.\n- Event source: in-process bus for locally delivered events plus tailing `deliveredAt`-marked outbox rows at `QIY_REALTIME_SUBSCRIBE_POLL_MS` (default 1000, min 100), so subscribers see events delivered by any replica (deduped by row id).\n\nThe generated `web/app/subscriptions.ts` also exposes a `graphql-ws` client (WebSocket at `/graphql/ws`) with `connection_init` token auth, `subscribe`/`next`/`error`/`complete` frames, ping/pong, exponential reconnect (1s..30s) and `stop()`. SSE has the same reconnect behavior and can be disabled with `reconnect: false`.\n\n## Outbox operations and monitoring\n\nCRUD repositories write `qiy_realtime_outbox` **in the same Drizzle transaction** as the business write and audit; after commit the service triggers one delivery. A background worker scans undelivered rows every `QIY_REALTIME_POLL_MS`; PostgreSQL/MySQL claim atomically with a transaction, lease and `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, release leases on failure and retry with exponential backoff. After `QIY_REALTIME_MAX_ATTEMPTS` the row gets `deadLetteredAt` and is no longer auto-claimed; only `admin` can inspect or replay it.\n\nDataflow `emit` writes both `dataflow_outbox` and the realtime channel, committed/rolled back with the business write; `allow roles` on a flow becomes the subscribe-only capability for that event channel.\n\nOperations endpoints (all `admin`, except the Prometheus text endpoint which accepts a read-only token):\n\n| Endpoint | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GET /api/v1/realtime/outbox/dead` | Latest 100 dead letters |\n| `GET /api/v1/realtime/outbox/metrics` | JSON metrics |\n| `GET /api/v1/realtime/outbox/metrics/prometheus` | Prometheus 0.0.4 text |\n| `GET /api/v1/realtime/outbox/health` | `200 ok` / `503 degraded` by threshold |\n| `POST /api/v1/realtime/outbox/:id/replay` | Replay one dead letter |\n| `POST /api/v1/realtime/outbox/replay` | Bulk replay 1..100 unique UUIDs -> `{ replayed, notFound }` |\n| `DELETE /api/v1/realtime/outbox/delivered?retentionDays=N` | Clean delivered history |\n\nReplay and manual cleanup write `audit_events` (`realtime.outbox.replayed`, `realtime.outbox.bulk_replayed`, `realtime.outbox.cleaned`) as the current admin in the same transaction; an audit failure rolls back the operation. Automatic background cleanup has no interactive admin and writes no audit. `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED=1` stops the worker and makes `/token` return 503 (used by generated tests).\n\nCLI (calls only the protected HTTP API; never bypasses auth or audit):\n\n```powershell\n$env:QIY_REALTIME_ADMIN_TOKEN = \"<admin-access-token>\"\nbun run realtime:admin -- metrics\nbun run realtime:admin -- health\nbun run realtime:admin -- prometheus\nbun run realtime:admin -- dead\nbun run realtime:admin -- replay 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001\nbun run realtime:admin -- cleanup 30\n```\n\n`replay` accepts 1..100 unique UUIDs; `cleanup` retention is 1..3650 days. Set `QIY_REALTIME_ADMIN_URL=https://admin.example.com/api/v1/realtime/outbox` for a remote server.\n\nEnvironment variables:\n\n| Variable | Default | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `QIY_ABLY_API_KEY` | empty | Required when realtime is enabled; **server only** - browsers get a short-lived TokenRequest |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED` | `0` | `1` stops delivery and makes `/token` 503 |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_POLL_MS` | `5000` | Delivery poll, min 250 |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_LEASE_MS` | `30000` | Claim lease, min 1000; must exceed normal publish latency |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_MAX_ATTEMPTS` | `10` | 1..1000; then dead letter |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_RETENTION_DAYS` | `7` | 1..3650 |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_CLEANUP_MS` | `86400000` | Cleanup interval, min 60000 |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_SUBSCRIBE_POLL_MS` | `1000` | SSE tail interval, min 100 |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_ADMIN_URL` | local `/api/v1/realtime/outbox` | CLI target |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_ADMIN_TOKEN` | empty | Admin access token for the CLI |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_METRICS_TOKEN` | empty | Read-only Prometheus scrape token |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_ALERT_MAX_PENDING` | `1000` | Health threshold |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_ALERT_MAX_DEAD_LETTERED` | `0` | Health threshold |\n| `QIY_REALTIME_ALERT_MAX_OLDEST_PENDING_MS` | `300000` | Health threshold |\n\nInvalid values fail closed at startup/first use (e.g. `QIY_REALTIME_LEASE_MS must be an integer of at least 1000ms`).\n\nGenerated monitoring for standalone projects: `deploy/kubernetes/realtime-servicemonitor.yaml`, `deploy/kubernetes/realtime-prometheusrule.yaml`, `deploy/observability/grafana/qiy-realtime-outbox.json`. Metrics: `qiy_realtime_outbox_pending`, `_leased`, `_dead_lettered`, `_delivered`, `_oldest_pending_age_seconds`, `_health`, deliberately without user/tenant/channel/event labels (cardinality). Operator CRDs, Alertmanager routes and Grafana import are your responsibility.\n\n## Realtime limits\n\n- **At-least-once delivery only.** A crash after provider success but before the delivered marker, or a publish exceeding the lease, can duplicate an event. Consumers must be idempotent; Qiy does not claim exactly-once.\n- List pages are **not** auto-subscribed by default (only show pages get `liveMode`); custom list pages must pass `liveMode`.\n- Field-level masking only; row isolation requires claim-segmented channels. `restrict` row predicates and claim-segmented channels are mutually exclusive.\n- Multi-replica SSE tails the outbox: every subscriber polls the database. At large subscription counts, use a dedicated message broker instead.\n- SQLite realtime is single-process. PostgreSQL/MySQL workers need the lease/dead-letter columns; existing databases must be regenerated and migrated.\n- S3 presigned PUT and native multipart are not implemented; resumable sessions are in-memory and need sticky sessions.\n- `Files` uploads are not atomic; partial uploads leave orphan objects for the orphan scan.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Upload 415 | MIME not in `@mime`, or `@upload` disallows the encoding | Adjust the field or the request header/encoding |\n| Upload 403 | Caller is `viewer` | Use an `admin`/`operator` session |\n| Download 404 | Not the owner/admin, or metadata missing | Use the uploader account; check `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` |\n| Files unreadable after restart | Still using in-memory metadata | Set `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` and migrate |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database is required for production file metadata` | Production startup check | Fix `.env.production` |\n| Upload succeeded but the field is empty | Upload only returns a key; the entity must be PATCHed | Let generated forms do it, or write the key yourself |\n| Signed URL is `null` | `local` provider has no presigning | Use the protected download endpoint |\n| Orphan scan deletes nothing | Dry-run default | Add `--apply` and confirm `removed > 0` |\n| `/api/v1/realtime/token` 403 | Principal lacks the claim needed for a segmented channel | Add the claim to the users row/IdP, or drop `when ... claim ...` |\n| Page receives no events | Role not in `roles`, or capability/channel name mismatch | Check `roles`, claims, and subscribe from token capability |\n| Events miss fields | A `mask` applies to a subscribable role | Adjust the mask or roles |\n| Dead letters keep growing | Ably unreachable/wrong key/retry cap hit | Check `outbox/health` and `outbox/dead`, fix, then replay |\n| Generation rejects realtime | Resource has a `restrict` row predicate / no `auth` / integration mode | Remove the predicate, add `auth`, or use a host LiveProvider |\n| `/token` 503 `Realtime is disabled` | `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED=1` | Unset it |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - `emit` and realtime channel linkage\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - roles, mask, restrict mutual exclusions\n- [Modeling and generation](modeling-and-generation.md) - `File`/`Files` field rules\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - storage/realtime acceptance and migration checks\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - block placement\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [realtime](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/realtime)\n- [storage (DSL)](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/storage)\n- [storage guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/storage)\n- [real services acceptance](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/real-services)\n",
  "references/system-features.md": "# System features, OpenAPI and API keys\n\nUse this file when you enable the generated developer/system pages, need to know exactly which routes, menus, endpoints, dependencies and tables exist for a feature flag combination, or you administer API keys.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/features (`/guide/api-docs-and-keys`)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [features block](#features-block)\n- [Gating matrix](#gating-matrix)\n- [The three system pages](#the-three-system-pages)\n- [REST and data endpoints](#rest-and-data-endpoints)\n- [OpenAPI filtering](#openapi-filtering)\n- [API keys](#api-keys)\n- [Environment variables](#environment-variables)\n- [Limits and security](#limits-and-security)\n- [CI recipes](#ci-recipes)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## features block\n\n```text\nfeatures \"{\" ( \"overview\" | \"apiDocs\" | \"apiKeys\" ) ( \"true\" | \"false\" ) \";\" \"}\"\n```\n\n```qiy\nfeatures {\n  overview true;   # /system/overview + menu entry (default true)\n  apiDocs true;    # /system/api-docs + OpenAPI endpoint (default false)\n  apiKeys true;    # /system/api-keys + key table/auth (default false)\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Default | Generates | Dependency |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `overview` | `true` | `/system/overview` (entities / dataflows / permission model) + menu entry | At least one of `apiDocs`/`apiKeys` must be on |\n| `apiDocs` | `false` | `/system/api-docs`, `GET /api/v1/openapi.json`, OpenAPI browser | Requires auth for access |\n| `apiKeys` | `false` | `/system/api-keys`, `qiy_api_keys` table, `/api/v1/auth/api-keys`, Bearer/`X-API-Key` fallback auth | **Requires an `auth` block** with an existing user entity |\n\nRules: only these three keys (`Unsupported features setting X; expected overview, apiDocs or apiKeys`); values must be `true`/`false`; duplicates fail; omit the block and no developer pages are generated (equivalent to `overview true; apiDocs false; apiKeys false;` with no `features.ts` menu links). `apiKeys true` without `auth` fails at parse time (`features apiKeys requires an auth block`); an unknown user entity fails at generation (`features apiKeys requires the auth user entity X`). `features` sits after `api` and before `realtime`/`elysia`/`storage`/`auth`.\n\n## Gating matrix\n\n| overview | apiDocs | apiKeys | Pages | Endpoints / tables |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| true | true | true | All three + three menu entries | `openapi.json`, `docs/model`, `api-keys`, `qiy_api_keys` |\n| true | true | false | Overview + API docs | `openapi.json`, `docs/model`; no key table/auth |\n| true | false | true | Overview + API keys | `docs/model`, `api-keys`, table; **no** `openapi.json` |\n| false | true | true | API docs + API keys | As row 1, without overview page/menu |\n| true/false | false | false | None | `features.ts` menu links empty; no `mermaid` dependency |\n\nGenerator formulas: `overviewRequested = overview && (apiDocs || apiKeys)`; `docsModelEnabled = apiDocs || overviewRequested`; `openapi.json` is generated only when `apiDocs` is true.\n\nDependency gating to remember:\n\n- `/api/v1/docs/model` exists when overview is requested **or** `apiDocs` is on.\n- `/api/v1/openapi.json` exists **only** with `apiDocs`.\n- `/api/v1/auth/api-keys` exists **only** with `apiKeys` (otherwise 404) and key headers are not parsed.\n- When all three pages are off, no developer routes, menu links or `mermaid` dependency are generated.\n\nMenu links come from `apps/web/app/features.ts` (`qiyMenuLinks`, plus `qiyFeatureFlags`). `buildMenuTree` appends them to a `System` group (creating it if needed) in fixed order. A link exists only when its page exists, so there are no dead routes.\n\n## The three system pages\n\n| Page | Route | Content |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Overview | `/system/overview` | Tabs: **entities** (Mermaid `classDiagram`, field/annotation table, relation table), **dataflows** (Mermaid `flowchart` per flow, allow rules, inputs, steps), **permissions** (fields/groups/verifications + the current user's effective permissions). No API-doc or key tab |\n| API docs | `/system/api-docs` | Full-page Ant Design OpenAPI 3.1 browser: tag list with operation counts, operation cards (method/path/summary/parameters/request body/responses/security/role+permission tags/copyable curl), case-insensitive search, empty state. **Read-only** - no try-it requests |\n| API keys | `/system/api-keys` | Full-page key management: explanation and curl examples (`Authorization: Bearer qiy_...` / `X-API-Key`), search/filter by name/prefix/status, active count/limit hint, permission tags (role/permission group + tooltips), create dialog (name + optional expiry), one-time secret display with copy, revoke confirmation |\n\nAll three live inside the `<Authenticated>` layout: unauthenticated access redirects to `/auth/login` (not 403). Their data comes from protected APIs (`/api/v1/docs/model`, `/api/v1/openapi.json`, `/api/v1/auth/api-keys`), so content is filtered by the current principal. Mermaid rendering falls back to raw source after a 10-second timeout or an error.\n\n## REST and data endpoints\n\nThe server always exposes REST under `/api/v1` and GraphQL under `/graphql`; `api { client ... }` only selects the Web transport.\n\n| Method | Path | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GET | `/api/v1/:resources` | List: pagination, sort, search, filters |\n| POST | `/api/v1/:resources` | Create |\n| GET | `/api/v1/:resources/:id` | Detail |\n| PATCH | `/api/v1/:resources/:id` | Partial update (no PUT; empty body -> 400 `Empty update`) |\n| DELETE | `/api/v1/:resources/:id` | Delete one |\n| DELETE | `/api/v1/:resources?ids=` | Delete many |\n| GET | `/api/v1/:resources/export` | Permission-constrained CSV export |\n| POST | `/api/v1/:resources/import` | Permission-constrained CSV import |\n| GET | `/api/v1/:resources/distribution` | Enum distribution |\n| GET | `/api/v1/:resources/trend` | Date trend |\n| GET | `/api/v1/:resources/aggregate?field&op` | Sum/avg/min/max (numeric fields) |\n| GET | `/api/v1/graphql/subscribe` | GraphQL subscription over SSE (graphql client + realtime) |\n| GET | `/api/v1/health` | Health probe (200) |\n\nCSV export uses the same query path as the list, so filters, `scope`, `restrict` rows and masks apply. `mask mode omit` drops the whole column (header included); `null`/`redact` keep masked values. Options: `ids=` (max 500), `columns=` (max 100), streaming in 250-row pages, default row cap 1000 (`QIY_EXPORT_MAX_ROWS`, 1..100000) with 400 `export.tooLarge`. Async mode (`?async=1`) returns 202 `{ jobId, total }` with `qiy_export_jobs`, admin-only job list/run endpoints, `409 export.claimed`/`export.notQueued`, and CSV built from the creator's principal snapshot. Every export writes a `<resource>.exported` audit event; out-of-scope writes return 403 `policy.outsideScope`.\n\nCSV import accepts `text/csv` with a header row and writes each row through the normal create path (masks and row predicates apply). Failures: 400 `import.unknownField`/`duplicateColumn`/`maskedField`/`rowLength`/`invalidRow`/`empty`, 403 `policy.outsideScope`; row cap 1000 (`QIY_IMPORT_MAX_ROWS`). Failures compensate by deleting rows created in that request (not one cross-row transaction); success returns 201 `{ imported }` and a `<resource>.imported` audit event. Async jobs live in `qiy_import_jobs` with progress/cancel/stale-job recovery (`QIY_IMPORT_JOB_STALE_MS`).\n\nSaved views (server-side, cross-device): `GET /api/v1/saved-views?resource=` returns own + shared views with `mine`; `POST /api/v1/saved-views` upserts by name (name <= 80, filters <= 50, sorters <= 10, columns <= 100); `DELETE /api/v1/saved-views/:id` allows the owner or an admin for shared views (`403 views.forbidden` otherwise). Persisted in `qiy_saved_views`; per-user limit 100 distinct names per resource (`400 views.limit`).\n\nGraphQL subscriptions: SSE at `/api/v1/graphql/subscribe`, or graphql-ws at `/graphql/ws` with `connection_init` token auth, subscribe/next/error/complete frames, ping/pong and exponential reconnect. Both respect realtime capability channels; see [storage-realtime.md](storage-realtime.md).\n\n## OpenAPI filtering\n\n`GET /api/v1/openapi.json` and `GET /api/v1/docs/model` are protected (`Cache-Control: no-store`; unauthenticated 401) and are generated per principal:\n\n| Rule | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| admin | All resources (including the user resource) and all commands |\n| non-admin | The auth user resource is hidden |\n| `restrict.roles` | Role not listed -> the whole resource disappears |\n| `pages` | Operations trimmed per action (`list`/`show`/`create`/`edit`/`delete`) |\n| viewer | Resource paths keep only `list`/`show` operations, even if `pages` allows writes |\n| command: admin | All |\n| command: `allow verification` | Hidden from non-admin (depends on runtime inputs) |\n| command: `allow roles` | Shown only when the role is listed |\n| command: `allow permission` | Requires every expanded permission **value** |\n| command: no `allow` | Hidden from non-admin (the default `admin, operator` list only helps admin) |\n\nThe document includes `info`, `servers`, `tags`, `components.securitySchemes` (`bearerSession` JWT Bearer and `apiKey` `X-API-Key`), per-resource CRUD plus `distribution`/`trend`/`aggregate`, each command as `POST /api/v1/commands/<name>`, `/auth/me`, `/auth/login` (when local login exists), the API-key and docs endpoints themselves, and `x-qiy-roles` / `x-qiy-permissions` / `x-qiy-verification` metadata. `x-qiy-permissions` records **expanded permission values** (`inventory:receive`), not declaration names; groups expand recursively and match command visibility and Web button visibility.\n\nImportant boundary: the Elysia plugin's own `/api/v1/openapi` endpoint is **public and unfiltered**. It does not contain Qiy permission filtering and must not be used as the production document source or as an attack-surface inventory. `restrict` row scopes, `mask` fields and `allow verification` commands are not represented structurally in the document at all.\n\n## API keys\n\n- Table `qiy_api_keys`: `id`, `userId`, `name`, `prefix`, `hash`, `createdAt`, `lastUsedAt`, `expiresAt`, `revokedAt` (indexes: user, unique hash).\n- Format `qiy_<8 hex prefix>_<43-char base64url secret>`. Only an HMAC-SHA256 hash (peppered with `QIY_AUTH_SECRET`) plus the prefix is stored; the full key appears once in the creation response.\n- Authentication: the normal authenticator runs first; on failure the server checks `Authorization: Bearer qiy_...` or `X-API-Key: qiy_...`. The resolved user row then goes through the same guard, scope, page and permission rules. `lastUsedAt` updates at most once per minute (best-effort).\n- Revoked/expired keys return 401. Keys carry **no id_token claims**, so `permission from claim` does not apply; they inherit the role group, the database permission column and scope-derived claim keys.\n\n| Method | Path | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `GET` | `/api/v1/auth/api-keys` | Masked list (`maskedKey` like `qiy_1a2b3c4d_********`) |\n| `POST` | `/api/v1/auth/api-keys` | `{ name, expiresAt? }` -> **201** `{ key, record }`; name 1..80; `expiresAt` must be a future ISO time; over the limit -> **409** |\n| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/auth/api-keys/:id` | Revoke your own key (idempotent); missing or someone else's -> 404 |\n\nAll key endpoints require a session and can only manage the caller's own keys. Limit: **10 active keys per user** (revoked/expired do not count); exceeding it returns 409 `At most 10 active API keys are allowed`. Revocation writes `revokedAt` and keeps the row for audit; issuing again creates a new key.\n\n`apiKeys false` means no table, no routes and no key-header fallback. Enabling it on an existing project requires a migration:\n\n```bash\ncd apps/server\nbun run db:generate\nbun run db:migrate\n```\n\n## Environment variables\n\n| Variable | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET` | **>= 32 chars**; HMAC pepper for API keys (shared with local login/OTP/onboarding). Missing/short -> hashing fails closed. Generated `.env` files only include it automatically for local/OTP auth; **a pure-OAuth project enabling `apiKeys` must add it manually** |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | `qiy_api_keys` and the other generated tables migrate through the normal path |\n| - | `features` has no dedicated variable; `overview`/`apiDocs`/`apiKeys` are baked in at generation time |\n\n## Limits and security\n\n1. **Flags gate generation, not access.** Generated pages are visible to any signed-in user; their content is filtered by role/permission. This is deliberate so every role can inspect what it may call.\n2. **The API document is a permission-filtered view**, not a complete attack surface: `allow verification` and data scope are not represented; verification-gated commands are admin-only in the document.\n3. **The document is read-only**: no try-it requests. curl examples use a placeholder token and must be replaced with a real session token or API key.\n4. **API keys are session-equivalent**: a leak grants the user's full permissions. Never echo the `key` field in CI logs; store it in a secret manager.\n5. **Revocation is irreversible**: `revokedAt` is kept for audit; re-issuing yields a new key.\n6. **Keys snapshot claims from the user row**, so role/scope column changes take effect on the next request without rotating keys; IdP claim changes (e.g. `roles`) never reach an API key.\n7. The overview page shows the caller's own effective permissions; low-privilege users seeing their own set is intended observability, not leakage.\n\n## CI recipes\n\nLeast-privilege key for automation: create a dedicated `viewer` (or narrowly permissioned) user, then create the key from that user's session rather than an admin's.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/api-keys \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CI_BOT_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"nightly-export\",\"expiresAt\":\"2027-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\"}'\n\ncurl -H \"X-API-Key: qiy_1a2b3c4d_...\" http://localhost:3000/api/v1/inventory\n```\n\nDocumentation-as-contract test: fetch `/api/v1/openapi.json` with tokens for each role and assert (a) viewer sees no write operations, (b) non-admin does not see the users resource, (c) no `allow verification` command appears for non-admin. Remember the `allow permission` document/filtering nuance and the public unfiltered `/api/v1/openapi`.\n\nGradual rollout: enabling `apiDocs true` only changes generation; access is always permission-filtered, so start with admin and grant permissions to operator/viewer later.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Unsupported features setting X; expected overview, apiDocs or apiKeys` | Typo/unknown key | Use one of the three |\n| `Duplicate features setting X` | Key repeated | Keep one |\n| `features apiKeys requires an auth block` | `apiKeys true` without `auth` | Add `auth` or disable keys |\n| `features apiKeys requires the auth user entity X` | `auth.user` does not exist | Declare the user entity |\n| Overview menu missing | `overview` true but `apiDocs` and `apiKeys` both false | Enable one docs feature |\n| `/api/v1/openapi.json` 404 | `apiDocs` false | Enable `apiDocs` |\n| `/api/v1/auth/api-keys` 404 | `apiKeys` false | Enable `apiKeys` and migrate |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET must be at least 32 characters to hash API keys` | Missing/short secret | Set a 32+ char secret in the server env |\n| API key returns 401 | Revoked, expired, or no session/claims | Re-issue; check `expiresAt`/`revokedAt` |\n| `At most 10 active API keys are allowed` (409) | Key limit reached | Revoke unused keys |\n| Viewer sees write operations in docs | Fetched the public `/api/v1/openapi` instead of `/api/v1/openapi.json` | Use the Qiy-filtered endpoint with auth |\n| Mermaid shows raw source | 10s timeout or render error | Check diagram syntax/size; fallback is intentional |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - API-key auth semantics, effective permissions, doc filtering rules\n- [UI, charts and i18n](ui-charts-i18n.md) - `qiy.docs.*`, `qiy.apiDocs.*`, `qiy.apiKey.*` copy\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - `features` position and settings\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - production verification and migrations\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - cross-area errors\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [features](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/features)\n- [API docs and keys guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/api-docs-and-keys)\n- [API and data sources](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/api)\n- [permissions: API docs relationship](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/permissions)\n",
  "references/testing-deployment.md": "# Testing, acceptance and deployment\n\nUse this file before claiming a generated project is usable or deploying it. It lists the generated scripts, what the generated test suites actually prove, migration/rollback/backup operations, deployment requirements, the real-service acceptance commands, and the common failure modes.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/deployment (`/guide/real-services`, `/guide/cli`)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Generated workspace and scripts](#generated-workspace-and-scripts)\n- [Verification pipeline](#verification-pipeline)\n- [What generated tests cover](#what-generated-tests-cover)\n- [Migrations, drift and rollback](#migrations-drift-and-rollback)\n- [Backup and restore](#backup-and-restore)\n- [Docker, Kubernetes and reverse proxies](#docker-kubernetes-and-reverse-proxies)\n- [Production environment requirements](#production-environment-requirements)\n- [Real-service acceptance](#real-service-acceptance)\n- [Production verification checklist](#production-verification-checklist)\n- [Common failure modes](#common-failure-modes)\n- [Release acceptance (maintainers)](#release-acceptance-maintainers)\n\n## Generated workspace and scripts\n\nStandalone `create`/`generate` produces a Turborepo + Bun workspace; `init` mounts the two packages into an existing Bun workspace under the configured aliases.\n\n```text\nmy-admin/\n├── apps/\n│   ├── server/   bun + Elysia API, Drizzle schema/repositories/services/routes/auth/storage, tests/\n│   └── web/      Refine + React Router SPA, app/{routes,components,hooks,providers,ui,extensions}, tests/\n├── deploy/       nginx.conf, vercel.json, kubernetes/{deployment,service,pvc,secret.example}, observability/grafana\n├── Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, turbo.json, package.json\n└── .qiy-generated.json\n```\n\nRoot scripts (exact names from a generated project):\n\n| Script | Command | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `dev` | `turbo run dev` | Run server + web together |\n| `dev:server` / `dev:web` | per-package dev | Run one side |\n| `build` | `turbo run build` | Build both packages |\n| `preview` | server preview | Local demo server (loopback only, in-memory repository) |\n| `test` | `turbo run test` | Server + web tests |\n| `typecheck` | `turbo run typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` in both packages |\n| `db:generate` / `db:migrate` | Drizzle generate + generated migration runner | Local schema/migration |\n| `db:migrate:production` | generated runner with `.env.production` | Production migration with locking |\n\nServer-package scripts: `dev`, `start`, `preview`, `test`, `typecheck`, `db:generate`, `db:migrate`, `db:migrate:production`, `db:rollback`, `db:backup`, `db:restore`, `db:check`, `attachments:cleanup`, `attachments:orphans`, `auth:bootstrap-admin`, `auth:set-password`, `realtime:admin`. Web-package scripts: `dev`, `build`, `typecheck`, `test`.\n\n`preview` binds only to loopback and keeps data in memory. It is a local demo, never a deployment target.\n\n## Verification pipeline\n\nRun in this order inside the generated workspace:\n\n```bash\nbun install\nbun run typecheck\nbun run test\nbun run build\n# optional local smoke\nbun run preview\n```\n\nThen, before any deployment claim: apply migrations to a real database, start the server with production-like env, probe `/api/v1/health`, verify anonymous requests are 401, and exercise one list/create/update/delete plus one command and one file upload with real credentials. A green `typecheck`/`test`/`build` proves structure and generated behavior, not your database, IdP, S3 bucket, backups, concurrency or browser flows.\n\n| Check | Proves | Does not prove |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `qiy create` / `qiy init` succeeds | Model and packages were generated | Runtime, database, identity, storage or business correctness |\n| `bun run typecheck` | Generated TypeScript is structurally valid | Transactions, authorization, real queries |\n| `bun test` | Included tests pass in their configured environment | Real PostgreSQL/MySQL, IdP, S3, concurrency, rollback |\n| `bun run build` | The build pipeline completes | Production health |\n| `preview` opens | The local demo path works | Public exposure, durable data, secrets, multi-replica safety |\n| Generated scenario tests | Dataflow authorization/isolation after principal injection | Real login/token verification, browser flows |\n\n## What generated tests cover\n\nThe generated `apps/server/tests/` and `apps/web/tests/` suites scale with the model and enabled features. Typical coverage (file names vary by model):\n\n- Server: per-resource CRUD/contract tests, pagination, filtering, distribution/trend/aggregate, GraphQL schema and queries, `dataflow.test.ts` (success, permission denial, idempotent replay/conflict, rollback, audit, outbox), `generated-values.test.ts`, `data-scope.test.ts`, `permissions.test.ts`, `auth.test.ts`, `local-auth.test.ts`, `hybrid-auth.test.ts`, `api-keys.test.ts`, `storage.test.ts`, `storage-metadata.test.ts`, `realtime.test.ts`, `realtime-admin.test.ts`, `realtime-outbox-transaction.test.ts`, `saved-views.test.ts`, `docs.test.ts`, `schema-drift.test.ts`, `backup-codec.test.ts`, `bins.test.ts`.\n- Web: `data-provider.test.ts`, `auth.test.ts`, `menu-tree.test.ts`, `column-visibility.test.ts`, `field-rules.test.ts`, `display-template.test.ts`, `relation-batch.test.ts`, `relation-options.test.ts`, `download-file.test.ts`, `export.test.ts`, `views.test.ts`, `i18n.test.ts`, `model-i18n.test.ts`, `chrome-i18n.test.ts`, `project-messages.test.ts`, `charts.test.ts`, `charts-render.test.tsx`, `features.test.ts`, `api-docs.test.ts`, `api-docs-render.test.tsx`, `api-keys.test.ts`, `api-keys-render.test.tsx`, `audit-provider.test.ts`, `tree.test.ts`, `date-fields.test.ts`, `generated-fields.test.ts`, `live-provider.test.ts`, `sider-state.test.ts`, `record-details.test.tsx`, `relation-cell.test.tsx`, `actions.test.ts`.\n- `app.test.qiy` scenarios compile into `apps/server/tests/qiy-scenarios.test.ts`; run them in the server package. See [dataflows-actions.md](dataflows-actions.md) for grammar, database requirements and isolation rules.\n- Realtime tests force `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED=1` so they do not depend on Ably; they are not real-provider acceptance.\n- Hybrid/OIDC tests inject principals and tokens; they do not perform a real browser login.\n\n## Migrations, drift and rollback\n\n`db:migrate` and `db:migrate:production` run the generated `src/db-migrate.ts` rather than calling Drizzle directly:\n\n1. **Concurrency guard**: PostgreSQL holds `pg_advisory_lock` on a dedicated connection; MySQL uses `GET_LOCK('qiy_migrate', 60)`. With multiple replicas, only one migrates and the rest wait and reuse the result. SQLite has no cross-process lock - run migrations from exactly one process (the script prints this warning).\n2. **Post-migration drift check**: after migrating, the same comparison as `db:check` runs; a mismatch exits 1 with `drift: ...`. \"Migration ran\" does not mean the schema is correct.\n3. **Ledger output**: prints applied counts before and after.\n\nRollback is a reviewed operation; Qiy does not guess reverse SQL:\n\n```powershell\n# 1) Write and review drizzle/down/<tag>.sql (tag from drizzle/meta/_journal.json)\n#    Separate multiple statements with --> statement-breakpoint\n# 2) Execute\nbun run --cwd apps/<server-alias> db:rollback -- --confirm\n```\n\n- Without `--confirm` the command refuses to run.\n- If the latest applied migration has no `drizzle/down/<tag>.sql`, it refuses and prints the exact path to create.\n- Reverse SQL runs in one transaction and deletes that migration's ledger row; any failure rolls back.\n- After rolling back, revert the corresponding `src/schema.ts`/generated code changes and confirm with `db:check`.\n\nDrift check:\n\n```bash\nbun run --cwd apps/<server-alias> db:check\n```\n\nIt compares actual tables/columns (`NULL`/`NOT NULL`, primary keys, type classes) with `src/schema.ts`, tolerates known storage equivalences (SQLite affinity, MySQL `tinyint(1)` booleans), reports indeterminate columns as `unverified` (never a false drift), and prints `migrations applied X/Y`. `Y > X` is an error (unapplied migrations); `X > Y` is a warning (database newer than code). Exit 1 means drift or unapplied migrations.\n\n## Backup and restore\n\n```powershell\nbun run --cwd apps/<server-alias> db:backup\nbun run --cwd apps/<server-alias> db:restore -- --file backups/qiy-<timestamp>.json --confirm\n```\n\n- `db:backup` writes one JSON file ordered by foreign-key dependencies (`--out-dir`, `--out` allowed) and keeps the newest `QIY_BACKUP_RETENTION` files (default 7; `0` disables cleanup; invalid values fail closed).\n- `db:restore` requires both `--file` and `--confirm`; it refuses when the backup `dialect` or table set does not match `src/schema.ts`, empties tables in reverse dependency order and inserts in forward order inside one transaction - a replace, not an append.\n- `createdAt`/`Date`, binary columns and bigints are tagged with `$qiy` for lossless round-trips (generated `apps/server/tests/backup-codec.test.ts`).\n- This is a **logical** backup for small/medium data and pre-migration restore points, not disaster recovery and not DDL. Use `pg_dump`/`mysqldump` or storage snapshots for large databases. `backups/` is gitignored because it contains production data.\n\n## Docker, Kubernetes and reverse proxies\n\nDocker/Compose use `apps/<server-alias>/.env.production` (default alias `server`); `init` projects keep the alias path and never touch host `.env*` files.\n\n```powershell\ncd out/erpadmin\ndocker compose build\ndocker compose up\n```\n\nContainer startup pattern: `bun src/db-migrate.ts && bun src/server.ts`. Health endpoint `/api/v1/health` returns 200; anonymous API requests return 401; wrong credentials return 4xx.\n\nKubernetes manifests: `deploy/kubernetes/{deployment,service,persistent-volume-claim,secret.example}.yaml`. The PVC is `ReadWriteOnce` (a default storage class satisfies it) and the Deployment sets `HOST=0.0.0.0`. Replace the image with your registry and create the Secret from `secret.example.yaml` (`DATABASE_URL`, `QIY_AUTH_SECRET` >= 32 chars, `QIY_STORAGE_*`).\n\nNginx: forward `/api/` and `/graphql` to the server, and fall back all other paths to `index.html` (the SPA uses browser routing, not hash routing).\n\nOther targets: `deploy/vercel.json` for Vercel; AWS via the Dockerfile + ECR/ECS; generic hosts run `bun run build` (Node 20+ can build) and Bun for the server.\n\n## Production environment requirements\n\n| Requirement | Why |\n| --- | --- |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | Real database; SQLite is single-writer and unsuitable for multi-replica production |\n| `QIY_DEV_MODE=0` | Production gate; no-auth apps refuse to start, and OTP dev codes/verbose errors are disabled |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET` (>= 32 chars) | Sessions, OTP challenges, onboarding tokens, API-key pepper; rotation invalidates all sessions and keys |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` | In-memory attachment metadata loses ownership across restarts/replicas and fails the production startup check |\n| `QIY_S3_*` (when `provider s3`) | Bucket, region, endpoint, credentials; server only |\n| `QIY_ABLY_API_KEY` (when realtime) | Server only; the browser receives short-lived subscribe-only tokens |\n| `QIY_CORS_ORIGINS` (when cross-origin) | Exact origins including ports; wildcards are rejected |\n| `HTTPS_PROXY` / `HTTP_PROXY` / `NO_PROXY` | Bun `fetch` proxy for IdP token endpoints in restricted networks |\n| Reverse-proxy TLS, SPA fallback, API forwarding | Browser routing and secure cookies/headers |\n\nNever put secrets in `.qiy`; they belong in generated `.env` files, secret managers and deployment manifests. Do not expose `QIY_S3_*`, `QIY_ABLY_API_KEY`, `QIY_AUTH_SECRET` or `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_CLIENT_SECRET` to the browser.\n\n## Real-service acceptance\n\nThese repository scripts prove protocol shape and, in some cases, real tenants. They are starting points: passing them does not mean your environment is accepted.\n\n| Area | Command | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| OIDC protocol (Docker fixture) | `bun run tools/verify-oidc-docker.ts --isolated` | HTTPS discovery/JWKS/token, `iss|sub` mapping, 401 paths |\n| Dex (real IdP, local) | `bun run tools/verify-dex.ts` | Real issuer/JWKS; wrong audience and unmapped subject rejected |\n| Keycloak | `bun run tools/verify-keycloak.ts` | Realm import, audience mapper, flattened tenant claim. Keycloak nests dotted claims (`tenant.customerId` -> object) while Qiy projects scalar claims only - use flat claim names |\n| Vendor tenants | `verify-okta.ts`, `verify-auth0.ts`, `verify-google.ts`, `verify-kinde.ts`, `verify-azure-b2c.ts`, `verify-azure-b2c-browser.ts` | Phase A discovery/JWKS/PKCE; Phase B needs tenant credentials or a browser |\n| Ably | `bun run tools/verify-ably.ts` | Real publish/history, subscribe-only capability, viewer 403; skips (exit 0) without `QIY_ABLY_API_KEY` |\n| S3 storage | `bun run tools/verify-s3-storage.ts`, `tools/verify-s3-acceptance.ts` | Real bucket upload/download/presign/ownership |\n| Resumable uploads | `bun run tools/verify-resumable-upload.ts` | Offset rules, complete, failure recovery |\n| Attachment cleanup | `bun run tools/verify-orphan-cleanup.ts` | Orphan and missing-object directions |\n| PostgreSQL/MySQL dataflow | `bun run tools/verify-postgres-dataflow.ts`, `tools/verify-mysql-dataflow.ts` | Real transactions, locking, rollback |\n| orderInventory workflow | `bun run tools/verify-postgres-erp.ts qiy-erp-pg` | Reservation/release/deduction, idempotency, tenant denial |\n| Realtime outbox | `bun run tools/verify-realtime-outbox.ts <dialect>`, `verify-realtime-claim.ts`, `verify-realtime-policy.ts` | Lease/SKIP LOCKED/backoff/dead letter, claim channels, mask trimming |\n| Multi-replica | `bun run tools/verify-multi-replica.ts` | Import/export job claiming across replicas |\n| Saved views / scope / policies | `verify-saved-views.ts`, `verify-scope-policy.ts`, `verify-org-scope.ts`, `verify-policy-expression.ts`, `verify-policy-or.ts`, `verify-resource-policy.ts` | Cross-tenant and expression semantics |\n| Container/Kubernetes deploy | `bun run tools/verify-docker-deploy.ts`, `tools/verify-k8s-deploy.ts` | Build image, migrate, health probe, 401 probe, PVC/service |\n| Migration ops / backup | `bun run tools/verify-migration-ops.ts`, `tools/verify-backup-restore.ts`, `verify-db-check.ts` | Locking, drift, rollback, restore |\n\nDocker-based database/IdP fixtures need a local Docker daemon. Browser flows (PKCE, silent renewal, multi-tab) need a real browser; Qiy ships no browser automation.\n\n## Production verification checklist\n\nBefore saying \"ready to deploy\", verify in the target environment:\n\n1. **Database**: dialect, extensions, migrations applied, `db:check` clean, indexes present, transaction/rollback behavior, concurrent writes, backup and restore rehearsed, retention policy.\n2. **Identity**: the real issuer/audience/JWKS, redirect/logout allowlists, JWKS rotation, claim mapping, session lifetime, role change propagation, tenant scope, onboarding/bind/unbind, and for OTP the delivery adapter, its rate limits, replay resistance and failure behavior.\n3. **Policy**: effective permissions per role (`/api/v1/auth/permissions`), verification boundaries, `restrict` row/mask behavior on list/detail/export/realtime, `pages` 403s, `allow` denials, and that command resources have no `restrict` block.\n4. **Storage**: bucket/permissions, upload size/MIME modes, signed URL TTL, ownership 404s, orphan/missing-object cleanup, retention, failure recovery.\n5. **Realtime**: real Ably capability is subscribe-only, claim channels segment tenants, masked fields are absent, dead letters/health/metrics alerting wired, replay audited.\n6. **API contract**: generated endpoints against the real web build, host adapters (integration mode), CORS, CSV import/export limits, saved views.\n7. **Operations**: TLS, SPA fallback, health checks, secrets injection/rotation, logging without secrets, metrics/alerts, backups, rollback runbook, multi-replica safety (storage metadata database, migration lock, realtime lease, import/export job claiming).\n\nAnything outside CRUD (connector authorization, queues, token encryption, revocation, audit policy, synchronization) belongs in domain services and must be tested independently. CRUD generation does not implement it.\n\n## Common failure modes\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Server exits at startup in production | No `auth` and `QIY_DEV_MODE` unset | Configure auth; never ship `QIY_DEV_MODE=1` |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET must be at least 32 characters` | Missing/short secret | Set 32+ chars from a secret manager |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database is required for production file metadata` | In-memory metadata in production | Set the variable and migrate |\n| Migration says applied but `db:check` reports `drift:` | Partial/manual schema change | Generate a corrective migration; never hand-edit applied SQL |\n| Concurrent replicas crash during migration | SQLite (no cross-process lock) or missing DB lock privileges | Migrate from one process; grant advisory/GET_LOCK privileges |\n| Rollback refuses | Missing `drizzle/down/<tag>.sql` or `--confirm` | Create/review reverse SQL; pass `--confirm` |\n| Restore refuses | Dialect/table-set mismatch or missing `--confirm` | Restore into a matching schema; pass both flags |\n| Export returns 400 `export.tooLarge` | Row cap (default 1000, `QIY_EXPORT_MAX_ROWS` 1..100000) | Narrow filters or raise the cap deliberately |\n| Import partially applied | Per-row writes with compensating delete; a failure returns 4xx | Inspect `import.*` error and the reported line; no partial rows remain |\n| Health 503 / dead letters grow | Ably or DB unavailable, retry cap exceeded | Check realtime health/dead endpoints, fix, replay |\n| Browser deep link 404 | Reverse proxy has no SPA fallback | `try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html` |\n| 401 on every cross-origin request | Missing exact CORS origin or token header | Configure `api { cors { ... } }`; allow `Authorization`, `Content-Type`, `Idempotency-Key`, `X-API-Key` |\n| IdP token exchange fails behind a proxy | Bun `fetch` cannot reach the token endpoint | Set `HTTPS_PROXY`/`HTTP_PROXY` |\n| `preview` works but production data is empty | Preview uses an in-memory repository | Migrate and start with the production env file |\n\n## Release acceptance (maintainers)\n\nRepository-level gate before a release (do not run a release from an application task):\n\n```powershell\nbun install\nbun run template:build\nbun run check\nbun test\nbun run docs:build\nbun run build:exe -- --all\n```\n\nStandalone black-box acceptance also starts the built preview server and checks the home page, static assets, SPA deep links, resource API, OpenAPI, unknown API 404s, and that a no-auth production entry refuses to start. Release artifacts are validated per platform (version, generation, clean install, typecheck/test/build, sync protection, offline skill) before a tag/release is created. Never create a duplicate tag for the same version.\n\n## Related references\n\n- [CLI workflows](cli-workflows.md) - create/init/generate, install, run, upgrade\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - attachment and outbox operations\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - identity, policy and security boundaries\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - scenario tests and command contracts\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - cross-area error table\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [deployment](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/deployment)\n- [real services acceptance](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/real-services)\n- [CLI and release](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/cli)\n- [project structure](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/project-structure)\n",
  "references/troubleshooting.md": "# Troubleshooting\n\nUse this file when something fails and you need the likely cause and exact fix. Find the symptom or error string, apply the fix, then re-run generation/typecheck/tests. Deeper explanations live in the area references linked per section.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/overview\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Validation and generation errors](#validation-and-generation-errors)\n- [Modeling errors](#modeling-errors)\n- [Auth and permission errors](#auth-and-permission-errors)\n- [Dataflow and command errors](#dataflow-and-command-errors)\n- [Storage and realtime errors](#storage-and-realtime-errors)\n- [CLI and workspace errors](#cli-and-workspace-errors)\n- [Build, test and CI failures](#build-test-and-ci-failures)\n- [Deployment failures](#deployment-failures)\n\n## Validation and generation errors\n\n| Error | Stage | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `Unexpected Qiy syntax at offset N` | Lexer | Unquoted `:`/`[`/`/`/`*`/`$`/non-ASCII, or an unsupported symbol | Quote the value; use only supported structure symbols ([language-reference.md](language-reference.md)) |\n| `Expected database near token N` | Parser | `database` is not the first declaration in `application` | Move it first |\n| `Expected <block> near token N` | Parser | Declaration order violated (enum after entity, menu after dashboard, ...) | Reorder per the declaration-order table |\n| `Expected <end> near token N` | Parser | Extra content after the application `}` or a missing brace | Check braces |\n| `Expected ; near token N` | Parser | Missing `;` on a declaration, or a `;` after a block `}` | Add/remove it |\n| `Expected value near token N` | Parser | Number/symbol where a string or identifier is required | Quote it or use an identifier |\n| `Unsupported field type X` | Parser | Not one of the 11 types + declared enums | Use `Text`/`Integer`/`Decimal`/... ([modeling-and-generation.md](modeling-and-generation.md)) |\n| `Unsupported field attribute @X` | Parser | Annotation not allowed on fields, or typo | Check the annotation inventory |\n| `duplicate ... annotation` | Parser | Same annotation twice where duplicates are rejected | Keep one |\n| `Missing default locale message for <purpose>: <key>` | Parser | `t(\"key\")` missing from the default locale, or `messages` declared too late | Add the key; move `messages` before enums/entities |\n| `Invalid message locale X: use a canonical BCP 47 language tag` | Parser | `fr_fr`, `FR-fr`, `en-us` | Use `fr-FR`, `en-US`, ... |\n| `Missing default message locale X` | Parser | `default` has no matching `locale` block | Add the block |\n| `Unsupported database dialect X` | Parser | Typo | `postgresql`/`mysql`/`sqlite` |\n| `Unsupported UI library mui; only antd is implemented` | Parser | Non-AntD UI library | `library antd;` |\n| `UI default theme X must be included in themes` | Parser | `theme` not in `themes` | Add it |\n| `Unsupported include selector ...` | Include | Selector other than `@messages`/`@message` | Include the whole fragment or use `@messages` |\n| `include path cannot contain ..` / `include path must be relative ...` | Include | Escaping the model directory | Keep fragments under the model root |\n| `Qiy include cycle detected: a -> b -> a` | Include | Cyclic includes | Break the cycle |\n| `Invalid Ant Design icon X` | Generation | Icon name is not `*Outlined` | Use an Ant Design icon name |\n| `X: V0 CRUD requires exactly one UUID primary key named id` | Generation | Missing/renamed/retyped PK | `field id UUID @id` |\n| `X: route path must be lowercase and URL-safe` | Generation | Uppercase/invalid `table` name | `^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$` |\n| `required field cannot be hidden from the create form` | Generation | Non-null field hidden by `@visible(false)`/`@formVisible(false)` | Add `@nullable` or keep it visible |\n| `V3 foreign keys require UUID fields` | IR | Non-UUID relation endpoint | Both endpoints `UUID` |\n| `only one-to-one/many-to-one foreign keys are supported` | IR | Relation cardinality `many` | Use `one`; model M2M with a join entity |\n| `target field must be primary or unique` | IR | Relation targets a non-unique field | Target the PK or add `@unique` |\n| `setNull requires a nullable source field` | IR | `@onDelete(setNull)` on a non-null FK | Add `@nullable` |\n| `Vector requires PostgreSQL and a declared pgvector extension` | IR | Wrong dialect or missing extension | PostgreSQL + `extension pgvector;` + `@extension(pgvector)` |\n| `hnsw requires PostgreSQL and pgvector` | IR | Vector index on another dialect | PostgreSQL + pgvector |\n| `Files cannot be a primary key` / `Files cannot be unique` | IR | `Files` used as PK/unique | Use `File` or a scalar key |\n| `duplicate entity or table name` | IR | Repeated include or name collision | Include once; unique names |\n| `X: duplicate @singular annotation` | Parser | Duplicate display annotation | Keep one |\n| `... cannot interpolate foreign key field X` | Generation | Display template references an FK source | Reference the target's scalar field |\n| `Output directory must be empty` | CLI | Non-empty target without `--sync` | New directory, or `--sync` on a Qiy-generated workspace |\n\n## Modeling errors\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Foreign key filled with a random UUID at create | No `relation` declared, so the UUID is treated as a system value | Declare `relation` |\n| `@code requires a Text field without an enum` | `@code` on UUID/enum | Use a non-enum `Text` field |\n| `@generated(uuid) requires a UUID field` | `@generated` on Text | Use `@code` or a UUID field |\n| `@code and @generated cannot be combined` | Both on one field | Keep one |\n| `the pattern needs {seq}, {count+1}, {random:…} or {uuid}` | Code template has no uniqueness token | Add `{seq:N}` or `{random:N}` |\n| `unknown token {X}` | Typo in a code template | Use only documented tokens |\n| `QIY_CODE_TIMEZONE is not a valid IANA timezone` | Bad env value | Use `Asia/Shanghai`, etc. |\n| Create returns 409 `generated.conflict` | Five uniqueness retries exhausted | Raise template entropy/width |\n| `Field type Text has no parameters` | Parentheses on a non-parameterized type | Remove them; enforce length in migrations/business code |\n| `Unsupported field attribute @required` | Fields have no `@required` | Required is default; use `@nullable` |\n| `dimension requires Vector` / `precision and scale require Decimal or Money` | Annotation/type mismatch | Match the annotation to the type |\n| Chart/label/menu errors | See [ui-charts-i18n.md](ui-charts-i18n.md) | - |\n\n## Auth and permission errors\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Auth: roleField must be an enum with admin, operator and viewer values` | Role enum has extra/missing values | Declare exactly those three |\n| `Auth: usernameField must be a required unique Text field` | Column contract violated | Make it non-null, unique, Text |\n| `Auth: passwordField must be a nullable Text field ...` | Hash column not nullable | Make it `@nullable` Text |\n| `Auth: subjectField must be a required unique Text field` | Missing/duplicate subject | Non-null unique Text |\n| `Auth: provider X subjectField Y must be nullable` | Per-provider identity column not nullable | `@nullable` + `@unique` |\n| `Auth: OAuth onboarding cannot populate required user fields: ...` | Required columns other than the auto-filled ones | Make them nullable |\n| `Auth accepts either provider or providers, not both` | Both keys used | Keep one |\n| `Auth providers cannot include otp` | `otp` inside `providers` | Use `provider otp;` |\n| `Auth provider local requires usernameField and passwordField` | Local login incomplete | Add both |\n| `Permission declarations require a generated auth block` | `permission` without `auth` | Add `auth` or remove permissions |\n| `Permission declarations require at least one permission field` | Only groups/verifications | Declare a `permission field` |\n| `provider is not a configured OAuth/OIDC provider` | Claim source provider missing | Add it to `providers` |\n| `local and otp sessions do not carry claims` | Claim source uses local/otp | Use a database column instead |\n| `Data scope claim org.id needs a matching field on users (expected orgId)` | Local/hybrid scope claim has no users column | Add `orgId` |\n| `Missing required data scope claim: <claim>` (403) | Principal lacks the claim | Use OIDC, add the users column, or use an API key |\n| `Restrict X: row conditions cannot target primary key id` | Row predicate on the PK | Use a non-PK column |\n| `Restrict X: row condition on nullable field Y is not supported` | Claim predicate on nullable column | Use a non-null column or `mask` |\n| `Restrict X: > on amount must compare two fields` | Literal used with `>`/`<` | Literals only with `==`/`!=`/`in`/`notIn` |\n| `Restrict X: mask mode redact for Y requires a replacement string` | Missing replacement | Add `replacement \"***\"` |\n| `Restrict X: dataflow Y cannot use a restricted resource ...` | Command touches any resource with a `restrict` block | Remove the resource from the command or drop `restrict` |\n| `when scope requires a matching scope declaration` | `scope` atom without `scope` | Declare `scope` for that resource |\n| `Page access denied` (403) | `pages` disallows the action | Adjust `pages`; export uses `list`, import writes use `create` |\n| Login page has no provider buttons | Provider env block incomplete | Fill `QIY_OIDC_<ID>_ISSUER/AUDIENCE/JWKS_URL/AUTHORIZATION_URL/CLIENT_ID` |\n| 401 immediately after login | Token `iss` differs from the configured issuer | Use the discovery issuer verbatim |\n| `State mismatch in the provider callback` | Concurrent logins or cleared sessionStorage | Log in again |\n| `The provider token exchange failed` | Redirect mismatch, missing secret, unreachable token endpoint | Align redirect/secret; set `HTTPS_PROXY` |\n| Onboarding 409 | Username/email exists or identity belongs to another account | Change username or bind from the original account |\n| Unbind 409 | Last login method | Set a password or bind another provider |\n| OTP 502 `auth.otpDeliveryFailed` | Delivery adapter unreachable/non-2xx/non-HTTPS | Fix `QIY_OTP_DELIVERY_URL`, token, timeout |\n| API key 401 | Revoked/expired | Re-issue |\n| `At most 10 active API keys are allowed` (409) | Key limit | Revoke unused keys |\n| `QIY_AUTH_SECRET must be at least 32 characters` | Missing/short secret | 32+ chars in a secret manager |\n\n## Dataflow and command errors\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Dataflow X requires input, context, and result blocks` | Missing block (even empty) | Write `input {}`, `context {}` |\n| `result must return a declared context binding` | Returned an undeclared name | Return a context/create binding |\n| 400 `A valid Idempotency-Key header is required` | Flow requires idempotency, no key sent | Send the header; generated actions do it |\n| 409 idempotency body mismatch | Same key, different body | Use a new key for a new request |\n| `cannot update scope field` | Command writes a scope column | Scope derives from the principal |\n| `cannot update password field` | Command writes the auth password hash | Remove it |\n| `create requires value for <entity>.<field>` | Non-null field not assigned | Assign it or make it `@nullable` |\n| `create primary key ... is generated automatically` | Assigning `id` in `create` | Remove the assignment |\n| `literal updates currently support Text and enum fields only` | Literal used for Integer/Decimal/Date | Use a matching `input.<f>` or `call` |\n| `require comparisons support Text, enum and Integer fields only` | Compared Decimal/Boolean/Date | Validate in a `call` adapter or redesign |\n| `require input must be @required` | Optional input used in `require` | Mark it `@required` |\n| `context bindings must declare @required ...` | Missing `@required` on a context binding | Add it |\n| 404 `Not found` + `resource` | Context record missing or out of scope | Check the id and data scope |\n| 403 `command.forbidden` | `allow permission`/`allow verification` denied | Inspect `/auth/me` permissions/groups |\n| `call` always 409 | Extension handler still fail-closed | Implement it in `extensions/dataflow-calls.ts` and return `{ ok: true }` |\n| Batch 400 `Batch item identifiers must be unique` | Duplicate IDs | Deduplicate |\n| Batch action rejected | Missing `batch true`, idempotency, list-only placement, or a `when` | Follow batch constraints |\n| GraphQL mutation missing `idempotencyKey` | Flow requires idempotency | Pass the argument |\n| Button not rendered | `when` mismatch, `CanAccess` denial, missing permission metadata | Check record, role, `/auth/me` |\n| Manual page overwritten by `--sync` | Code outside `app/extensions/` | Move it into `app/extensions/` |\n\n## Storage and realtime errors\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Upload 415 | MIME not allowed, or `@upload` disallows the encoding | Adjust field/request |\n| Upload 403 | Caller is `viewer` | Use admin/operator |\n| Upload 409 `Storage key already exists` | Duplicate key | Generate a unique key |\n| `Invalid storage key` (400) | Illegal segments or > 240 chars | Use `resource/<uuid>/<name>` |\n| Download 404 | Not owner/admin, or metadata missing | Use the uploader account; `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` |\n| Files unreadable after restart | In-memory metadata | Set `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` and migrate |\n| `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database is required for production file metadata` | Production startup check | Fix `.env.production` |\n| Upload succeeded but field empty | Key must be written to the entity | Let the form do it, or PATCH the key |\n| Signed URL `null` | `local` provider has no presigning | Use the protected download endpoint |\n| Orphan scan removes nothing | Dry-run default | Add `--apply` |\n| `Realtime requires generated authentication` | No `auth` | Add `auth` |\n| `Realtime X: restrict row predicates cannot be enforced on a shared channel` | Row predicate + realtime | Remove the predicate or realtime |\n| `a claim-scoped channel already isolates rows; remove the restrict row predicates` | Both isolation styles | Keep the claim channel |\n| `claim field X must be non-nullable` | `when` field nullable | Make it non-null |\n| `/api/v1/realtime/token` 403 | Missing claim for a segmented channel | Add the claim or drop `when` |\n| `/token` 503 `Realtime is disabled` | `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED=1` | Unset it |\n| Dead letters grow | Ably unreachable/wrong key/retry cap | Check health/dead, fix, replay |\n| Page receives no events | Role not allowed or capability/channel mismatch | Check `roles`, claims, token capability |\n| Events miss fields | A `mask` applies to a subscribable role | Adjust mask/roles |\n\n## CLI and workspace errors\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `qiy is not recognized` | Not on `PATH` | Add it, reopen the terminal |\n| `qiy init requires packageManager to declare Bun` | No Bun declaration in the host `package.json` | Add `\"packageManager\": \"bun@<version>\"` |\n| `Refusing to overwrite existing host file` | Alias/script collision | Change `workspace.aliases`/`name` |\n| `Unknown command: dev` | Qiy has no dev/build/deploy subcommand | Run `bun run dev` in the generated workspace |\n| `application mode integration requires an integration block` | `mode integration` without settings | Add `integration { apiBase ... }` |\n| `application mode integration must be mounted with qiy init ...` | Used `create`/`generate` | Run `qiy init` in the host |\n| `application mode integration cannot configure generated server features` | Server blocks in an integration model | Remove `auth`/`storage`/`env`/`dataflow`/... |\n| `integration apiBase must be an absolute http(s) URL or a path starting with /` | Relative `apiBase` | `/api/v2` or a full URL |\n| `Integration auth options are only supported for cookie transport` | `csrfCookie` outside `auth cookie` | Move it |\n| `integration tenant requires header and identity` | Half a tenant config | Provide both |\n| `Qiy skill has local changes` | Official skill files edited | `qiy skill install --force` |\n| `qiy skill install` writes to the wrong place | Legacy `.agent/skills/qiy` exists | Remove/rename it, or use `--dir` |\n\n## Build, test and CI failures\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `tsc --noEmit` errors in generated code after a model edit | Generated files out of sync with the model | Re-run generation/`--sync`, then typecheck |\n| Typecheck passes locally but CI installs a different dependency set | Generated `package.json` changed; lockfile stale | `bun install` in the generated workspace and commit the lockfile |\n| `bun test` scenario tests refuse to run | PostgreSQL/MySQL without `QIY_TEST_DATABASE_URL` (or not `qiy_test_*`) | Create/migrate a dedicated test DB and set both variables |\n| Scenario test wipes data | Tests clear model tables | Never point them at a business database |\n| Scenario test fails on FK cleanup | Cyclic foreign keys | Remove the cycle; generation rejects it too |\n| Realtime tests fail without Ably | They should force `QIY_REALTIME_DISABLED=1` | Do not set a real key in unit tests |\n| Snapshot/SSR tests fail without `window` | Code assumes browser APIs | Use the generated `useQiyUiOptional()`/SSR-safe helpers |\n| `preview` works, CI build fails | Preview uses an in-memory repository and dev env | Build with the production env requirements |\n| Docs/skill assets stale in CI | `bun run docs:assets`/`skill:build` not run | Run them and commit generated assets |\n| Release workflow skips | A Release already exists for that version | Do not recreate tags for an existing version |\n\n## Deployment failures\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Server exits at startup | No `auth` and `QIY_DEV_MODE` unset | Configure auth; never ship `QIY_DEV_MODE=1` |\n| Migration runs twice/fails under replicas | SQLite has no cross-process lock, or DB lock privilege missing | Migrate from one process; grant lock privileges |\n| `drift: <table>.<column>: ...` after deploy | Schema differs from `src/schema.ts` | Generate the missing migration; do not hand-edit applied SQL |\n| Rollback refuses | Missing `drizzle/down/<tag>.sql` or `--confirm` | Create/review reverse SQL; pass `--confirm` |\n| Restore refuses | Dialect/table-set mismatch or missing `--confirm` | Restore into a matching schema with both flags |\n| Browser deep link 404 | No SPA fallback | `try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html` |\n| Cross-origin 401 | CORS origin mismatch or auth headers not allowed | Exact origins including ports |\n| Exports 400 `export.tooLarge` | Row cap (`QIY_EXPORT_MAX_ROWS`) | Narrow filters or raise the cap deliberately |\n| Imports partially applied | Compensating delete on failure | Fix the reported line; no partial rows remain |\n| Health 503 after deploy | DB/Ably unavailable or realtime thresholds exceeded | Check DB connectivity, realtime health/dead endpoints |\n| S3 upload works locally, fails in cluster | Local storage on one replica | Use `s3` or a shared volume; `QIY_STORAGE_METADATA=database` |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - syntax and declaration order\n- [Modeling and generation](modeling-and-generation.md) - modeling errors\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - 401/403 and policy errors\n- [Dataflows and actions](dataflows-actions.md) - command errors\n- [Storage and realtime](storage-realtime.md) - upload and outbox errors\n- [CLI workflows](cli-workflows.md) - CLI/workspace errors\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - CI and production failures\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [DSL overview and common errors](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/overview)\n- [application errors](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/application)\n- [permissions](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/permissions)\n- [deployment](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/deployment)\n",
  "references/ui-charts-i18n.md": "# UI, charts, menus and i18n\n\nUse this file when you change look-and-feel, navigation, the overview page, charts, or any user-visible text. It covers `ui`, `menu`, legacy `dashboard`, `chart`/`chart panels`, `messages`/i18n keys, and the persistence keys the generated admin uses.\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/charts (`/guide/ui-theming`, `/guide/menu-dashboard`, `/dsl/i18n`)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [ui block](#ui-block)\n- [Themes, color mode and persistence](#themes-color-mode-and-persistence)\n- [Menu](#menu)\n- [Legacy dashboard metrics](#legacy-dashboard-metrics)\n- [chart grammar](#chart-grammar)\n- [chart data mini-language](#chart-data-mini-language)\n- [labels](#labels)\n- [chart panels](#chart-panels)\n- [Chart behavior, theme and limits](#chart-behavior-theme-and-limits)\n- [messages and i18n](#messages-and-i18n)\n- [Derived keys and fallback chain](#derived-keys-and-fallback-chain)\n- [Generated system pages](#generated-system-pages)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## ui block\n\n`ui` sits after `workspace` and before `api` inside `application`.\n\n```text\nui {\n  library antd;\n  theme <blue|purple|green|orange|red>;\n  themes <key>, <key>, ...;\n  colorMode <light|dark|system>;\n  allowThemeSwitch <true|false>;\n  allowColorModeSwitch <true|false>;\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\nui {\n  library antd;\n  theme purple;\n  themes purple, blue, green, orange;\n  colorMode system;\n  allowThemeSwitch true;\n  allowColorModeSwitch true;\n}\n```\n\n| Setting | Values | Default | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `library` | `antd` only | `antd` | `mui`/`mantine`/`chakra` fail with `Unsupported UI library X; only antd is implemented` |\n| `theme` | five keys | first of `themes`, else `blue` | Initial brand color; must be included in `themes` |\n| `themes` | comma list, >= 1 | all five | Header theme candidates; only one key hides the selector |\n| `colorMode` | `light`, `dark`, `system` | `system` | Initial mode; `system` follows `prefers-color-scheme` |\n| `allowThemeSwitch` | boolean | `true` | Render the theme control |\n| `allowColorModeSwitch` | boolean | `true` | Render the light/dark/system control |\n\nRules: each setting at most once (`Duplicate UI setting X`), unknown keys rejected, trailing comma in `themes` is invalid, `theme` not in `themes` fails with `UI default theme X must be included in themes`.\n\nTheme registry (`colorPrimary` only; `borderRadius: 6` is fixed):\n\n| key | Color | Copy override key |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `blue` | `#1677ff` | `qiy.themeBlue` |\n| `purple` | `#722ed1` | `qiy.themePurple` |\n| `green` | `#389e0d` | `qiy.themeGreen` |\n| `orange` | `#d46b08` | `qiy.themeOrange` |\n| `red` | `#cf1322` | `qiy.themeRed` |\n\nThere is no free-form `primaryColor` and no sixth theme key. For a custom brand color, pick the closest key or override `colorPrimary` in a host wrapper.\n\n## Themes, color mode and persistence\n\nResolution: `resolvedColorMode = colorMode === \"system\" ? (prefersDark ? \"dark\" : \"light\") : colorMode`. It selects the Ant Design `darkAlgorithm` or `defaultAlgorithm` and sets `<html data-theme>`, `<html data-color-mode>` and inline `color-scheme`. `system` listens for `prefers-color-scheme` changes.\n\nlocalStorage keys (all reads are wrapped in try/catch and degrade silently in private mode/quota errors):\n\n| Storage | Key | Value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| localStorage | `qiy.ui.theme` | theme key (only if valid and in `themes`) |\n| localStorage | `qiy.ui.color-mode` | `light`/`dark`/`system` |\n| localStorage | `qiy.ui.sider-collapsed` | `collapsed`/`expanded` |\n| localStorage | `qiy.locale` | BCP 47 tag |\n| localStorage | `qiy.charts.panel` | selected panel name |\n| localStorage | `qiy.columns.<resource>` | `{ fields, selected }` JSON |\n| localStorage | `qiy.access_token` | session JWT |\n| localStorage | `qiy.id_token`, `qiy.expires_at` | OIDC id token/expiry |\n| sessionStorage | `qiy.oidc.verifier`, `qiy.oidc.state`, `qiy.oidc.return_to`, `qiy.oidc.silent_attempt` | PKCE intermediate state |\n\nTheme and color mode are written on every mount, so changing the model default does not affect users who already have a stored value. Clearing browser storage resets theme, color mode, language, sider, panel and column preferences.\n\nDo not hand-edit `app/ui/theme-config.ts`, `app/ui/index.tsx` or `app/styles.css` for a long-lived change: they are manifest-owned and `--sync` rewrites them. Use the `ui` block, host-level wrapping, or unowned extension components. Do not override `.ant-btn-primary` colors with CSS; the dark algorithm and `data-theme` derive many shades.\n\n## Menu\n\n```text\nmenu {\n  group <name>\n    [@label(\"...\")] [@icon(IconName)] [@parent(<group>)] [@comment(\"...\" | t(\"key\"))] {\n    resource <tableName>;\n    ...\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\nmenu {\n  group masterData @label(\"Master data\") @icon(AppstoreOutlined) {\n    resource suppliers;\n    resource customers;\n    resource products;\n  }\n  group sales @label(\"Sales\") @icon(ShoppingOutlined) @parent(masterData) @comment(\"Sales entry points\") {\n    resource orders;\n    resource order_lines;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Values | Default | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| group name | unique identifier | required | Group key (`menu-<name>`) and `qiy.menu.<name>.label` |\n| `@label` | string | group name | Sidebar title |\n| `@icon` | `*Outlined` | `AppstoreOutlined` | Group icon (visible when collapsed) |\n| `@parent(<group>)` | declared group | none | Nested submenu; unknown parent or cycle rejected |\n| `@comment` | doc | none | Metadata |\n| `resource <tableName>` | entity table name, repeatable | required (>=1) | Order within the group |\n\nRules: at most one `menu` in the application; only `group` inside; a resource appears in at most one group; unknown resources fail (`Menu group X: unknown resource Y`). Without a `menu`, every resource becomes a flat root menu. Resources not listed in any group are appended at root. A group whose children are all filtered out by permissions is not rendered. System pages (`features`) are linked under a default `System` group with the overview entry `qiy-overview` first.\n\nSidebar behavior: expanded width 248px, collapsed shows icons with tooltips, collapsed state persisted, the active route's group opens by default, and mobile uses a drawer.\n\n## Legacy dashboard metrics\n\n```text\ndashboard {\n  metric <name> <resource>\n    [@label(\"...\")] [@icon(IconName)] [@span(8|12|24)]\n    [@type(<count|distribution|trend|aggregate>)]\n    [@groupBy(<field>)] [@days(<1..365>)]\n    [@field(<field>)] [@agg(<sum|avg|min|max>)]\n    [@comment(\"...\" | t(\"key\"))]\n    ;\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\ndashboard {\n  metric orderCount orders @label(\"Orders\") @span(8) @comment(t(\"dashboard.orders\"));\n  metric orderStatus orders @label(\"Status\") @span(8) @type(distribution) @groupBy(status);\n  metric orderTrend orders @label(\"Last 30 days\") @span(24) @type(trend) @groupBy(createdAt) @days(30);\n  metric orderAmount orders @label(\"Amount\") @span(8) @type(aggregate) @field(amount) @agg(sum);\n}\n```\n\n| Type | Generated content | Validation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `count` | Total count card, links to the list | - |\n| `distribution` | Enum distribution bars using value labels/comments | `distribution requires an enum groupBy field` |\n| `trend` | Daily trend for `@days` (1..365) | `trend requires a DateTime groupBy field`; `days must be between 1 and 365` |\n| `aggregate` | Numeric statistic | `aggregate requires a numeric field`; `aggregate requires agg sum, avg, min or max` |\n\n`@span` is only 8/12/24; `@field`/`@agg` are only valid on `aggregate`; `@days` only on `trend`; `@groupBy` is ignored on other types. Cards are wrapped in `CanAccess`, so resources the user cannot list are hidden. Prefer `chart` for new models.\n\nHome page fallback:\n\n| Model | Overview page |\n| --- | --- |\n| `dashboard` block | Declared metric cards |\n| No `dashboard` and no `chart` | One `count` metric per entity (`span 8`, entity label/icon) |\n| No `dashboard`, has `chart` | No metrics; chart panels render |\n| Both | Charts render; dashboard metrics do not |\n\n## chart grammar\n\n`chart` and `chart panels` are written after `menu` and before `dataflow`, sharing a slot with legacy `dashboard`.\n\n```text\nchart [const|pie|bar|line|table] <ChartName> {\n  icon  = \"<IconName>\" ;\n  title = \"<text>\" ;\n  data  = <data expression> ;\n  labels = <enumField> ;\n  labels [=] { <value> \"<text>\" ; ... } ;\n}\n\nchart panels <PanelName> {\n  title = \"<text>\" ;\n  grid <cols> <rows> ;\n  <ChartName> {\n    <variant> <x> <y> <w> <h> ;\n    ...\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nChart view properties are `key = value;`; a trailing `;` may be omitted only before `}`. `labels` is the exception: `labels { ... }`, `labels = { ... }` and `labels = role;` are all accepted. Always quote `icon`/`title` strings.\n\n| Property | Required | Values | Default | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| kind | no | `const`, `pie`, `bar`, `line`, `table` | `const` | Omitting kind produces a statistic card |\n| `icon` | no | Ant Design `*Outlined` | none | Card icon; see chart limits |\n| `title` | no | string | chart name | Chart-level title |\n| `data` | **yes** | data mini-language | - | Exactly once per declaration |\n| `labels` | no | enum field or mapping block | none | Only meaningful for `pie`/`bar`; silently ignored elsewhere |\n\nMulti-view semantics: declaring the same chart name with different kinds creates multiple views of one card, in declaration order; the first declaration is the default view. The same kind twice fails (`Chart <name>: duplicate <kind> view`), and two kind-less declarations both become `const` and collide. Chart-level `title`/`icon` come from the first view that declares them (not from the first view's whole attribute set). View title fallback: view `title` -> chart `title` -> chart name. The card header (icon/title) is chart-level and does not change when switching views; the view title appears inside the card.\n\n## chart data mini-language\n\n| `data` expression | Allowed kind | Generated request | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `count <entity>` | `const` | list `page=1&pageSize=1`, use `total` | Single count |\n| `sum\\|avg\\|min\\|max <entity>.<field>` | `const` | `GET /api/v1/<entity>/aggregate?field=&op=` | Numeric aggregate |\n| `count <entity> group by <enumField>` | `pie`/`bar` | `GET /api/v1/<entity>/distribution?field=` | Enum distribution |\n| `trend <entity>.<dateTimeField> days <1..365>` | `line` | `GET /api/v1/<entity>/trend?field=&days=` | Daily count trend |\n| `list <entity> columns <a>, <b>, ...` | `table` | list `page=1&pageSize=5` | Read-only first 5 rows |\n\n| Kind | Accepts | Rejects with |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `const` | ungrouped `count`; `sum`/`avg`/`min`/`max` | `count data cannot group by (use pie or bar)`, `const views require count or sum/avg/min/max data` |\n| `pie`/`bar` | `count <entity> group by <enum field>` | `pie/bar views require \"count <entity> group by <enum field>\" data` |\n| `line` | `trend` | `line views require \"trend <entity>.<DateTime field> days <n>\" data` |\n| `table` | `list` | `table views require \"list <entity> columns ...\" data` |\n\nValidation:\n\n- `<entity>` may be an entity name or table name; it normalizes to the table name in metadata/requests (`unknown entity`).\n- `<field>` is the entity field name, not a column name and without table prefix (`unknown field`).\n- `group by` must be an enum field (`group by field X must be an enum field`).\n- Aggregate fields must be `Integer`, `Decimal` or `Money` (`aggregate field X must be Integer, Decimal or Money`).\n- `trend` fields must be `DateTime`; `days` is 1..365 (`trend field X must be a DateTime field`, `days must be between 1 and 365`).\n- `list` needs at least one column; `Vector` columns cannot be rendered (`cannot render a Vector column (X)`).\n- `sum ... group by ...` is parsed but unsupported by every kind. Use `count ... group by`, a `table` view or an extension page.\n- Chart data goes through the same resource endpoints, so `scope`, `restrict`, `pages`, `mask` and role guards still apply. Charts never bypass data permissions.\n\n## labels\n\n`labels` affects only the numeric labels/legend of `pie`/`bar`, not counts.\n\n1. Without `labels`, pie/bar metadata auto-expands every enum value (label = enum value label, key `qiy.charts.<chart>.labels.<value>`).\n2. `labels = <enumField>` uses another enum field's value labels; it must be an enum field.\n3. `labels { ... }` lists explicit values only; unlisted values render the raw string.\n4. Runtime order: dictionary `qiy.charts.<chart>.labels.<value>` -> generated metadata label (explicit mapping or enum value label) -> raw value. The dictionary always wins.\n5. Keys are per chart name, not per view: `pie` and `bar` share the same label keys.\n6. `labels` on `const`/`line`/`table` is silently ignored.\n7. Empty mapping fails (`labels mapping needs at least one entry`); duplicate values fail; each entry needs a quoted string and `;`.\n\n## chart panels\n\n| Element | Required | Values | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `title` | no | string | Panel title; key `qiy.charts.<panel>.label`; duplicates silently overwrite |\n| `grid cols` | yes | 1..24 | CSS grid columns |\n| `grid rows` | yes | 1..200 | Grid row bound |\n| chart reference | yes (>=1) | declared chart name | Each reference needs >= 1 placement; no duplicate chart in one panel |\n| `<variant>` | yes (>=1) | see below | One placement per variant name |\n| `x`,`y` | yes | integer >= 0 | 0-based origin |\n| `w`,`h` | yes | integer >= 1 | Column/row span |\n\nResponsive variants:\n\n| Variants | Category | Viewport |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `larger`, `large`, `lg`, `xl` | larger | >= 1200px |\n| `medium`, `md` | medium | >= 768px |\n| `small`, `sm`, `xs` | small | < 768px |\n\nUnknown variants fail and list the full set. Same-name variants fail (`duplicate <variant> placement`); different aliases of the same category are accepted but only the **first declared** is used (later aliases are dead code). Prefer `larger`/`medium`/`small`.\n\nBounds: `x + w <= cols`, `y + h <= rows`, `x,y >= 0`, `w,h >= 1` (`placement larger exceeds 24 grid columns`, `grid rows must be between 1 and 200`). There is **no overlap detection**: two charts may occupy the same cells and will stack visually. `grid` is required exactly once. A panel needs at least one chart; a chart reference needs at least one placement; unknown/duplicate chart names fail. Chart and panel names share a namespace (`panels` is reserved).\n\nPanel selection: multiple panels render a selector in declaration order; the choice persists in `qiy.charts.panel`. A single panel hides the selector but still renders its title. A stored panel missing from the model falls back to `panels[0]`; unavailable localStorage falls back silently. The stored value is read on first mount, so SSR always renders `panels[0]` and hydration may visibly switch. Charts not referenced by any panel do not render. Without `chart panels`, all charts tile with `Row`/`Col` (`xs=24`, `lg=12`).\n\n## Chart behavior, theme and limits\n\nRendering: `const` uses Ant Design `Statistic` (count is localized; aggregates append `agg · field`; Money/Decimal use 2 decimals). `pie` is inline SVG with a legend; `bar` uses `Progress` rows; `line` is inline SVG with first/last dates and max; `table` is a read-only Ant Design `Table` (max 5 rows) linking to the resource list. No charting library is used, so SSR works.\n\nData views are wrapped in `CanAccess resource=<entity> action=\"list\"`; in panels mode the whole grid cell is wrapped too.\n\nTheme: cards, tables, text and controls follow Ant Design tokens, but **chart graphics do not**: the pie palette (`#1677ff`, `#52c41a`, `#faad14`, `#eb2f96`, `#722ed1`, `#13c2c2`, `#fa541c`, `#8c8c8c`) and the line color are hardcoded light values. They stay visible in dark mode but do not adapt.\n\nChart icons: use an Ant Design `*Outlined` name. Chart-level and per-view icons are collected into `qiyIcons` together with entity/field/enum/menu/metric icons. Generation validates only the `*Outlined` name shape (`Invalid Ant Design icon`); a name Ant Design does not export passes generation and then fails the generated project's typecheck/build. Theme colors are not applied to chart graphics.\n\nKnown chart limits to state explicitly: `labels` silently ignored on non-pie/bar; alias variants beyond the first are dead code; overlapping placements are not detected; `table` view titles are not displayed; charts do not theme their graphics; only the five view kinds exist.\n\nGenerated files: `apps/web/app/charts.ts`, `apps/web/app/components/charts.tsx`, `apps/web/app/routes/home.tsx`, `apps/web/app/dashboard.ts`, `apps/web/tests/charts.test.ts`, `apps/web/tests/charts-render.test.tsx`.\n\n## messages and i18n\n\n`messages` sits after `env` and before `permission`/`workflow`/`enum`/`entity`.\n\n```text\nmessages {\n  default \"<locale>\";\n  locale \"<locale>\" {\n    \"<key>\" \"<value>\";\n    ...\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n```qiy\nmessages {\n  default \"zh-CN\";\n  locale \"zh-CN\" {\n    \"qiy.resources.reviews.label\" \"审核单\";\n    \"review.note\" \"请说明审核决定\";\n  }\n  locale \"en-US\" {\n    \"qiy.resources.reviews.label\" \"Reviews\";\n    \"review.note\" \"Explain the decision\";\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Item | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| `default` | Required, first in the block, canonical BCP 47 tag; a matching `locale` block must exist (`Missing default message locale X`) |\n| `locale` | At least the default; unique tags (`Duplicate message locale`); canonical form only (`Invalid message locale X: use a canonical BCP 47 language tag`) |\n| key | `^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z_0-9.-]*$`; no spaces/`:`/`/`; no `__proto__`/`prototype`/`constructor` segment (`Invalid message key`) |\n| value | Any string; supports i18next `{{name}}` interpolation and CLDR plural suffixes |\n| duplicates | Duplicate key within a locale fails (`Duplicate message key <locale>.<key>`) |\n\nCanonical tags include `zh-CN`, `en-US`, `ja-JP`, `fr-FR`, `ar-EG`, `zh-Hans`, `es-419`; `fr_fr`, `FR-fr`, `en-us` are rejected. Keys use `.` as a literal character (`keySeparator: false`), not a nesting separator.\n\nWithout `messages`, the default is `zh-CN`, project messages are empty, and the UI still works using built-in chrome plus DSL text fallback. `include \"modules/messages.qiy\" @messages;` imports only one top-level `messages` block.\n\n`t(\"key\")` is only valid in documentation positions: `@comment`, `@label`, `@confirm`, `@error`. The key **must exist in the default locale** (`Missing default locale message for <purpose>: <key>`), because it is resolved at parse time for generated source/docs while the key is retained for runtime translation.\n\n## Derived keys and fallback chain\n\nKeys are derived from identifiers, never from label text. Renaming an identifier invalidates translations; editing label text does not.\n\n| Key | Covers | Fallback |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `qiy.resources.<resource>.label` | Resource base name, related-record cards | entity `@label` -> entity name |\n| `qiy.resources.<resource>.singular` | Create/edit/detail/drawer singular titles | `@singular` -> `.label` dictionary -> `@label` -> entity name |\n| `qiy.resources.<resource>.plural` | Menu nodes, list titles, `viewResource` | `@plural` -> `.label` dictionary -> `@label` -> entity name |\n| `qiy.resources.<resource>.fields.<field>.label` | Column headers, detail labels, form labels, filter placeholders | field `@label` -> field name |\n| `qiy.enums.<enum>.label` | Enum description | enum name |\n| `qiy.enums.<enum>.values.<value>` | Enum Tag, select options, distribution legend | enum value label -> value name |\n| `qiy.menu.<group>.label` | Sidebar group | group `@label` -> group name |\n| `qiy.dashboard.<metric>.label` | Legacy metric card title | `@label` -> metric name |\n| `qiy.charts.<chart>.label` | Chart card title | chart `title` -> chart name |\n| `qiy.charts.<chart>.views.<kind>.label` | View-internal title | view `title` -> chart `title` -> chart name |\n| `qiy.charts.<chart>.labels.<value>` | Distribution labels (shared by views) | explicit mapping/enum label -> raw value |\n| `qiy.charts.<panel>.label` | Panel title/selector | panel `title` -> panel name |\n| `qiy.actions.<action>.label` / `.confirm` / `.inputs.<input>.label` | Command button, confirmation, form field | action text -> dataflow `@label`/`@confirm` -> input name |\n| `qiy.dataflows.<dataflow>.label` | Dataflow name on the overview page | `@label` -> flow name |\n\n`<resource>` is the **table** name (`entity Product table products` -> `qiy.resources.products.*`), which is also what menus, charts, commands and endpoints use. Permission `@label` does **not** derive a key: it is literal unless written as `@label(t(\"key\"))`.\n\nTranslate fallback chain at runtime (later wins): Refine/AntD messages for the locale -> built-in chrome (`qiy.*`, zh-CN for `zh-CN`, English for everything else) -> default-locale project messages -> current-locale project messages -> the caller's fallback (the DSL literal). Any missing layer falls back instead of failing.\n\nConsequence: adding a third language such as `ja-JP` and translating only business keys leaves English chrome. Override the `qiy.*` keys you care about in that locale.\n\nBuilt-in chrome groups you can override: list/form (`qiy.new`, `qiy.edit`, `qiy.delete`, `qiy.batchDelete`, `qiy.search`, `qiy.filters`, `qiy.visibleColumns`, `qiy.noData`, `qiy.autoGenerated`, ...), import/export and saved views, pagination, filters operators (`qiy.filters.mode.*`), theme/color mode, login/OAuth/OTP/profile, 403/audit/tree, chart view (`qiy.chartView`, `qiy.chartViewKind.*`), system pages (`qiy.docs.*`, `qiy.apiDocs.*`, `qiy.apiKey.*`). `qiy.requiredWithLabel` is an exception: it uses Ant Design's `${label}` placeholder, not `{{label}}`.\n\nInterpolation uses `{{name}}` with `escapeValue: false` - inserted values are plain text, never HTML. Plurals use CLDR suffixes (`_one`, `_other`, `_few`, `_many`) with `count`. Locale selection persists in `qiy.locale`; supported locales always include `zh-CN` and `en-US` plus every declared locale. Switching updates the Refine i18n provider, Ant Design locale, and `<html lang/dir>`; `ar`/`fa`/`he`/`ur` prefixes set RTL.\n\nAnt Design component locales are imported only for exact tags: `ja-JP`, `ko-KR`, `fr-FR`, `de-DE`, `es-ES`, `pt-BR`, `ru-RU`, `ar-EG`, `hi-IN`, `it-IT`, `zh-TW`. Use these full tags for localized pagination/date pickers.\n\nAdding a language: add the `locale` block, use a canonical tag, cover the `qiy.*` chrome keys you need, point `default` at the new block if it becomes default (and move every `t(\"key\")` into it), choose an exact AntD tag for component localization, regenerate, then run the generated `apps/web` tests.\n\n## Generated system pages\n\nWhen `features` enables them, three authenticated pages appear under a `System` menu group: `/system/overview` (entities, relations, dataflows, permission model, OpenAPI browser), `/system/api-docs`, and `/system/api-keys`. Their copy lives in `qiy.docs.*`, `qiy.apiDocs.*`, `qiy.apiKey.*` and can be overridden. Page entries are visible to any signed-in user; content is filtered by the current principal's permissions. Details and gating: [system-features.md](system-features.md).\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Error / symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Unsupported UI library mui; only antd is implemented` | Non-AntD library | Use `antd` |\n| `Unsupported UI theme teal` | Theme key outside the five | Use a built-in key |\n| `UI default theme purple must be included in themes` | `theme` not in `themes` | Add it |\n| Theme selector missing | `allowThemeSwitch false` or one theme | Enable it / add candidates |\n| Theme resets after changing defaults | localStorage holds the old choice | Clear `qiy.ui.theme` / `qiy.ui.color-mode` |\n| `Menu group X: unknown resource Y` | Entity not declared, or entity name used instead of table name | Use the `table` name |\n| Menu group missing | All its resources are permission-filtered | Check `restrict`/`pages` |\n| `distribution requires an enum groupBy field` | `@groupBy` not enum | Use an enum field |\n| `trend requires a DateTime groupBy field` | Used `Date` | Use `DateTime` |\n| `Chart X pie view: pie/bar views require \"count <entity> group by <enum field>\" data` | Wrong data expression | Use `count ... group by` |\n| `Chart panel P: placement larger exceeds 24 grid columns` | `x + w > cols` | Shrink `x`/`w` or enlarge grid |\n| Chart cards overlap | No overlap detection | Make `x` ranges disjoint |\n| `Invalid message locale fr_fr` | Non-canonical tag | `fr-FR` |\n| `Missing default message locale ja-JP` | `default` without a matching block | Add the block |\n| `Missing default locale message for field comment: key` | `t(\"key\")` absent from the default locale, or `messages` declared too late | Add the key; keep `messages` before enums/entities |\n| Untranslated English buttons in a third language | Built-in chrome is English for non-`zh-CN` | Override the `qiy.*` keys |\n| `Invalid message key x:y` | `:` in key | Use `.` and the allowed character set |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - `ui`, `menu`, `dashboard`, `chart`, `messages` placement\n- [Modeling and generation](modeling-and-generation.md) - enums and fields backing charts\n- [System features](system-features.md) - `/system/*` pages and gating\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - menu/page filtering by role\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - error table\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [chart](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/charts)\n- [enum / menu / dashboard](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/enum-menu-dashboard)\n- [i18n / messages](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/i18n)\n- [UI and theming guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/ui-theming)\n- [menu and dashboard guide](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/menu-dashboard)\n",
  "references/workspace-integration.md": "# Workspace integration (existing Bun projects and host APIs)\n\nUse this file when Qiy output must live inside an existing Bun repository, when aliases/scripts/paths collide with host files, or when the host already owns the API and only the Refine admin should be generated (`mode integration`).\n\nCanonical reference: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/existing-bun-project (`/dsl/application` for `mode`/`integration`)\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Decide: create, init or integration](#decide-create-init-or-integration)\n- [init prerequisites](#init-prerequisites)\n- [workspace block and aliases](#workspace-block-and-aliases)\n- [Mounted layout](#mounted-layout)\n- [Scripts and dependencies](#scripts-and-dependencies)\n- [Sync and ownership boundary](#sync-and-ownership-boundary)\n- [Integration mode contract](#integration-mode-contract)\n- [Host auth bridge and error contract](#host-auth-bridge-and-error-contract)\n- [CSRF, envelopes and tenant forwarding](#csrf-envelopes-and-tenant-forwarding)\n- [Path collisions](#path-collisions)\n- [Extension points](#extension-points)\n- [Limits](#limits)\n- [Pitfalls](#pitfalls)\n\n## Decide: create, init or integration\n\n| Situation | Command | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| New project, no existing repository | `qiy create -f model.qiy -n name -o dir` | Standalone Turborepo + Bun workspace, server + web + deploy |\n| Existing Bun repo, Qiy should own API + DB + admin | `qiy init -f model.qiy` | `apps/<server-alias>` + `apps/<web-alias>` + aliased deploy files |\n| Existing Bun repo with its own API/users/database | `qiy init` with `mode integration` | Only a Refine web package + host adapters; no Qiy server |\n\nDo not use `create` to \"add\" Qiy to an existing repository: it would write a second root workspace. Do not use `init` on a standalone project Qiy already generated - use `generate ... --sync` there.\n\n## init prerequisites\n\n- Run from the host project root (or pass `-o <project-root>`).\n- Root `package.json` must declare Bun, e.g. `\"packageManager\": \"bun@1.3.13\"`. `qiy init` refuses to write otherwise.\n- Existing workspace patterns are preserved; `apps/*` is added only when missing.\n- Root scripts are not replaced. Qiy adds direct `bun --cwd` scripts under `qiy:<name>:*`; a conflicting existing script with a different command makes the command fail.\n- Qiy never writes the host root `.env*` files.\n\n```bash\ncd /path/to/existing-bun-project\nqiy init -f ./models/admin.qiy\nbun install\nbun run qiy:admin:typecheck\nbun run qiy:admin:test\n```\n\n## workspace block and aliases\n\n```qiy\nworkspace {\n  name admin;\n  aliases {\n    server ops-api;\n    web ops-console;\n    deploy ops-admin;\n  }\n  packages {\n    server \"@example/ops-api\";\n    web \"@example/ops-console\";\n  }\n}\n```\n\n| Key | Allowed | Default |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `name` | Identifier | Application name |\n| `aliases.server` / `.web` / `.deploy` | Lowercase letters, digits, hyphens | `<name>-server`, `<name>-web`, `<name>` |\n| `packages.server` / `.web` | Valid npm package name (scope allowed) | Derived from the workspace name |\n\nOnly `name`, `aliases` (`server`/`web`/`deploy`) and `packages` (`server`/`web`) are allowed; duplicates and invalid identifiers fail. `aliases` affects `init` only; `create`/`generate` always use `apps/server` and `apps/web`. `-n` overrides the name once at the command line; prefer setting `workspace.name` in the model.\n\n## Mounted layout\n\n```text\nhost-project/\n├── apps/\n│   ├── ops-api/                 # Bun + Elysia API (Qiy)\n│   └── ops-console/             # Refine SPA (Qiy)\n├── deploy/ops-admin/            # nginx, Kubernetes, Vercel examples\n├── ops-admin.Dockerfile\n├── docker-compose.ops-admin.yml\n├── .qiy-admin.generated.json    # manifest of Qiy-owned files\n├── openwiki/qiy-admin/          # namespaced generated wiki\n└── package.json                 # keeps host workspaces/scripts; adds apps/* and qiy:admin:*\n```\n\n- Agent entrypoints go into `apps/<web-alias>/` (`AGENTS.md`, `AGENT.MD`) so host root instructions are untouched.\n- Generated OpenWiki docs go to `openwiki/qiy-<name>/`; host `openwiki/` files are preserved.\n- Env files: `apps/<server-alias>/.env.{development,production,example}`, `apps/<web-alias>/.env.*`.\n- Docker/Compose are named from the deploy alias and build from the host root without requiring Turborepo.\n\n## Scripts and dependencies\n\n- Qiy adds `qiy:<name>:<script>` entries (for example `qiy:admin:typecheck`, `qiy:admin:test`, `qiy:admin:preview`) that call `bun --cwd apps/<alias> ...`.\n- It does not add `turbo.json`, a `turbo` dependency, or replace root scripts.\n- Deployment uses `docker-compose.<deploy-alias>.yml`; production migrations use `bun run --cwd apps/<server-alias> db:migrate:production`.\n\n## Sync and ownership boundary\n\n`--sync` (re-run the same `init` command) updates only files listed in `.qiy-<name>.generated.json`, deletes registered files the model no longer generates, and never overwrites unowned host files. A path collision fails instead of merging. Put custom code in unowned files:\n\n```text\napps/ops-api/src/host-extension.ts\napps/ops-api/src/integrations/example-auth.ts\napps/ops-api/src/modules/connectors/\napps/ops-console/app/plugins/host-data-provider.ts\napps/ops-console/app/hooks/use-connector-status.ts\napps/ops-console/app/extensions/\n```\n\nFor `mode integration`, a generated `app/host/data-provider.ts`, `auth.ts` and `access-control.ts` are unowned adapters that `--sync` will not overwrite. When upgrading, review them manually and port any new host-contract behavior; Qiy will not patch unowned files.\n\n## Integration mode contract\n\n```qiy\nqiy v0;\napplication catalog-admin {\n  database sqlite {}\n  mode integration;\n  integration {\n    apiBase \"/api/v2\";\n    auth cookie { csrfCookie \"XSRF-TOKEN\"; csrfHeader \"X-XSRF-TOKEN\"; };\n    response { data \"items\"; total \"meta.count\"; error \"message\"; };\n    pagination offset;\n    tenant { header \"X-Tenant-Id\"; identity \"tenantId\"; };\n  }\n  workspace {\n    name catalog;\n    aliases { web host-admin; }\n    packages { web \"@example/host-admin\"; }\n  }\n  entity products { field id UUID @id; field title Text; }\n}\n```\n\n```text\nintegration {\n  apiBase \"<absolute http(s) URL or /path>\" ;\n  auth none | bearer | cookie | portal ;\n  auth cookie { csrfCookie \"<name>\" ; csrfHeader \"<header>\" ; } ;\n  response { data \"<path>\" ; total \"<path>\" ; error \"<path>\" ; } ;\n  pagination page | offset | none ;\n  tenant { header \"<header>\" ; identity \"<identity-key>\" ; } ;\n}\n```\n\n| Setting | Values | Default | Behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `apiBase` | `https://...`, `http://...`, or a path starting with `/` | required | Host API prefix; `VITE_QIY_API_BASE` affects both DataProvider and auth requests |\n| `auth none` | - | yes | No credentials attached |\n| `auth bearer` | - | - | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from the host bridge |\n| `auth cookie` | optional `csrfCookie`/`csrfHeader` | - | Same-origin cookies; CSRF options are only valid here |\n| `auth portal` | - | - | Host portal/BFF injects identity |\n| `response.data/total/error` | dotted JSON keys (`items`, `meta.count`) | `data`, no total, `error` | Read-envelope paths; `$.items` is rejected (`dotted JSON path`) |\n| `pagination` | `page`, `offset`, `none` | `page` | `page`+`pageSize`, `offset`+`limit`, or no parameters |\n| `tenant.header` | simple HTTP header name | none | Header that carries the host tenant |\n| `tenant.identity` | simple identity key | none | Key read from `window.qiyHostAuth.getIdentity()` |\n\nGenerated baseline: `apps/<web-alias>/app/host/data-provider.ts` implements `getList`/`getOne`/`create`/`update`/`deleteOne` using `apiBase`, the entity table name, the response envelope, pagination and the tenant header. Sorting, filtering, nested resources and bulk endpoints stay in the unowned adapter.\n\nValidation and ordering: `mode integration` requires an `integration` block (`application mode integration requires an integration block`), and an `integration` block requires `mode integration`. Each key appears once; `response` needs at least one path; paths are dotted keys only. Integration mode **rejects** `api { cors }`, `auth`, `scope`, `restrict`, `workflow`, `dataflow`, `permission`, `storage`, `elysia`, `env` and `realtime` with `application mode integration cannot configure generated server features; use integration auth and host adapters instead.` (`api { client ... }` itself is allowed). It also cannot be generated standalone: `application mode integration must be mounted with qiy init inside an existing Bun workspace`.\n\nIntegration output: only the web package plus `apps/<web-alias>/QIY_INTEGRATION.md`, host adapters, and default list/show pages. No server, Drizzle schema, migrations, Docker/Compose or deploy files.\n\n## Host auth bridge and error contract\n\nThe generated app expects a host bridge object. Implement it in unowned files:\n\n```ts\n// apps/host-admin/app/host/auth.ts\nwindow.qiyHostAuth = {\n  ...window.qiyHostAuth,\n  getAccessToken: async () => sessionToken,\n  getIdentity: async () => ({ id: userId, tenantId: currentTenant }),\n};\n```\n\n```ts\n// apps/host-admin/app/host/access-control.ts\nimport type { QiyHostAuthBridge } from \"./auth\";\n\nwindow.qiyHostAuth = {\n  ...window.qiyHostAuth,\n  can: async ({ resource, action }) => ({ can: resource === \"products\" && [\"list\", \"show\"].includes(action) }),\n} satisfies QiyHostAuthBridge;\n```\n\n- `getAccessToken` supplies bearer/portal tokens; `getIdentity` supplies the object the `tenant.identity` key is read from.\n- `can` is the single visibility source for navigation actions and pages in integration mode (`action allow` cannot replace host policy). A missing, throwing or non-`{ can: true }` response denies access.\n- `hostRequest` errors keep `statusCode`; the Refine AuthProvider passes them to the optional `window.qiyHostAuth.onError(error)`. Without the hook, 401 redirects to `/auth/login`, 403/server errors do not. Qiy never refreshes tokens or replays requests (especially not commands with side effects); the caller retries explicitly.\n- Requests are confined to the `apiBase` origin/path and automatic redirects are rejected, so tokens/CSRF values are not sent elsewhere. Hosts must still enforce server-side permissions and session refresh.\n\n## CSRF, envelopes and tenant forwarding\n\n- `auth cookie` requires the admin and API to be same-origin. Non-GET/HEAD/OPTIONS requests must include a readable CSRF cookie configured by `csrfCookie`; the session cookie itself should stay HttpOnly host-side.\n- `response` describes the **read** envelope only; write requests assume the host returns the record itself. If `total` is omitted, the current page length is used as the total. If a declared path is missing, list unwrapping falls back to the whole body as an array (record: as an object).\n- `tenant` forwards a host identity value as a required header. If the identity value is missing, empty or not a string, the request is **not sent** (fail-closed: `Host tenant identity is missing`). Hosts must still validate tenant ownership server-side.\n- CORS only solves browser origin checks; it does not adapt API contracts.\n\n## Path collisions\n\nCollisions fail the command instead of overwriting host content. Resolve them in the model, not by deleting host files:\n\n1. Change `workspace.aliases.server/web/deploy` to unused lowercase names.\n2. Change `workspace.packages.*` if the host already uses those package names.\n3. If an existing root script uses a `qiy:<name>:*` name with a different command, rename the Qiy workspace (`workspace.name`) or the host script.\n4. Re-run `qiy init`; then `bun install` so the new workspace packages are linked.\n\nDo not delete host files just to let generation pass, and do not point Qiy at a directory that already contains a different project.\n\n## Extension points\n\n| Need | Put it in |\n| --- | --- |\n| Host-specific URL mapping, sorting, filters, nested/bulk endpoints | `apps/<web>/app/host/data-provider.ts` (integration) |\n| Host identity, refresh, logout | `apps/<web>/app/host/auth.ts` (integration) |\n| Host authorization bridge | `apps/<web>/app/host/access-control.ts` (integration) |\n| Custom command/page | `apps/<web>/app/extensions/` via `action ... page manual` |\n| Server plugin/domain logic | `apps/<server>/src/integrations/`, `src/modules/`, `src/extensions/`, `src/host-extension.ts` |\n| Refine providers/hooks | `apps/<web>/app/plugins/`, `app/hooks/`, `app/providers/` (unowned files only) |\n\nAlways verify which files are in `.qiy-<name>.generated.json` before editing; those are rewritten by `--sync`.\n\n## Limits\n\n- Integration mode generates no Qiy server, so there is no Qiy auth, permission, scope, restrict, dataflow, storage or realtime enforcement. The host API is authoritative.\n- The generated host DataProvider is a baseline; sorting/filtering/nested/bulk calls need adapter work.\n- `can` is client-side visibility only; it does not secure host data.\n- Qiy does not implement host token refresh, CSRF validation, tenant authorization or audit; implement and test them in the host.\n- Mounting multiple Qiy admins into one Bun workspace is possible via distinct aliases, but each has its own manifest and env files; script names must not collide.\n\n## Pitfalls\n\n| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `qiy init requires packageManager to declare Bun` | No Bun declaration | Add `\"packageManager\": \"bun@<version>\"` and `bun install` |\n| `Refusing to overwrite existing host file` | Alias/script collision | Change `workspace.aliases`/`name`; never delete host files |\n| `application mode integration requires an integration block` | `mode integration` without settings | Add `integration { apiBase ... }` |\n| `integration block requires application mode integration` | Block without the mode | Add `mode integration;` |\n| `integration apiBase must be an absolute http(s) URL or a path starting with /` | Relative path | Use `/api/v2` or a full URL |\n| `Integration auth options are only supported for cookie transport` | `csrfCookie` under bearer/portal | Move them into `auth cookie { ... }` |\n| `integration tenant requires header and identity` | Only one tenant key | Provide both |\n| `application mode integration cannot configure generated server features` | `auth`/`storage`/`env`/`dataflow` in an integration model | Remove them; implement in the host |\n| `application mode integration must be mounted with qiy init ...` | `create`/`generate` with integration mode | Run `qiy init` in the host project |\n| Requests fail before being sent | Tenant identity missing/empty/non-string | Fix `getIdentity()` |\n| Host calls 401 loop | `onError` not implemented or token refresh expected from Qiy | Implement the hook and retry from the caller |\n| Custom host adapter overwritten | File was in the manifest | Move it to an unowned path |\n| `qiy:admin:*` script missing after install | Workspace not installed | `bun install` at the host root |\n\n## Related references\n\n- [CLI workflows](cli-workflows.md) - `init` flags, doctor, skill install, sync\n- [Language reference](language-reference.md) - `mode`/`integration`/`workspace` settings\n- [Auth and permissions](auth-permissions.md) - what Qiy enforces in standalone mode\n- [Testing and deployment](testing-deployment.md) - aliased Docker/Compose and migrations\n- [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md) - cross-area errors\n\n## Canonical docs\n\n- [existing Bun project](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/existing-bun-project)\n- [application: mode and integration](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/application)\n- [CLI](https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/cli)\n",
  "SKILL.md": "---\nname: qiy\ndescription: \"Build and maintain applications with the Qiy CLI and .qiy models: scaffold a Bun + Elysia + Drizzle + Refine admin, add entities/fields/relations, permissions, dataflows, charts, modules, integrations and deployment checks. Use when the user mentions qiy, .qiy, Qiy DSL, qiy create/init/generate/skill/sync, or wants a Refine admin/CRUD app with API, database, auth, RBAC generated from one model.\"\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  short-description: \"Build apps from .qiy models with the Qiy CLI\"\n  version: \"0.2.1\"\n  homepage: \"https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/\"\n  skill-docs: \"https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/agent-skill\"\n  llms-txt: \"https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/llms.txt\"\n---\n\n# Qiy\n\nQiy compiles a declarative `.qiy` model into editable TypeScript: a Refine + React Router admin, a Bun + Elysia REST/GraphQL API, a Drizzle database layer, tests, OpenWiki docs and deployment examples.\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- The user wants to create, extend, review or maintain a Qiy application.\n- The task involves `.qiy` blocks: entities, fields, relations, indexes, enums, generated codes, permissions, dataflows, actions, charts, menus, messages, auth, storage, realtime, scope/restrict, pages, features, modules.\n- The user mentions `qiy create`, `qiy init`, `qiy generate --sync`, `qiy skill install`, or an existing generated workspace.\n- The user wants an admin/CRUD app generated from a model instead of hand-written boilerplate.\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task involves a different framework and no `.qiy` model or Qiy CLI.\n- The user wants to modify the Qiy compiler/generator itself (maintainer work, not application work).\n\n## Choose a workflow\n\n| Situation | Command |\n| --- | --- |\n| New standalone project | `qiy create -f <model.qiy> -n <name> -o <empty-dir>` |\n| Existing Bun repo, Qiy should own API + DB + admin | `qiy init -f <model.qiy>` from the repo root |\n| Existing Bun repo with its own API/users | `qiy init` with `mode integration` in the model |\n| Previously Qiy-generated standalone workspace | `qiy generate <model.qiy> <dir> --sync` |\n\n`--sync` only works on a workspace Qiy generated (it follows `.qiy-generated.json`). Never use `--sync` on an arbitrary repository. There is no `qiy dev`/`qiy build`/`qiy deploy`; use Bun scripts inside the generated workspace.\n\n## Install this skill\n\nThe CLI bundles this skill offline:\n\n```bash\nqiy skill install                  # <project>/.agents/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --global         # ~/.agents/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --dir .claude/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --dir ~/.codex/skills/qiy\nqiy skill install --force          # after a CLI upgrade, replace modified official files\n```\n\nRepeats are idempotent; local edits to official files are refused unless `--force`; unrelated files are preserved; a legacy `.agent/skills/qiy` is updated in place. Static copies: `https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/skills/qiy/SKILL.md` and `.../skills/qiy-skill.tar.gz`. Installing this skill does not install the CLI.\n\n## First run\n\n1. `qiy --version` and `qiy doctor`; if missing, install the release binary for the OS/CPU from GitHub Releases.\n2. Generate (see the workflow table), then `bun install` in the generated workspace.\n3. `bun run typecheck`, `bun run test`, `bun run build`; `bun run preview` is a loopback-only demo with in-memory data, never a deployment target.\n4. For a real database, fill `apps/<server-alias>/.env.development`, then `bun run db:generate` and `bun run db:migrate`. Production needs `apps/<server-alias>/.env.production`.\n\nA server without `auth` refuses to start unless `QIY_DEV_MODE=1`.\n\n## Progressive disclosure\n\nOpen only the reference that matches the task. Every reference is self-contained, offline, and ends with canonical doc URLs.\n\n| Task | Read |\n| --- | --- |\n| Any DSL syntax: lexical rules, declaration order, every block/setting, annotations, field types | [language-reference.md](references/language-reference.md) |\n| Model data: includes/modules, fields, relations, indexes, `@code`/`@generated`, display templates, limits | [modeling-and-generation.md](references/modeling-and-generation.md) |\n| Login, OIDC/OTP/hybrid providers, roles, permissions, verification, restrict/scope/pages, 401/403 | [auth-permissions.md](references/auth-permissions.md) |\n| Generated Refine providers: DataProvider mapping, AuthProvider, `can()`, live/audit/notification/i18n/router wiring | [refine-providers.md](references/refine-providers.md) |\n| Business commands, dataflows, actions, batch, `workflow orderInventory`, `app.test.qiy` | [dataflows-actions.md](references/dataflows-actions.md) |\n| Theme/layout, menu, dashboard, charts and panels, messages/i18n keys | [ui-charts-i18n.md](references/ui-charts-i18n.md) |\n| `features`, system pages, OpenAPI filtering, API keys | [system-features.md](references/system-features.md) |\n| File fields, uploads, S3, attachment cleanup, realtime/outbox | [storage-realtime.md](references/storage-realtime.md) |\n| Typecheck/test/build, generated test suites, migrations, deployment, real-service acceptance | [testing-deployment.md](references/testing-deployment.md) |\n| CLI commands/flags, output layout, env requirements, `--sync`, upgrade | [cli-workflows.md](references/cli-workflows.md) |\n| Mount into an existing Bun project, aliases, integration mode, CSRF/envelope/tenant | [workspace-integration.md](references/workspace-integration.md) |\n| A failure with an exact error string or symptom | [troubleshooting.md](references/troubleshooting.md) |\n| A complete model to copy and generate | [warehouse-admin example](examples/warehouse-admin/README.md) |\n\n## Safety rules\n\n- **No secrets in `.qiy`.** Passwords, JWT/OIDC secrets, database URLs and S3 keys go in `.env` files, secret managers or deployment secrets.\n- **Do not hand-edit owned generated files.** `.qiy-generated.json` lists them; `--sync` rewrites or removes them. Put lasting custom code in `apps/web/app/extensions/`, `apps/server/src/extensions/`, host adapters or plugins.\n- **Hiding a button is not authorization.** `when`, `pages` and `CanAccess` are UI. Server `allow`/`require`/`restrict`/`scope` enforce.\n- **`admin` does not bypass explicit allowlists.** `allow roles operator;` also rejects admin.\n- **Permissions are additive.** There is no subtraction; change the role, database column or IdP claim to demote.\n- **No rate limiting is generated.** Add it at the gateway/WAF or delivery adapter. OTP challenges are reusable within their window.\n- **`mask` protects generated read paths, not the database.** Backups, DB access, logs and external systems still see plaintext.\n- **Realtime is at-least-once.** Consumers must be idempotent. List pages are not auto-subscribed by default.\n- **`mode integration` has no Qiy security.** The host API owns auth, permissions, CSRF and tenancy.\n- **Do not promise unsupported behavior**: no arbitrary expressions, no custom roles in `allow roles`, no generated business workflow beyond `orderInventory`/dataflows, no integration-mode server generation.\n- **Verify before saying done.** Regenerate, review migrations, then run typecheck, tests and build; a passing build does not prove database, IdP, S3 or deployment health.\n- **Regenerate after CLI upgrades.** The DSL is not forward compatible; run `qiy generate ... --sync` or `qiy init --sync`, review migrations, then `qiy skill install --force`.\n\n## Canonical web links\n\n- Home: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/\n- Agent Skill docs: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/agent-skill\n- DSL overview: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/dsl/overview\n- Goal-oriented recipes: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/dsl-cookbook\n- Machine-readable index: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/llms.txt\n- Full text: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/llms-full.txt\n- CLI and release: https://ai-nodev.github.io/qiy/guide/cli\n- Releases: https://github.com/AI-NoDev/qiy/releases\n"
};
